26178eee9068,30911-01,30911-01,Intergulf Development Group,495 Hartford Ave Los Angeles,client,draft,1/2,,2019-03-19,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30911-01 (495 Hartford Ave, Los Angeles)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Consultant Agreement- TEMPLATE - bb.docx",,1.02,"1.02	Commencement of Performance – The Consultant will commence the performance of its obligations in accordance with Schedule 1 - Services, Rates and Schedule ",indemnity|insurance|payment|standard_of_care|permits_approvals|dispute|warranty_reperform|assignment_subconsultants,1023,"1.02 Commencement of Performance – The Consultant will commence the performance of its obligations in accordance with Schedule 1 - Services, Rates and Schedule to this Agreement or as otherwise directed by Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC in writing.


1.03 Consultant’s Standard of Care – In providing the Consultant Services under this Agreement, the Consultant will perform at all times in a manner consistent with the degree of care and skill ordinarily exercised by members of the Consultant’s profession currently practicing under similar circumstances at the same time and in the same or similar locality, and the Consultant will comply with all applicable laws in the provision of the Consultant Services under this Agreement. If any of the Consultant Services, in the opinion of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC are deficient or require correction due to the Consultant not meeting these standards, the Consultant will make the necessary corrections, without additional compensation or time, as specified by Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC in a rectification notice issued pursuant to Section 7.03 of this Agreement. The Consultant Services shall be performed in a matter, sequence and timing so that they will be co-ordinated with those of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC and other consultants.

1.04 Notification by the Consultant to Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC - During the provision of the Consultant Services under this Agreement, the Consultant will notify Intergulf Development (495 Hartford) LLC, promptly of: (a) any contradictions, discrepancies or errors found or noted in this Agreement, including all referenced and incorporated Schedules; (b) supplementary details, instructions or directions that do not correspond with this Agreement; and/or (c) any omissions or other deficiencies that become evident and should be corrected in order to provide the Consultant Services in accordance with this Agreement. If circumstances or conditions that were not reasonably contemplated by Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC and the Consultant are revealed, to the extent that they materially affect the Consultant Services, Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC and the Consultant will enter into good faith negotiations of the relevant portions of this Agreement to address the changed or unanticipated condition(s). Any change under this provision will not be effective until a Change Order reflecting the change has been executed by Intergulf Development (495 Hartford) LLC, and the Consultant. 


1.05 Performance by Specified Individuals Only – The Consultant agrees that where specific individuals are named in Schedule 1 - Services, Rates and Schedule to this Agreement, as being responsible for the provision of the Consultant Services, or any portion thereof (“Named-Individuals”), only those Named-Individuals will provide the Consultant Services. The Consultant will not replace or substitute any of the Named-Individuals without Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC’s prior written consent, not to be unreasonably withheld. Should the Consultant require the substitution or replacement of any Named-Individual(s), it is understood and agreed that any proposed replacement(s) must possess similar or greater qualifications than the individual being replaced, subject to the prior written approval of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford) LLC. The Consultant’s Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC -approved replacement will not be compensated at a rate greater than those established under Schedule 1 - Services, Rates and Schedule to this Agreement.


1.06 Rights and Remedies – The express rights and remedies of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford) LLC, and the Consultant set out in this Agreement are in addition to and will not limit any other rights and remedies available to Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC or the Consultant at law or in equity. Any failure by either Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC or the Consultant to insist on strict performance and compliance by the other of any term, right or remedy under this Agreement will not be construed as a waiver by Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC or the Consultant of its right to require strict performance of any such term, right or remedy, and the duties of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC or the Consultant with respect to such contractual performance will continue in full force and effect.


1.07 Professional Licences and Registrations – The Consultant is responsible for obtaining and maintaining all applicable professional licences, registrations, permits, insurances (including in respect of workers compensation insurance, state disability insurance or equivalent insurance requirements) and approvals required by law to deliver the Consultant Services under this Agreement (the “Professional Requirements”). To the extent required by applicable law or as requested by Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC the Consultant shall deliver to Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC appropriate documentation evidencing obtaining or maintaining Professional Requirements, including (with respect to workers compensation and/or state disability insurance and/or equivalent requirements) clearance letters or certificates of proof of coverage. The Consultant shall immediately inform Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC of any changes of status of Professional Requirements and the Consultant shall indemnify and hold harmless Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC from and against any Claims (as defined below), to the extent arising out of or resulting from the Consultant's failure to obtain or maintain the Professional Requirements, or inform Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC of any changes in relation thereto. 


1.08 Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC Provided Information – Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC will furnish information, requirements, reports, data, surveys and instructions required for the Consultant’s provision of the Consultant Services. Subject to Section 1.04 of this Agreement, the Consultant will use such information, requirements, reports, data, surveys and instructions in performing the Consultant Services and is entitled to rely upon the accuracy and completeness thereof to the same extent Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC is entitled to rely upon such information.

1.09 Sub-consultants to the Consultant –If the Consultant wishes to retain sub-consultants, the Consultant will notify and obtain Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC’s approval in writing prior to engagement of a sub-consultant, such approval to not be unreasonably withheld. Without limiting the generality of the conditions which Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC may require prior to consenting to the Consultant’s use of a specific sub-consultant, every contract entered into by the Consultant with a sub-consultant must adopt all of the terms and conditions of this Agreement for the provision of the Consultant Services provided by the sub-consultant."
26178eee9068,30911-01,30911-01,Intergulf Development Group,495 Hartford Ave Los Angeles,client,draft,1/2,,2019-03-19,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30911-01 (495 Hartford Ave, Los Angeles)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Consultant Agreement- TEMPLATE - bb.docx",,2,"Section 2 – Nature of the Relationship Between Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC and the Consultant",termination|payment|permits_approvals|dispute|assignment_subconsultants,781,"Section 2 – Nature of the Relationship Between Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC and the Consultant

2.01 Consultant Not a Partner, Agent or Employee – The Consultant will have no authority to contractually bind Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC or to assume or create any legal obligation or responsibility, express or implied, on behalf of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC. Nothing in this Agreement will have the effect of creating a partnership, agency or employment relationship between Intergulf Development (495 Hartford),LLC and the Consultant or any of the Consultant’s directors, officers, partners, agents, employees, affiliates, sub-consultants or volunteers.

2.02 Assignment – Other than in compliance with Section 1.09 of this Agreement, the Consultant will not transfer, sublet or assign any rights or duties under, or interest in, this Agreement, including but not limited to, monies that are due or monies that may be due, without the prior written consent of the other party. Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC may immediately terminate this Agreement should the Consultant subcontract for the provision of part or all of the Consultant Services or assigns this Agreement without obtaining Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC’s prior written consent. Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC may assign this Agreement with the prior agreement of the Consultant, not to be unreasonably withheld 

2.03 Duty to Disclose Change of Control – Should the Consultant propose to undergo a change of legal control, the Consultant will immediately disclose, by written notice, any such proposed change to Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC and will comply with any reasonable terms and conditions subsequently required by Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC resulting from the Consultant’s change of control.


2.04 Material Change in Financial Position – Should the Consultant undergo or experience or expect to experience a material change in its financial condition or have difficulty in meeting its day-to-day financial commitments, the Consultant will immediately disclose, by written notice, any such change or deterioration or expected change or deterioration in its financial condition to Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC.


2.05 Conflict of Interest – In the provision of the Consultant Services under this Agreement, the Consultant will: (a) avoid any conflict of interest in the performance of its obligations under this Agreement; (b) disclose immediately any actual or potential conflict of interest arising during the performance of its obligations under this Agreement; and (c) comply with any requirements prescribed by Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC to resolve any actual or potential conflict of interest. In addition to all other rights and remedies available at law or in equity, Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC may immediately terminate this Agreement upon giving notice to the Consultant where: (a) the Consultant fails to comply with any requirements prescribed by Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC to resolve a conflict of interest; or (b) the Consultant’s conflict of interest cannot be resolved. Conflict of interest under this provision includes, but is not limited to, any situation or circumstance where the Consultant’s other commitments, relationships or financial/commercial interests: (a) could or could be seen to exercise an improper influence over the objective, unbiased and impartial exercise of its independent judgement in the provision of the Consultant Services; or (b) could or could be seen to compromise, impair or be incompatible with the effective performance of its contractual obligations under this Agreement. 


2.06 Ethical Standards – Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC and the Consultant represent that neither it nor any of its affiliates has not offered, promised or given financial or other advantage directly or indirectly to a governmental or public official or any employee or other person acting on their behalf, or any employee or other person acting on behalf of the other party herein, in connection with any matter related to the provision of the Consultant Services. In performing its obligations and exercising its rights under this Agreement, Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC and the Consultant will comply with this Agreement and applicable laws, including those pertaining to the regulation of public markets, competition among market participants and the corruption and bribery of governmental or public officials or others; lobbying and money laundering; export controls, customs and anti-boycott laws; health and safety matters including worker compensation requirements; protection of personal and private information; mutual respect in the workplace; and safeguarding children and vulnerable adults, human rights, human trafficking and modern slavery. The parties further agree that they will exercise their respective obligations under this Agreement, deal with their employees, suppliers, business and governmental organizations, in a fair manner and conduct themselves, in all matters related to the provision of the Consultant Services, in a manner consistent with business best practices and the values and principles promoted by their respective organizations."
26178eee9068,30911-01,30911-01,Intergulf Development Group,495 Hartford Ave Los Angeles,client,draft,1/2,,2019-03-19,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30911-01 (495 Hartford Ave, Los Angeles)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Consultant Agreement- TEMPLATE - bb.docx",,3,Section 3 – Payment for Consultant Performance and Audit,payment,276,"Section 3 – Payment for Consultant Performance and Audit

3.01 Consultant Payments According to Agreement Rates – Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC will, subject to the Consultant’s performance of its duties and obligations under this Agreement, pay the Consultant for the provision of the Consultant Services, plus applicable taxes, as set out in Schedule 1 - Services, Rates and Schedule to this Agreement. Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC’s obligations to the Consultant pursuant to this Section 3.01 are expressly subject to Section 3.02 of this Agreement.



3.02 Agreement Billing and Payment – Unless Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC and the Consultant expressly set out a different billing and payment process in Schedule 1 - Services, Rates and Schedule to this Agreement, payment for the Consultant Services will be based on the Consultant’s submission to Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC of: (a) an invoice no later than the last day of the month referencing or including: (i) the Agreement number; (ii) a brief description, inclusive of relevant supporting documentation, of the Consultant Services provided during the month; and (iii) such other information as required under this Agreement. Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC will approve or reject the Consultant’s invoice within fifteen (15) days of receipt. In the event Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC rejects the Consultant’s invoice, or any portion thereof, it will advise the Consultant promptly in writing requesting the provision of the appropriate billing information/documentation to correct the deficiency. Subject to Section 3.01 of this Agreement and Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC’s approval of the Consultant’s invoice, Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC will make payment to the Consultant by last day of the following month."
26178eee9068,30911-01,30911-01,Intergulf Development Group,495 Hartford Ave Los Angeles,client,draft,1/2,,2019-03-19,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30911-01 (495 Hartford Ave, Los Angeles)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Consultant Agreement- TEMPLATE - bb.docx",,3.03,"3.03	Consultant’s Payment of Taxes and Duties – Unless expressly agreed in writing, the Consultant will pay all applicable federal, provincial, state and munici",termination|payment|permits_approvals,180,"3.03 Consultant’s Payment of Taxes and Duties – Unless expressly agreed in writing, the Consultant will pay all applicable federal, provincial, state and municipal taxes, including sales, value added, payroll and excise duties and taxes, incurred with respect to the provision of the Consultant Services under this Agreement.


3.04 Document Retention and Audit – For ten (10) years after the expiry or termination of this Agreement, the Consultant will retain, maintain and safeguard all project files, including but not limited to drawings, specifications, calculations, sketches, graphics, data, notes, photographs, models, daily logs, meeting minutes, invoices, communications, correspondence, records, reports, and necessary financial records and billing documents to substantiate all charges and payments made and received under this Agreement. At any time during the ten (10) years, the Consultant will permit and reasonably assist Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC in conducting audits of the Consultant to verify payments made pursuant to the Consultant’s provision of the Consultant Services under this Agreement. Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC will provide the Consultant with reasonable prior notice of its requirement to conduct such audit."
26178eee9068,30911-01,30911-01,Intergulf Development Group,495 Hartford Ave Los Angeles,client,draft,1/2,,2019-03-19,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30911-01 (495 Hartford Ave, Los Angeles)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Consultant Agreement- TEMPLATE - bb.docx",,4,Section 4 – Confidentiality,confidentiality|assignment_subconsultants,205,"Section 4 – Confidentiality

4.01 Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC Confidential Information – The Consultant agrees to keep confidential and not to use or to disclose to any person or entity, other than its directors, officers, partners, agents, employees, affiliates, sub-consultants and volunteers (collectively, the “Representatives”), any data or information learned or generated by the Consultant in the performance of this Agreement or disclosed to the Consultant by or on behalf of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC in connection with this Agreement, other than is necessary to perform the Consultant Services. The Consultant further agrees to ensure that those of its Representatives who have been provided with Confidential Information will keep all such information confidential and only use or disclose same as necessary to perform the Consultant Services. This provision does not apply to information in whatever form that was in the public domain prior to the execution of this Agreement, nor does it restrict the Consultant from giving notices required by law or when complying with an order to disclose as issued by a court, administrative agency or other regulatory authority, or if disclosure is reasonably necessary for the Consultant to defend itself from any action, claim, demand, lawsuit, or other proceeding at law."
26178eee9068,30911-01,30911-01,Intergulf Development Group,495 Hartford Ave Los Angeles,client,draft,1/2,,2019-03-19,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30911-01 (495 Hartford Ave, Los Angeles)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Consultant Agreement- TEMPLATE - bb.docx",,4.02,"4.02	Access and Use Restrictions – The Consultant agrees that unless it obtains specific written preauthorization from Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC",confidentiality,53,"4.02 Access and Use Restrictions – The Consultant agrees that unless it obtains specific written preauthorization from Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC, any access to or use of Confidential Information that is not necessary for the performance of its obligations in the provision of the Consultant Services under this Agreement is strictly prohibited."
26178eee9068,30911-01,30911-01,Intergulf Development Group,495 Hartford Ave Los Angeles,client,draft,1/2,,2019-03-19,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30911-01 (495 Hartford Ave, Los Angeles)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Consultant Agreement- TEMPLATE - bb.docx",,5,Section 5 – Intellectual Property,intellectual_property,630,"Section 5 – Intellectual Property

5.01 Ownership of Instruments of Service – The Consultant agrees that all reports, drawings, specifications, field data, notes and other documents and instruments prepared by the Consultant and provided to Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC under this Agreement (“Instruments of Service”) are the exclusive and sole property of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC. Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC will retain, at all times, the Instruments of Service common law, statutory and other reserved rights, including, without limitation, the copyrights thereto. 

5.02 Intellectual Property Ownership – The presumption governing this Agreement is that Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC will be the sole owner of any Intellectual Property in any form created for or during the provision of the Consultant Services. Intellectual Property includes any intellectual, industrial or other proprietary right of any type in any form protected or protectable under the laws of the United States including, without limitation, any intellectual, industrial or similar proprietary rights protected or protectable by legislation, common law or at equity.


5.03 Assignment and Waiver – The Consultant hereby assigns, and upon performance of each element of the Consultant Services automatically assigns to Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC all of the Consultant’s and its Representative’s rights, titles and interests, if any, in or to the Instruments of Service and Intellectual Property inherent in the provision of the Consultant Services under this Agreement. This assignment includes any and all rights to secure any patent, trade-mark, copyright, industrial design or other registrations (including any renewals or extensions thereto) with respect of the Instruments of Service and Intellectual Property inherent in the Consultant Services, in the United States, and elsewhere. The Consultant hereby unconditionally and irrevocably waives and shall cause its Representatives to unconditionally and irrevocably waive all moral rights of the Consultant or its Representatives that exist or may exist in any Instruments of Service or Intellectual Property inherent in the Consultant Services under this Agreement.


5.04 Consultant’s Grant of Licence – The Consultant agrees that it will not incorporate into the Consultant Services any Intellectual Property that would restrict the right of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC to use the Consultant Services in any way Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC deems necessary, or that would prevent Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC from entering into any contract with any contractor for the further or other use of the Consultant Services. If Intellectual Property of the Consultant or any third party forms any part of the Consultant Services, the Consultant will notify Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC prior to the delivery of the Consultant Services containing such Intellectual Property. For those parts of the Consultant Services containing Intellectual Property of the Consultant or its Representatives, the Consultant, pursuant to this provision, grants Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC a perpetual, royalty-free, irrevocable, non-exclusive licence to exercise all such Intellectual Property rights and every other right, title and interest in the Consultant Services without obligation to account to, or obtain consent from, the Consultant or its Representatives. 


5.05 Title to Improvements and Modifications – All Intellectual Property rights arising from any further development or modification of the Consultant Services that are conceived, developed, effected or first reduced to practice by or on behalf of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC under this Agreement, will vest in Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC, and will not vest in the Consultant or its Representatives except pursuant to subsequent written agreement.


5.06 Confirmation of Intellectual Property Rights – The Consultant shall, upon Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC request, obtain from each and every one of its Representatives any waiver, agreement or assignment required to confirm ownership rights in the Instruments of Service and Intellectual Property inherent in the Consultant Services in favour of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford) LLC under this Agreement."
26178eee9068,30911-01,30911-01,Intergulf Development Group,495 Hartford Ave Los Angeles,client,draft,1/2,,2019-03-19,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30911-01 (495 Hartford Ave, Los Angeles)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Consultant Agreement- TEMPLATE - bb.docx",,6,Section 6 – Indemnity and Insurance,indemnity|consequential_damages|insurance|termination|permits_approvals|assignment_subconsultants,661,"Section 6 – Indemnity and Insurance

6.01 Consultant Indemnity – To the extent permitted by law, the Consultant will indemnify and hold harmless Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC from and against any claims, damages, losses, costs and expenses, including reasonable legal and professional fees (collectively, the “Claims”), to the extent arising out of or resulting from the Consultant's negligent acts, errors and/or omissions in the provision of the Consultant Services under this Agreement. To the fullest extent permitted by law, neither Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC nor the Consultant will be liable to the other for any incidental, consequential, indirect, special or punitive damages arising out of this Agreement, damages related to loss of use, loss of profit, loss of income, unrealized energy savings, diminution of property value or loss of reimbursement or credit from governmental or other regulatory agencies, in each case regardless of a party being advised of the possibility of such damages.


6.02 Consultant’s Insurance – Prior to Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC’s execution of this Agreement, the Consultant agrees to put in effect and maintain insurance until the date that is three (3) years after the expiry or termination of this Agreement, at its own cost and expense, with insurers having a secure A.M. Best rating of A or equivalent, all the necessary and appropriate insurance that a prudent person in the business of the Consultant would maintain including, but not limited to: 

commercial general liability insurance on an occurrence basis for third party bodily injury, personal injury and property damage, to an inclusive limit of not less than $1,000,000 per occurrence and $1,000,000 in the aggregate. The policy must include:

Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC, as an additional insured with respect to liability arising in the course of the performance of the Consultant’s obligations under, or otherwise in connection with, this Agreement;
contractual liability coverage;
a cross-liability clause;
employers’ liability coverage;
a thirty (30) day written notice of cancellation or termination clause; and
non-owned automobile coverage with blanket contractual coverage for hired automobiles.
(b) professional liability insurance for damages incurred by reason of any negligent act, error and/or omission of the Consultant in the amount of $500,000.

(c) automobile liability insurance for personal and bodily injury including death and property damage in the amount of $1,000,000. 


6.03 Proof of Insurance – Upon request, the Consultant will provide Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC with proof of the insurance required pursuant to Section 6.02 of this Agreement, in the form of valid certificates of insurance and confirm the required coverage, and renewal replacements on or before the expiry of any such insurance. Upon the request of Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC, a copy of each insurance policy will be made available to it. The Consultant agrees to maintain on an ongoing basis all insurance required under this Agreement for a period of three (3) years following expiry or termination of this Agreement.

6.04 Continuity of Insurance – The Consultant agrees that it will require each of its sub-consultants to obtain all necessary and appropriate insurance that a prudent person in the business of the sub-consultant would maintain and that, upon request, Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC is named as an additional insured under the commercial general liability and automobile liability insurances coverages required under Section 6.02(a) and (c) to this Agreement with respect to any liability arising in the course of performance of the sub-consultant's obligations under its contract with the Consultant for the provision of the Consultant Services. The Consultant further covenants and agrees to pay when due, and to ensure that each of its sub-consultants pay when due, all amounts required to be paid by it/its sub-consultants pursuant to this Section 6. Failing payment, Intergulf Development (495 Hartford), LLC will have the right to pay any amount due and unpaid by the Consultant or its sub-consultants and to deduct and set off such amount from any amount due and owing under Section 3.03 of this Agreement."
