Dear Mr. DesRoches: 
Pursuant to your request, I have reviewed the proposed Consultant Agreement 
with J16SD, Inc. from a legal perspective pursuant to California law. A copy of this 
Agreement is attached for your reference. 
Provided that the Agreement and its Exhibits otherwise have been reviewed from 
fiscal, administrative, insurance, and engineering perspectives, I have the following 
comments and recommendations in order to make the Agreement clearer and more 
favorable to you: 
(1) 
In the introductory section: 
(a) 
The effective date needs to be corrected. 
(b) 
I suggest adding the following to the end of the introductory section: 
“Company and Consultant are referred to herein as ‘Party’ and 
collectively as ‘Parties.’” Then, these terms should be capitalized 
consistently where appropriate throughout the Agreement. 
(c) 
Regarding sub-section “B,” I point out that the “Company” and the 
“Owner” are the same entity which may create some contractual 
ambiguity, such as in Exhibit A. 
(d) 
The name of the general contractor needs to be inserted into sub-
section “C.”"
