b2bb1aaa72fc,30921-01,30921-01,J16SD LLC,The Fellow J16 Lofts San Diego,client,draft,1/5,,2019-08-30,opportunities,Management\Project Opportunities\Pending\Client Agreements & Contracts for Review\30921-01 Burke Williams & Sorensen LLP 2019-08-26 - Review J16SD Inc. Contract.pdf,,0p8,I. ,termination|schedule_delay,354,"I. 
CONSULTANT'S BASIC SERVICES 
A. 
Consultant shall furnish Services to Company as described in Exhibit A, ""Services"" attached and made a part hereof. 
B. 
Consultant agrees to render the Services in a proper, timely, competent, and efficient manner in accordance with that degree of 
care and skill ordinarily exercised by members of the same profession currently practicing under similar circumstances using only 
qualified personnel. Consultant understands and agrees that time is of the essence with respect to Consultant’s obligation to 
provide the Services in accordance with the agreed upon schedule between Company and Consultant. Subject to Section II.A. 
below, Consultant shall devote as much of Consultant’s productive time, attention, knowledge and skill to the Services provided 
as may be necessary to competently discharge Consultant’s duties hereunder. 
C. 
Consultant understands and agrees that Company has entered into this Agreement in reliance on the skills, experience, and 
qualifications of the following personnel: Jim DesRoches (“Key Personnel”). Consultant agrees that the Key Personnel shall be 
and remain primarily responsible for rendering the Services. If any of the Key Personnel should no longer be employed by the 
Consultant and/or are unable to work on the Project for any other reason, Consultant must notify Company of the same. In 
addition to any other basis for termination, should two or more of the Key Personnel no longer be available to work on the Project, 
the Company will have the right to terminate this Agreement in accordance with Section IX below. Company shall reserve the 
right to compel Consultant to replace Key Personnel if Company is not in any way satisfied with any such person. 
D. 
Consultant shall meet with Company from time to time as requested by Company to discuss the progress of the Services 
rendered to date and to ensure that Company is satisfied with the scope and quality of the Services. Company may have a 
representative present at any meeting of Consultant concerning the Project. 
E. 
Consultant shall not engage the services of any other consultant, person, or entity in connection with the Services to be provided 
to the Company by Consultant without prior written consent of Company."
b2bb1aaa72fc,30921-01,30921-01,J16SD LLC,The Fellow J16 Lofts San Diego,client,draft,1/5,,2019-08-30,opportunities,Management\Project Opportunities\Pending\Client Agreements & Contracts for Review\30921-01 Burke Williams & Sorensen LLP 2019-08-26 - Review J16SD Inc. Contract.pdf,,0p10,II. ,indemnity|insurance|termination|payment|permits_approvals|dispute|assignment_subconsultants|lien|schedule_delay,854,"II. 
COMPENSATION TO THE CONSULTANT 
A. 
Company shall compensate Consultant for the Services in the amount set forth in Exhibit B, not to exceed the sum of $120,000for 
Structural Engineering Services as defined in Exhibit A. Payment beyond the not to exceed amount and/or payment for any 
additional work not required by Exhibit A will not be paid without written consent from the Company prior to the performance of 
the alleged additional services. 
B. 
Company will reimburse Consultant for reasonable expenses, at Consultant’s cost without mark-up, incurred by Consultant in 
providing consulting services to Company, provided all such expenses are made with Company’s prior written consent. 
Consultant will notify Company in advance of the categories and estimated amounts of any expenses which Consultant expects 
to incur in connection with providing services to Company during the course of this engagement. Upon Company’s request, 
Consultant agrees to provide receipts, invoices or other reasonable proof of such expenses. No compensation shall be allowed 
for administrative, overhead, insurance, word processing (normal or overflow secretarial time or overtime, or computer time or 
service), telephone calls, and mail and delivery costs payable to the United States Postal Service. 
C. 
Consultant shall submit one application for payment per month to be accepted for processing in accordance with Schedule of 
Invoice Submittal and Payment Dates (Exhibit C). The Payment Application must be submitted prior to the 10th of each month. If 
a properly completed payment application is submitted by the last day of each month, the Company will make any payment by 
the 10th of the following month. If, however, Company has a disagreement about the amount of the payment application, the 
Company will notify the Consultant, in writing, before the last day of the following month of the reasons for Company's 
disagreement and the amount of the payment that is being withheld. If Company believes that it has suffered any cost, loss, 
damage or liability arising from any negligent act or omission of the Consultant, the Company may withhold from further payment 
150% of the amount of the cost, loss, damage or other liability as estimated, in good faith, by the Company. 
III. 
GENERAL PROVISIONS 
A. 
The term of this Agreement shall begin on March 29, 2019 and terminate upon completion of Consultant’s Services as stated by 
the Company, unless otherwise terminated pursuant to Section IX, but no later than March 29, 2023. 
B. 
This Agreement shall be binding upon the successors or assigns of the Company and Consultant. 
C. 
Neither Consultant nor Company shall be responsible for delays or damages, or declared to be in default by reason of delays in 
performance or by reason of strikes, lockouts, accidents, acts of God, and other delays unavoidable or beyond Company’s or 
Consultant’s reasonable control, delays in approval by governmental agencies, or delays in work of other consultants performing 
services on behalf of Company. 
D. 
In the event Consultant discovers or becomes aware of apparent discrepancies or errors in the Contractor’s or other 
subcontractors’ or consultants’ or Company’s work during the performance of Consultant’s services, Consultant agrees to 
immediately notify Company. 
E. 
Consultant shall not permit or suffer any mechanic’s or materialmen’s lien filed by any subcontractor, subconsultant, employee, 
supplier, or vendor of Consultant to remain upon the property of Company unless said lien is a result of nonpayment by the 
Company. In the event any such lien is filed upon the property of Company, Consultant shall cause such lien to be removed by 
posting the necessary bond. If Consultant fails to do so, Company will have the right to cause such lien to be removed and 
Consultant shall indemnify, defend and hold harmless Company against all liability, cost and expense, including attorneys' fees, 
incurred by Company in causing such lien to be removed. Company may retain out of any payment otherwise due Consultant 
amounts sufficient to reimburse Company for any such liability, cost, fees and expenses. 
F. 
Consultant assumes full and exclusive responsibility and liability for withholding and paying, as may be required by law, any and 
all federal, state and local taxes, and contributions, with respect to or assessed against, or measured by Consultant’s earnings 
under this Agreement, or the salaries or compensation of Consultant’s principals and other personnel, or other contributions for 
which Consultant may be responsible under federal, state and local laws. Consultant shall file any and all returns or other 
documents required in connection with any and all such laws. 
G. 
Any and all Services to be provided under the Agreement by Consultant, its principals, employees and agents shall be performed 
as an independent contractor, and not as an employee or agent of Company. Nothing in this Agreement shall constitute or be 
construed to create a partnership, joint venture, principal-agent or employer-employee relationship between the Company and 
Consultant. In rendering Services under this Agreement, the Consultant will control the operation of its Services and will 
determine the means and methods of Consultant’s performance. Consultant shall have no right or authority, express or implied, 
to commit or otherwise obligate Company in any manner whatsoever unless and until Consultant is expressly authorized to do so 
in writing by Company."
