b07cb962031b,OPP:GKC Architecture Swartz Bay Victoria (DUE JUL 31),,,,client,draft,1/1,yes,2026-07-13,opportunities,Management\Project Opportunities\Submitted to Client\GKC Architecture Swartz Bay Victoria (DUE JUL 31)\On-site_Services_Agreement.pdf,,1.1,"During the Term, Contractor covenants and warrants that it will:",intellectual_property|insurance|standard_of_care|permits_approvals|dispute|warranty_reperform|assignment_subconsultants|lien,1055,"1.1 During the Term, Contractor covenants and warrants that it will: 
(a) 
provide to BCF the services and Work Product described in Schedule A, together with all incidental 
services (the “Services”), at the premises or facility identified therein (the “Site”), for the fees also 
specified therein (the “Fees”); 
(b) 
provide the Services (including all Work Product) at all times: (i) in accordance with the terms, 
conditions and specifications of this Agreement, including the Schedules attached; (ii) in a 
competent, professional, diligent and workmanlike manner, using the highest standard of care in the 
industry to which the Services relate; (iii) in compliance with all applicable laws, regulations and 
requirements of federal, provincial, municipal and other relevant governing authorities; (iv) in 
accordance with all reasonable instructions or directions provided by BCF; and (v) in a manner that 
reflects favourably at all times on the goodwill and reputation of BCF; 
(c) 
supply at its own expense all labour, materials, equipment, machinery, tools, supplies, transportation, 
personnel, knowledge, expertise, resources and approvals necessary to perform the Services, except 
as expressly set forth herein; 
(d) 
maintain all equipment, machinery, tools, supplies and materials used in the performance of the 
Services in good working order, and operate them in a safe and lawful manner; 
(e) 
obtain and maintain all federal, provincial and municipal permits, licenses and approvals required for 
the performance of the Services; 
(f) 
ensure all persons employed or engaged by it to perform the Services have the skills, qualifications 
(including any applicable licences, credentials, certifications, and professional designations) and 
experience necessary to perform the Services in accordance with the requirements of this Agreement, 
and remain fully responsible and liable to BCF for all acts and omissions by any such persons in the 
performance of the Services; 
(g) 
comply with, and ensure that all persons employed by or engaged by it to perform the Services 
comply with, the BCF Contractor’s Safety Guidelines as set out (as of the Effective Date) at: 
https://www.bcferries.com/web_image/h43/hf2/8928443826206.pdf and such other health and safety 
policies, procedures and rules in effect for the Site from time to time; 
(h) 
obtain and maintain the insurance coverages set forth in Schedule B and provide proof of same upon 
request; 
(i) 
comply with, and ensure that all persons employed or engaged by it to perform the Services, comply 
with all security requirements and policies in effect from time to time for the Site and BCF’s 
systems; 
(j) 
take all reasonable precautions for the safety of, and provide all reasonable protection to prevent 
damage, injury or loss to: (i) all personnel engaged in connection with the Services, all other persons 
who may be affected by the performance of the Services, and all persons entitled to be on the Site, 
including by keeping the Site in an orderly state appropriate to the avoidance of danger to such 
persons, and by providing all appropriate personal protective equipment to Contractor’s personnel; 
(ii) the Site; (iii) all equipment, machinery, tools, supplies, materials or other items provided or used 
in connection with the Services, including by adopting any security measures reasonably required for 
the proper safety and protection of the foregoing from robbery and theft; and (iv) all other property at 
the Site or adjacent to the Site, including trees, shrubs, pavements, roadways, structures and utilities; 
(k) 
to the extent applicable to the nature of the Services, erect and maintain, as required by existing 
conditions and progress of the Services, all reasonable safeguards for safety and protection, including 
erecting barriers, lights, ladders, railings and walkways, posting danger signs and other warnings 
against hazards, promulgating safety regulations, and notifying owners and users of adjacent areas of 
any dangerous or hazardous conditions; 

- 3 - 
 
(l) 
in the event of any incident, accident, injury, property damage or near-miss incident, immediately 
report the matter to BCF, fully cooperate with and assist in any investigation of the matter, and 
provide BCF with copies of all notices to or from, inspections by, or written communications with, 
governmental authorities and insurance companies with respect to such matters, and provide such 
written reports relating thereto as may be reasonably requested by BCF (excluding any written 
communications subject to legal privilege); 
(m) 
ensure that its personnel do not bring onto the Site any alcohol, illegal drugs, firearms, or potentially 
hazardous materials; 
(n) 
ensure that its personnel do not assist or permit unauthorized persons to enter the Site; 
(o) 
without limiting any other provision of this Agreement, comply with all statutory occupational health 
and safety requirements under the Workers Compensation Act (BC) in connection with the 
performance of the Services, and Contractor represents and warrants to BCF that Contractor is in 
compliance with all requirements of the Workers Compensation Act, including registration; 
(p) 
without limiting any other provision of this Agreement, comply with, and ensure that its employees, 
officers, agents, Subcontractors and representatives comply with, all applicable laws, statutes, 
regulations and codes relating to anti-slavery and human trafficking laws, including but not limited to 
the Fighting Against Forced Labour and Child Labour in Supply Chains Act (Canada). Contractor 
will take all reasonable steps to monitor and manage its own supply chain’s and its Subcontractors’ 
compliance (including implementing appropriate policies and procedures) with all such anti-slavery 
and human trafficking laws, statutes and regulations from time to time in force, and will demonstrate 
the effective implementation of its policies and procedures relating to anti-slavery and human 
trafficking laws if requested by BCF; 
(q) 
pay and satisfy all claims for wages of its personnel, and all other claims which might constitute a 
lien upon the Site or the property of BCF or any other persons at the Site, immediately upon such 
claims becoming due. If any personnel of Contractor or any other person for whom Contractor is 
responsible files or registers a lien against the Site or the property of BCF or any other persons at the 
Site, Contractor will take such steps and make such payments, including the posting of security or 
payment into court, as are necessary to remove such lien. Without limiting any other provision of this 
Agreement, Contractor will comply with the requirements of the Builders Lien Act (BC), to the 
extent applicable to the performance of the Services; and 
(r) 
perform all obligations within the timeframes specified in this Agreement, any failure to meet such 
timeframes will constitute a material breach of this Agreement."
