Agreement and prior to commencing any Services, the Consultant will obtain and maintain during the 
performance of the Services or as otherwise required by this Agreement, at its own expense and with 
insurance providers acceptable to the Owner, acting reasonably, the following insurance: 
(a) 
Workers’ Compensation coverage for all employees engaged in the Services in accordance with 
the Workers Compensation Act (British Columbia); 
(b) 
automobile liability on all owned and non-owned vehicles used by the Consultant in connection 
with this Agreement in the minimum amount of $5 million per occurrence in respect of bodily 
injury, death and property damage; 
(c) 
subject to Section 6.4, professional liability insurance for the minimum amount of $2 million per 
claim with an aggregate limit of $2 million per 12 month policy period, which coverage will be 
maintained for a period ending no sooner than six (6) years after the Consultant has ceased to 
provide Services to the Owner under the terms of this Agreement; and 
(d) 
commercial general liability insurance for the minimum amount of $5 million per occurrence in 
respect of bodily injury, death and property damage, which coverage will include a cross liability 
and severability of interests clause. The above referenced limit may be satisfied with a 
combination of commercial general liability and umbrella/excess liability policies."
