98630fabc82f,10189-01,10189-01,Wesgroup Properties Ltd.,RD Parcel 35/36 Vancouver Pursuit,client,draft,1/2,,2024-09-03,opportunities,Management\Project Opportunities\Submitted to Client\Wesgroup RD Parcel 35& 36 Vancouver JM KW (DUE SEP 17 10189-01)\1.0 Standard Form Consultant Agreement.pdf,,6.4,"Project Specific Liability Insurance.  Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this Agreement,",insurance|warranty_reperform,223,"6.4 Project Specific Liability Insurance. Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this Agreement, 
the Owner may, at its option and cost, arrange for and maintain a single project professional liability 
insurance policy (the “Project Policy”) in accordance with the following terms and conditions: 
(a) 
The Project Policy will have a limit of no less than $5,000,000, to cover against any and all claims 
made for negligent acts, errors or omissions of, or attributable to, or relating to the Consultant’s 
design and performance of the Services, for which the Consultant and the Consultant’s sub-
consultants (if applicable) are at law responsible, with sub-limits, conditions and deductibles in 
amounts reasonably obtainable at the time of policy placement and as selected by the Owner; 
(b) 
The Project Policy shall be the primary policy for insured consultants in connection with the 
Project; 
(c) 
The Consultant shall comply with the underwriters of the Project Policy to the extent reasonably 
required to procure and maintain coverage under the Project Policy; and 
(d) 
The Consultant shall be required to represent and warrant to the Owner and the Owner’s insurer 
that, to the best of its knowledge, there are no claims pending relating to the Project. 
If the Owner opts not to obtain the Project Policy, the Consultant shall obtain and maintain the 
professional liability insurance coverage contemplated in Section 6.1(c)."
