5f13b2b72453,OPP:Wesgroup River District Parcel 30 JM JS DUE OCT 16),,,,client,draft,1/1,yes,2026-10-05,opportunities,Management\Project Opportunities\Submitted to Client\Wesgroup River District Parcel 30 JM JS DUE OCT 16)\(26) Standard Form Consultant Agreement (Without Alternate Clauses)- April 2026.docx,,0p1,CONSULTANT AGREEMENT,intellectual_property|insurance|termination|payment|standard_of_care|permits_approvals|warranty_reperform|assignment_subconsultants,1953,"CONSULTANT AGREEMENT
THIS CONSULTANT AGREEMENT (this “Agreement”) made the [____] day of [________], [20__]
BETWEEN:
[Insert Full Legal Name of the Beneficial Owner of Property] LIMITED PARTNERSHIP by its general partner [__________________], Suite 2000 – 595 Burrard Street, Vancouver, BC, V6C 0E4 (the “Owner”) 
[NTD: Use Beneficial Owner of Property and general partner of Beneficial Owner; if you are unsure which entity to use, please check with legal]
AND:
[insert full legal name of the Consultant], [insert full mailing address of the Consultant] (the “Consultant”)
WHEREAS:
The Owner wishes to engage the Consultant to provide consulting services in relation to [insert brief description of the project, i.e. a low-rise condominium development known as “…”] (the “Project”); and
The Consultant wishes to enter into a formal contract with the Owner for the performance of the Services. 
NOW THEREFORE in consideration of the mutual covenants and conditions contained in this Agreement, the Owner and the Consultant agree as follows: 
SERVICES and schedule
Scope of Services. The Consultant will provide to the Owner, as and when requested by the Owner in writing, consulting services (the “Services”) relating to the Project, which Services are, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, described in Schedule “A” – Scope of Services. The Consultant will only provide Services which have been specifically authorized in writing by the Owner.
Standard of Care. The Consultant will perform the Services:
with that degree of care, skill and diligence normally provided by a qualified and experienced service provider performing services similar to the Services;
with qualified, experienced, capable and safety trained personnel;
in accordance with this Agreement; and
in accordance with applicable laws and permits.
Schedule. The Consultant will perform the Services in accordance with the schedule attached at Schedule “A” – Scope of Services, and if no schedule is attached, then in accordance with the schedule provided by the Owner, each as may be adjusted in accordance with this Agreement.
Working Drawing Checklist. The Consultant hereby confirms that it has received a copy of the Wesgroup Working Drawing Checklist (the “Checklist”) and covenants and agrees that it shall complete and submit the Checklist to the Owner as each stage of the Services is completed and submitted. The Consultant further confirms that it shall ensure that the Work Product submitted at each stage of the Project includes the level of detail and the Work Products described in the relevant portion of the Checklist.
Project Management Platform and Required Software. The Consultant shall use Autodesk Construction Cloud as the primary project management platform for the duration of the Project. If applicable, the Consultant shall use such additional software for the Project as is described in detail in Schedule “A” – Scope of Services.
COMPENSATION AND PAYMENT
Contract Price. As full and complete payment for the total performance of the Services, the Owner will pay the Consultant the stipulated lump sum amount as set out in Schedule “B” – Compensation (the “Contract Price”). The Contract Price will be the maximum and entire amount of compensation owing to the Consultant for the performance of the Services. The Consultant hereby acknowledges and agrees that it will be responsible for payment of provincial sales taxes or similar taxes (“PST”), if any, that are owed in respect of the Services. The Contract Price shall be exclusive of PST and, to the extent that the Consultant is obliged to remit to PST in respect of the Services to any governmental authority, the Consultant shall be solely responsible to pay or remit such PST at its own cost without any contribution from the Owner. The Owner will pay any GST payable on the Contract Price, which will be set out as a separate line item on any invoice submitted by the Consultant. All payments will be in Canadian funds. 
Invoices. Prior to the 25th of each month, the Consultant will prepare and submit to the Owner a detailed invoice of fees and pre-authorized expenses. The invoice will include a contract summary report in the form attached as Schedule “D” – Contract Summary Report (a “Contract Summary Report”), which lists the work broken down by ‘Services Category’ as shown in Schedule “B” – Compensation, and includes columns for the contract amount, percentage of the “Services Category” complete, the previous billings, current invoice amount and the balance remaining. All invoices will be provided with evidence substantiating time spent and expenses incurred.
Timesheets. If requested by the Owner, the Consultant will deliver timesheets for all employees of the Consultant and of any subconsultant performing Services.
Payment. The following will apply with respect to payment of an invoice:
Invoices, along with a Contract Summary Report, must be submitted to payables@wesgroup.ca prior to the 25th of a month for payment by the Owner to be made on the last day of the following month. Invoices received after the 25th of a month will not be processed for payment until the following month and payment will become due on the last day of the second month after receipt of the invoice.
The amount invoiced by the Consultant shall be the value of the Services performed by the Consultant or any subconsultant on or before the date of the invoice, proportionate to the Contract Price (as shown in Schedule “B” – Compensation) agreed to between the Owner and the Consultant. 
If the Owner does not agree with the invoice or portion of an invoice, the Owner will review the invoice with the Consultant. If the disagreement cannot be resolved between the Owner and the Consultant, the Owner will pay the undisputed portion of the invoice and will include with the payment an explanation for any such invoice reduction and withhold the disputed payment until such dispute is resolved.
Payment Not a Waiver. No payment made under this Agreement will constitute a waiver of any terms of this Agreement or other rights at law or in equity.
CHANGES
Changes. The Owner may, without invalidating this Agreement, by written direction to the Consultant, make changes to the Services by altering, adding to or deducting from the Services, with adjustments, if any, to the Contract Price or the time for the performance of the Services or both. The Contract Price will be adjusted by the addition or deletion of fixed price line items in Schedule “B” Compensation, unless otherwise agreed by the parties. Any such adjustment to the Contract Price and the time for performance of the Services will be agreed to in consultation with the Consultant and shall only be effective upon written authorization of the Owner to the Consultant.
WORK PRODUCT
Ownership of Work Product. Copyright for the Consultant’s Work Product belongs to the Consultant, and remains the property of the Consultant whether the project for which they are made is executed or not, and whether or not the Consultant has been paid for the Services. The Consultant represents and warrants that it has not breached, and will not breach, any third party’s intellectual property rights in connection with the performance of the Services.
Grant of Licence. Subject to the Owner’s fulfilment of its payment obligations under this Agreement, the Consultant hereby grants to the Owner an irrevocable, perpetual, nonexclusive, fee-free, royalty-free, assignable licence to use, reproduce, or publish (including in a future procurement process), and to permit others on behalf of the Owner to use, reproduce, or publish (including in a future procurement process), any intellectual property rights owned by, controlled by, licensed to or used by the Consultant to the extent such intellectual property rights are incorporated into the Work Product, in connection with the construction, completion, operation, maintenance, repair, refurbishment or alteration of the Project or any part of the Project, including in the event of termination of the Consultant prior to completion of the design.
“Work Product” means anything created or developed by or on behalf of the Consultant, whether alone or jointly with others, in connection with the Services, including, without limitation, all designs, reports, photographs, drawings, plans, specifications, computer software and print-outs, surveys, calculations and other data, information and materials collected, computed, drawn, created, developed or produced by the Consultant in the performance of the Services and all concepts, products or processes produced by or resulting from the Services rendered by the Consultant, or which are otherwise developed or first reduced to practice by the Consultant, whether alone or jointly with others, in the performance of the Services.
The Owner’s Right to Access the Work Product. The Owner will at all times have the right to review all Work Product and may, from time to time, require the Consultant to deliver Work Product to the Owner for review, acceptance and further handling or distribution as permitted by this Agreement, in such formats as the Owner may reasonably request and at no cost to the Owner. Such review and acceptance by the Owner will not affect or diminish in any way the obligations and liabilities of the Consultant with respect to the Services or otherwise arising, provided such review is carried out in a timely manner so as to not affect the schedule for the Project.
Consent to Use after Termination. In the event of termination of this Agreement, for any reason, the Consultant will provide its consent to any successor professional, including any architect, to use the Work Product so that such successor professional can continue with the Project and complete the design.
Alteration of Work Product. Without limiting any of the Consultant’s obligations under this Agreement, if the Owner (or another consultant of the Owner) alters the Work Product after completion or termination of this Agreement, then the Consultant shall have no liability to the Owner in respect of any losses to the extent such losses arise from the alteration of the Work Product.
Subconsultants
Subconsultants and Subcontracting. The Consultant will not engage any subconsultants, or subcontract its obligations under this Agreement, in whole or in part, without the Owner’s prior written consent. Neither the engagement of a subconsultant by the Consultant nor the approval or consent by the Owner of or to a subconsultant will in any way reduce or amend or otherwise alter the Consultant’s responsibility for the performance of the Services as set out in this Agreement.
INSURANCE 
Consultant Insurance. Without limiting any of the Consultant’s obligations or liabilities under this Agreement and prior to commencing any Services, the Consultant will obtain and maintain during the performance of the Services or as otherwise required by this Agreement, at its own expense and with insurance providers acceptable to the Owner, acting reasonably, the following insurance:
Workers’ Compensation coverage for all employees engaged in the Services in accordance with the Workers Compensation Act (British Columbia);
automobile liability on all owned and non-owned vehicles used by the Consultant in connection with this Agreement in the minimum amount of $5 million per occurrence in respect of bodily injury, death and property damage; 
subject to Section 6.4, professional liability insurance for the minimum amount of $2 million per claim with an aggregate limit of $2 million per 12 month policy period, which coverage will be maintained for a period ending no sooner than six (6) years after the Consultant has ceased to provide Services to the Owner under the terms of this Agreement; and 
commercial general liability insurance for the minimum amount of $5 million per occurrence in respect of bodily injury, death and property damage, which coverage will include Broad Form Completed Operations coverage, a cross liability and severability of interests clause. 
“Consultant Required Policies” means the insurance policies to be obtained and maintained by the Consultant pursuant to Section 6.1(a) to Section 6.1(d), inclusive. The Consultant Required Policies limit may be satisfied with a combination of commercial general liability and umbrella/excess liability policies."
