the commercial general liability insurance required under Section 6.1(d) will include [insert the full legal names of the beneficial owner, general partner and the registered owner of the property] and all subsidiary, affiliated and associated entities, and their respective partners, directors, officers, shareholders, employees, servants and agents as additional insureds in respect of liability arising out of the Consultant's operations, and will contain a waiver of any right or subrogation or recourse abating the Owner, its directors, officers, shareholders, employees, servants and agents;
certificates of insurance for the Consultant Required Policies (including a WorkSafeBC Clearance letter as evidence of Worker’s Compensation coverage) will be submitted to the Owner prior to commencing any Services and upon renewals of such insurance not less than ten (10) days prior to the expiration of any such policy. All such policies will be placed with insurers acceptable to the Owner and be in a policy form acceptable to the Owner. The approval or non-approval of any such policy by the Owner will in no way relieve the Consultant of its obligations to provide the insurance required by this Agreement; and
contain a provision that the insurance cannot be cancelled, lapsed on renewal or detrimentally and materially changed without at least 30 days written notice to the Owner.
Minimum Amount No Limit on Recovery. The Consultant Required Policies are the minimum policy limits and types of insurance that are to be obtained and maintained by the Consultant. The Consultant will be solely responsible for determining whether the policy limits and types of insurance are adequate and for placing any excess insurance and any additional insurance which it considers necessary to protect and indemnify itself.
Project Specific Liability Insurance. Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this Agreement, the Owner may, at its option and cost, arrange for and maintain a single project professional liability insurance policy (the “Project Policy”) in accordance with the following terms and conditions:
The Project Policy will have a limit of no less than $5,000,000, to cover against any and all claims made for negligent acts, errors or omissions of, or attributable to, or relating to the Consultant’s design and performance of the Services, for which the Consultant and the Consultant’s sub-consultants (if applicable) are at law responsible, with sub-limits, conditions and deductibles in amounts reasonably obtainable at the time of policy placement and as selected by the Owner; 
The Project Policy shall be the primary policy for insured consultants in connection with the Project; 
The Consultant shall comply with the underwriters of the Project Policy to the extent reasonably required to procure and maintain coverage under the Project Policy; and
The Consultant shall be required to represent and warrant to the Owner and the Owner’s insurer that, to the best of its knowledge, there are no claims pending relating to the Project.
If the Owner opts not to obtain the Project Policy, the Consultant shall obtain and maintain the professional liability insurance coverage contemplated in Section 6.1(c).
Deductibles. The Consultant shall be responsible for and shall not seek contribution from the Owner for any deductibles or self-insured retentions under any of the Consultant Required Policies (or arranged by the Owner in accordance with Section 6.4, if applicable) to the extent that the Consultant is responsible for the negligent act, error or omission in respect of which the claim is made. Provided however that, in the event that the Owner obtains project specific liability insurance in accordance with Section 6.4, the Consultant shall only be responsible for a deductible up to a maximum of $50,000 and, if the deductible exceeds such amount, the Owner shall be responsible for any portion of the deductible in excess of $50,000.
TERMINATION
Termination for Default
If the Consultant should fail or neglect to perform the Services properly and expeditiously, or the Consultant should otherwise fail to comply with the requirements of this Agreement to a substantial degree, then the Owner may provide the Consultant with written notice stating the nature of the Consultant’s default and instructing the Consultant to correct the default within five days after receipt of such notice. 
If the Consultant fails to correct the default in the time specified in Section 7.1.1 or subsequently agreed in writing, or, if, for any reason, the default cannot be corrected, then the Owner may, without prejudice to any of its other rights or remedies, terminate this Agreement.
Termination for Convenience. The Owner may terminate this Agreement at any time for any reason (or no reason) upon ten days written notice to the Consultant.
Effect of Termination. Upon termination of this Agreement pursuant to Section 7.0:
the Owner will pay the Consultant for Services performed in accordance with this Agreement to the date of termination; and
provided the Owner has complied with Section 7.3(a) (and for certainty, subject to the Owner’s right to withhold disputed amounts in accordance with Section 2.4(c)), the Consultant will promptly provide the Owner with the Work Product and all other information requested by the Owner.
INDEMNITY
The Consultant shall indemnify and save harmless the Owner, its affiliates and their respective directors, officers, shareholders, employees, agents and consultants (the “Releasees”) from and against any and all liabilities, damages, assessments, penalties, fines, causes of action, claims, suits, judgments, costs and expenses, of whatever kind (a “Claim”), arising by reason of any injury to or death of any person, or damage to any property including consequential loss, which the Releasees may incur or suffer or be put to by reason of or in connection with or arising solely from:"
