any error, omission or negligent act of the Consultant or any person for whom it is responsible for, at law, in connection with or incidental to the Services to be performed under this Agreement,
provided that if it is determined by final adjudication of a court of competent jurisdiction, or the final award of a binding arbitration, that the Consultant was only partially responsible for a Claim, the Consultant shall be required to indemnify and save harmless the Owner only for that portion thereof which such court or arbitrator determines is attributable to or is the responsibility of the Consultant.
CONFIDENTIALITY
The Consultant will not, and will ensure that its employees and subconsultants will not, during or after the performance of the Services, disclose any information concerning the business affairs of the Owner, which the Consultant may have acquired in the course of or incidental to this Agreement or otherwise, unless to further the interests of the Owner or as required by law.
The Consultant will be responsible for any breach of this obligation of confidentiality by its employees or subconsultants. This confidentiality provision will remain in full force and effect until the earlier of the date in which the confidential information becomes available in the public domain (other than by breach of this Agreement by the Consultant, its employees or subconsultants) or for a period of five years after the completion or termination of this Agreement.
NOTICE
Address for Notice. Any notice or communication required or permitted to be given under this Agreement will be in writing and will be considered to have been sufficiently given when delivered by registered mail, by hand or by email to the address of the applicable party set out below:
to the Owner:
Suite 2000 – 595 Burrard Street
Vancouver, BC V6C 0E4
Fax: 604-632-1737"
