Email: [____________________] 
to such other address as either party may, from time to time, designate in the manner set out above.
GENERAL TERMS
Conflict of Interest. The Consultant will notify the Owner immediately in writing of any circumstance, situation or event which could potentially cause, directly or indirectly, a conflict of interest in the performance of the Services. In the event the Consultant notifies the Owner of a circumstance, situation or event under this Section 10.1, the Consultant acknowledges and agrees that the Owner may, in its sole discretion and without having to justify its decision, suspend or terminate immediately this Agreement.
Independent Contractor. The Consultant will be deemed to be acting solely as an independent contractor and nothing contained in this Agreement will at any time be construed as creating the relationship of employer and employee, partnership, principal and agent, or joint venture as between the Owner and the Consultant. The Consultant will have no authority to make any statements, representations, or commitments of any kind, or to take any action, which will be binding on the Owner, except as may be expressly provided for in this Agreement or as otherwise expressly authorized in writing by the Owner.
No Assignment. The Consultant may not assign this Agreement, or the proceeds thereof, in whole or in part without the Owner’s prior written consent.
Survival. The exclusions, waivers and limitations of liability, representations and warranties and indemnities in this Agreement, the provisions of Sections 4.0 (Work Product), 7.4 (Indemnity) and 8.0 (Confidentiality) and rights accrued prior to completion or termination of this Agreement will survive the completion or termination of this Agreement.
Governing Law. This Agreement will be governed and construed in accordance with the laws of the Province of British Columbia.
Severability. Each provision of this Agreement is severable. If any provision of this Agreement is to any extent invalid or unenforceable, the remainder of this Agreement will not be affected and each remaining provision of this Agreement will be separately valid and will be enforceable.
Entire Agreement, Waivers and Consents in Writing. This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties, expressly superseding all prior agreements and communications (both oral and written) between the parties with respect to the performance of the Services. No waiver of any provision of this Agreement and no consent required pursuant to this Agreement is binding or effective unless it is in writing and signed by the party providing such waiver or consent. A waiver of any breach of this Agreement is not a waiver of any continuing or subsequent breach.
Enurement. This Agreement will enure to the benefit of and be binding upon the successors and permitted assigns of the parties.
Counterparts. This Agreement may be executed and delivered in several counterparts, including by facsimile (or other similar electronic means, including via pdf), each of which when so executed and delivered will be deemed to be an original and such counterparts together will be but one and the same instrument.
Dispute Resolution. If any disputes arise during the performance of the Services as to the interpretation, application or administration of this Agreement, including in respect of payments under Section 2.4, the Consultant and the Owner shall make all reasonable efforts to resolve disputes by amicable negotiations and shall provide, on a without prejudice basis, frank, candid and timely disclosure of relevant facts, information and documents to facilitate negotiations. If the parties so agree, the dispute may be submitted to mediation or arbitration in accordance with CCDC 40- Rules for Mediation and Arbitration of Construction Industry Disputes, in effect on the date of this Agreement."
