After the initial stages of design are complete, Jim DesRoches will be assisted by senior partner, John Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng. Struct.Eng., PE, SE, who is a licensed Structural Engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, California, Washington, Arizona, and Texas, and has more than 30 years of experience designing a wide variety of buildings, including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, and institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, and office buildings. John Markulin is responsible for delivering innovative structural engineering solutions for some of the firm’s most notable projects. John is an accomplished engineer with significant project experience in the design of reinforced concrete, pre-cast concrete, cast-in-place concrete, post-tensioned concrete, tilt-up concrete, structural steel, load-bearing steel stud, wood-frame, and masonry, as well as floor systems, vertical load systems and seismic and lateral systems. 

