These Standard Terms and Conditions shall form part of the Agreement to which they are attached.

Responsibilities of Kinetica
The responsibilities of Kinetica are expressly limited to those services as described in the attached Agreement. 

Where services involve:
The provision of Construction Cost Estimates: Kinetica does not warrant the accuracy of these estimates; 
Structural Modeling: Kinetica does not warrant any of the modeling parameters (mass, stiffness and/or damping) of the building assumed by the Engineer of Record. If the built building structure behaves differently from those assumed in the structural model used to study the impact of the dampers or overall structural behavior, Kinetica does not warrant the effects of those differences on the accuracy of the structural performance or the damping system performance.
Structural Loading: Kinetica does not warrant any of the loads provided from the wind tunnel or inherent damping of the structure itself used to produce those lateral loads or accelerations.

Where services involve Construction Phase-Contract Administration: 
Kinetica shall not be required to make exhaustive or continuous reviews of the Work beyond General Reviews;
Kinetica shall not be responsible for the acts or omissions of the Contractor or any other persons performing any of the Work, or the failure of any of them to carry out the Work in Accordance with the Contract Documents;
Kinetica shall not have control or responsibility for construction ways, means, methods, techniques, or safety. 

Responsibilities of the Client or Clients Representatives
The Client or client’s representatives shall provide full information required for Kinetica to provide their services including:
A program setting forth Project objectives, constraints, schedules, and criteria;
A Construction Budget, including reasonable contingencies, and;
All building structural properties including geometry and structural properties.

The Client or client’s representatives shall: 
Examine all documents and requests presented by Kinetica and promptly provide, in writing, decisions, approvals, and instructions;
Obtain and pay the cost of all specialty consultants;
Authorize a person to act on the Client’s behalf;
Promptly fulfill the Client’s responsibilities for the orderly progress of the services of Kinetica;
Immediately notify Kinetica in writing if the Client observes or otherwise becomes aware of a fault or defect in the Project or any nonconformity with the requirements of the Construction Contract.

Payment
The Client shall pay Kinetica the fees as described in the attached Agreement, plus all applicable taxes, and duties. 

The Client shall pay for any additional services agreed to that are not included in services described in the attached Agreement. 

If the scope, size, budget, or schedule of the Project, or of the services provided by Kinetica are changed, then the fees shall be equitably adjusted.

Payment shall follow the standard payment procedures of Kinetica unless provided otherwise in the attached Agreement. Kinetica will submit monthly invoices to the Client for services rendered to the date of invoice. The Client shall pay the full amount within 30 days of the date of invoice. Overdue accounts shall incur interest at 3% above prime rate. Kinetica may, at its discretion, suspend services for non-payment of accounts overdue by more than 60 days of the date of the invoice. 

Copyright & Use of Documents
Kinetica shall be deemed the authors and owners of their respective Instruments of Service, and shall retain all common law, statutory and other reserved rights, including copyrights.  

Upon execution of the attached Agreement, Kinetica grants to the Client a nonexclusive license to use the Instruments of Service solely and exclusively for purposes of constructing, managing, using, maintaining, altering and adding to the Project, provided that the Client substantially performs its obligations, including prompt payment of all sums when due, under this Agreement.  

In the event the Client uses the Instruments of Service without retaining Kinetica, the Client releases Kinetica from all claims and causes of action arising from such uses and agrees to indemnify and hold harmless Kinetica and Kinetica’s consultants from all costs and expenses, including the cost of defense, related to claims and causes of action asserted by any third person or entity to the extent such costs and expenses arise from the Client’s use of the Instruments of Service.

Indemnity
Kinetica carries professional errors and omissions liability insurance coverage. 

All claims, whether in Contract or in Tort, that the Client has or hereafter may have against Kinetica, including corporate owners and directors, agents, representatives, or sub-consultants of Kinetica, in any way arising out of or related to Kinetica’s duties and responsibilities pursuant to this Agreement, shall be limited to the value of the contract. The Client shall indemnify Kinetica from and against any and all claims made against Kinetica in excess of such amount. In any event, Kinetica shall not, in any circumstances, be liable for any losses other than those caused by Kinetica’s negligent acts and shall not be liable for any consequential loss or damage such as loss due to delays to the Project, loss of earnings, or loss of profits, howsoever caused. 

Kinetica will perform the services to the Standard of Care ordinarily exercised by other members of the profession under similar circumstances, at the same time and in the same or a similar locale. 

Kinetica shall be entitled to rely upon product information published by manufacturers and shall not be held liable for relying on information or representation which it reasonably believes to be accurate.

Kinetica shall not: 
be required to make exhaustive or continuous on-site reviews; 
be responsible for acts or omissions of the contractor, subcontractors, suppliers or any other persons performing any of the Work, or for failure of any of them to carry out the Work in accordance with the contract documents; 
have control, charge, or supervision, or responsibility for construction means, methods, techniques, sequences, or procedures, or, for safety precautions and programs required in connection with the Work.

The Client acknowledges that either Kinetica or the Client may engage consultants on behalf of and for the benefit and convenience of the Client; and agrees that Kinetica shall not be liable to the Client, in contract or in tort, for the acts, omissions or errors of such consultants whether retained by Kinetica or the Client. The Client also agrees to limit the professional liability for services rendered by such consultants to the lesser of the amount stated in this agreement or the amount of the professional liability insurance carried by each consultant.

The Client shall not commence any claim or proceeding in contract, tort, breach of statutory duty or otherwise against any current or former employee, officer or director of Kinetica arising out of acts omissions or errors of such person pursuant to this contract. 

Termination
Unless otherwise stated in the attached Agreement, the services of Kinetica terminate after completion of the work. 

Mediation 
In an effort to resolve any conflicts that arise during the design or construction of the project or following the completion of the project, the Client and Kinetica agree to use all reasonable efforts to resolve such disputes between themselves. 

The Client and Kinetica further agree that all disputes between them arising out of or relating to this Agreement shall be submitted to nonbinding mediation unless the parties mutually agree otherwise. 

Governing Laws and Assignment
This Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario. Neither the Client nor Kinetica shall assign their obligations without the consent of the other. Such consent shall not be unreasonably withheld."
