Kor Structural (""KOR"") is a Vancouver based Structural Engineering firm with satellite offices in Kelowna and Nanaimo. For over 25 years, we’ve provided expert consultation, design, and field review services throughout British Columbia and across North America.
With a portfolio of over 2,000 projects across Canada and the United States, we specialize in delivering efficient, creative, and buildable Structural solutions. Our expertise covers all building types from tall towers (up to 65 storeys), mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, institutional/public facilities, sports facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, office buildings, and more. 
Our team of Professional Engineers are licensed in provinces across Canada and in multiple U.S. States, including Washington, California, Arizona, and Texas. 
Founded by three seasoned Professional Engineers, Kor has grown to a team of 40+ professionals driven by a commitment to superior client service, innovative design, and quality execution. We collaborate closely with your design team to ensure every project starts with a strong foundation, both structurally and collaboratively, built on technical excellence, innovative tools, and a steadfast commitment to supporting you and your team at every stage of development, design, and construction. 
Our Services
At Kor, Structural Engineering is a seamless blend of creative design and practical solutions where we bring innovative structures to life through collaboration and precision. Our expertise includes:
Residential / Commercial
High-rise reinforced concrete structures
Mid-rise multifamily buildings (wood and concrete)
Structural steel buildings
Commercial developments and mixed-use projects
Office buildings and hotels 

Community, Cultural, and Industrial 
Community and cultural buildings
Healthcare facilities and social housing
Sport facilities and arenas 
Warehouses and light industrial facilities

Renovations & Retrofits
Renovations, retrofits, and structural upgrades
Analysis and design of unique or complex structural systems

Performance-Based Design
Seismic performance-based analysis and design
Our integrated Engineering, Drafting, and Construction teams work to deliver innovative designs that reduce turnaround times and optimize costs. Our goal is to make your vision structurally possible while being a reliable, responsive partner every step of the way"
8e6e6e86aad3,31247-01,31247-01,Baydo Contracting Corporation,13433 Gateway Dr Surrey,KOR,proposal,,,2026-09-22,opportunities,Management\Project Opportunities\Word Documents for Awarded Projects\31247-01 Baydo Contracting 13433 Gateway Dr Surrey BC 2026-09-16 KOR OAP JM.docx,,0p5,Project Description,permits_approvals|field_review,329,"Project Description
Our proposed fees are based on the following assumptions:
The project comprises two towers ranging from 30 to 40 storeys in height with a 4-storey podium built over 6 levels of below grade parking structure shown as East and West Towers:
East Tower (Ph1): 37-storey tower including approximately 258 residential units, amenity and childcare space.
West Tower (Ph2): 40-storey tower including approximately 407 residential units, amenity and childcare space.
The total gross buildable area for the above including foundations, parking, amenity, childcare, balconies, roofs and other structural areas is estimated to be 1,108,130 sq.ft. with 7.44 FSR (3.5 base + 0.7 FSR bonus), and the estimated breakdown is as follows:
East Tower: 317,375 sq.ft. gross calculated area including podium. 
West Tower: 426,364 sq.ft. gross calculated area.
Parking: 364,392 sq.ft. gross calculated area.
The below fixed fees are based on1,108,130 sq.ft. of structural area. If the final area is increased or decreased, then our fees will be adjusted proportionally.
Proposed Fees
The following fees are for complete Structural Engineering services for the project as noted in the following Scope of Structural Services. The proposed fixed fees for our services are as follows:
† Additional field reviews over the above specified limit will be billed at a rate of $350 per visit, covering up to 2.0 hours, at which point hourly rates will apply. 
Over and above the noted proposed fixed fees, we recommend a budget allowance of $1,500 for normal disbursements (e.g., courier costs and printing drawing sets, if required).
Scope of Structural Services
Our scope of services encompasses comprehensive collaboration with the Architect and other consultants, ensuring seamless project development using Revit LOD 300. We prioritize effective coordination throughout the construction documentation process, allowing for structural adjustments as necessary to align with the Architect's vision and the requirements of other consultants. Additionally, we are committed to maintaining budgetary alignment while incorporating recommendations from specialist consultants as needed. Building Permit schedules are included in our fees.

Schematic Design:"
8e6e6e86aad3,31247-01,31247-01,Baydo Contracting Corporation,13433 Gateway Dr Surrey,KOR,proposal,,,2026-09-22,opportunities,Management\Project Opportunities\Word Documents for Awarded Projects\31247-01 Baydo Contracting 13433 Gateway Dr Surrey BC 2026-09-16 KOR OAP JM.docx,,0p6,Prepare schematic design documents in sufficient detail to establish the following structural systems:,permits_approvals|field_review,274,"Prepare schematic design documents in sufficient detail to establish the following structural systems:
Foundation system.
Structural framing concept.
Preparation of structural sketches or drawings as necessary to describe the structural concept.
Attendance at design meetings as required by the Architect and/or Client.

Design Development:

Prepare preliminary documents in sufficient detail to establish the following main structural systems in sufficient detail for coordination with other disciplines:
Foundation system including typical details.
Structural framing system including typical details.
Coordinate structure with special design criteria.
Coordinate structural systems with Client and other affected disciplines.
Attendance at design meetings as required by the Architect and/or Owner.

Construction Documents:

Finalize the preparation of the following documentation:
Structural Drawings.
Structural Specifications.
Structural Calculations.
Typical and custom details.
Building Permit Schedules
Coordinate documents with Architect and other affected disciplines.
Attendance at design meetings as required by the Architect and/or Owner.
Incorporate the recommendations of any specialist consultants if required.
Assist in establishing testing and inspection requirements for concrete and other materials to be carried out by the Client or by their representatives.
Respond to plan check comments and revise structural construction documents as required by the local authority or government agency.
Provide structural addenda or clarifications during Client bidding or negotiating with construction contractors.
Provide Final Design drawings at project completion that incorporate any structural revisions that occur during the construction phase.

Construction Administration:

Perform site reviews of structural elements during construction, including coordinating with the contractor for scheduling of field reviews.
Respond to contractor information requests during construction and provide interpretations of structural construction documents.
Review shop drawing submittals for structural elements.
Review material testing and inspection reports

Excluded Services"
8e6e6e86aad3,31247-01,31247-01,Baydo Contracting Corporation,13433 Gateway Dr Surrey,KOR,proposal,,,2026-09-22,opportunities,Management\Project Opportunities\Word Documents for Awarded Projects\31247-01 Baydo Contracting 13433 Gateway Dr Surrey BC 2026-09-16 KOR OAP JM.docx,,0p7,"Construction Management, other than the construction support services identified in the Scope of Services.",insurance|payment|permits_approvals|assignment_subconsultants|field_review,342,"Construction Management, other than the construction support services identified in the Scope of Services.
Cost Estimating Services.
Clash detection or other Coordination with sub-contractors to the General Contractor.
Review of Value Engineering reports or studies.
Design of excavation shoring and underpinning of adjacent buildings for the construction of the project.
Design of temporary structures utilized by contractors for construction means and methods, such as crane tiebacks, crane foundations, platforms, climbing formwork systems, thrust blocks, erection support systems and methods, etc.
Design of non-load bearing exterior wall panels, walls, cladding, and railings.
Design of secondary structures not forming part of the base building structure but associated with the civil engineering components of the project, such as filtration well containers, manhole sleeves, precast buried sump pits, water meter vaults, and similar ancillary structures.
Subsurface soil investigation and inspection of geotechnical aspects of foundation construction, including sampling, testing, and reporting on materials used in construction, and coordination with specialist consultants such as geotechnical and materials testing engineers.
Design and construction review of concrete formwork and design changes to accommodate temporary construction conditions.
Design and supervision of nonstructural components, such as monument signage, exterior infill framing, equipment racks or connections, interior architectural system attachments, window washing systems, and tiedowns.
Design of connections for mechanical, electrical, or plumbing equipment and systems.
Government tax on professional fees.
Providing details for repair of defective construction.
Review of Core Holes in existing structures.
Normal disbursements, which include courier costs, plotting of other consultants’ drawings, and printing, etc. We do not markup disbursements.
Insurance and Billing
Kor Structural carries professional liability insurance. Monthly invoices will be issued for completed work and reimbursable expenses.

We trust the foregoing proposal meets your expectations. We wish to thank you for your consideration of Kor Structural for this project, and we look forward to working with you and your team on this project.
Yours truly,
Kor Structural
