Dear Dennis,

Re: Fee Proposal for Structural Engineering Services
 990 George Street, Vancouver, B.C. – Core Hole Review 
 Kor Reference Number: 40102-07

Enclosed is our fee proposal for structural engineering services for the above noted project. The project is described in your Request for Structural Consulting Services Fee Proposal dated June 8, 2023.

Project Description

Our scope of structural engineering services includes the following:

Review of the proposed core hole locations.

The proposed fixed fees for our services are $2,000.

Pre-payment is required for all projects. We require a 100% payment of the fee + GST prior to commencement of services. 

Please note that we carry sufficient professional liability insurance.

Summary of Typical Services and Exclusions

Our services would not include any of the following:

Design and construction review of concrete formwork and design changes to accommodate temporary construction conditions.
Design and supervision of non-structural components. Normal current practice is that non-structural components are designed and certified by subtrades' engineers. For example, exterior windows are commonly designed and certified by the window subcontractor's professional engineer. Please note that we will provide the architect with all necessary advice and specification requirements for such items as he may request.
Services outside the original scope of work outlined above will be billed on an hourly rates basis in addition to the proposed fixed fees.
Normal disbursements, which include courier costs, plotting of other consultants’ drawings, and printing, etc. We do not markup disbursements.
Government tax on professional fees.



Approval to Proceed

We will proceed with our work upon receipt of a signed copy of this fee proposal. If you have any questions or need additional information, please contact the undersigned.

We propose to invoice on a monthly basis. It is our policy to state that we reserve the right to discontinue our work if the client fails to meet his commitments, and we will not be responsible for any damages arising therefrom.

We trust the foregoing proposal meets your expectations. We wish to thank you for consideration of Kor Structural for this project, and we look forward to working with you again. 
Yours truly,

Kor Structural
EGBC Permit #1000378







____________________________________________
Chelsea Armstrong, née Lewis
Principal, Finance/Office Manager for:
Kevin Wurmlinger, P.Eng. Struct.Eng., CEng, MIStructE
Principal, Senior Structural Engineer





