ab9108c9e4a9,OPP:PCY -Marriott Hotel Fee Proposal from John Bryson,,,,KOR,proposal,,,2003-03-27,opportunities,Management\Project Opportunities\Word Documents for Awarded Projects\0. Archived Proposals (1998-2017)\2003\PCY -Marriott Hotel Fee Proposal from John Bryson.doc,,2,"2.      Structural observations and construction phase services                        $  15,000.00 CDN",insurance|permits_approvals|field_review,622,"2. Structural observations and construction phase services $ 15,000.00 CDN

 Total Fees: $ 75,000.00 CDN


The foregoing fees are for normal basic structural engineering services provided by Seattle structural engineers for building projects, and includes all structural engineering design and working drawings for the base building structure, and construction phase services which includes “structural observations” required by the Uniform Building Code and also review of the reports by the special inspector and materials testing engineers and also dealing with site questions and clarifications. Note that “structural observations” will be made in accordance with the requirements of the Uniform Building Code and the City of Bellevue, however, detailed inspections of construction of structural aspects of the work are to be a “special inspector” as required by the Uniform Building Code, and our fixed fee does not include hiring or paying the “special inspector”.





In addition to the foregoing fixed fees, we will bill for normal disbursements at cost, only, with no mark-up. Normal disbursements include printing costs (printing of design calculations in booklet form as required by the Building Department and printing of drawings); plotting of other consultants’ drawings; courier costs, including overnight courier services; and travel expenses (mileage costs, which we will bill at a fixed rate of $100.00 U.S. per trip to Seattle). 


We will bill you on a monthly basis for our services. 


The foregoing fixed fees are for normal structural engineering services, as follows:

Design and working drawing phase

This phase includes all structural engineering services up to the point when building permit is obtained. 

Structural engineering design, specifications and working drawings for all structural elements of the base building structure, including building permit drawings and construction-ready drawings. . Response to the City of Bellevue’s structural review is included, along with all building permit re-submittals required by the City of Bellevue, up to the point when a building permit is received. 

Construction phase services

Detailed inspections of the structural aspects of construction are to be by a special inspector, hired and paid by the owner. The cost of the special inspector is not included in our fees. 

Structural observations. We will make structural observations as required by the 1997 Uniform Building Code and by the City of Bellevue.

We will review test reports by others, the special inspector’s reports and structural shop drawings, as required by the 1997 Uniform Building Code and the City of Bellevue.

We will provide all documentation required by the City of Bellevue to be submitted by the structural engineer of record.


Please note that the foregoing construction phase services does not make us guarantors of the contractor’s work. The contractor is responsible for the construction of the structure in accordance with the approved building permit drawings. Also, the contractor is responsible for construction safety issues, including the safety of any temporary work, such as shoring, formwork, and any other work aid used by him.





Please note that we carry 1 million Canadian dollars professional liability insurance, and we are insured in the U.S.A. The amount of our liability insurance can be increased for this project, however, we would expect the client to pay any additional premiums.



Services Not Included
 
Our services do not included any of the following:

 Subsurface soil investigation and report, and inspection of the geotechnical aspects of foundation construction; sampling, testing and reporting on materials used in construction; and retaining specialist consultants such as geotechnical engineers and testing engineers.

Detailed inspection of construction of the structural aspects of the work. Our site visits will be solely for the purposes of making “structural observations” as required by the 1997 Uniform Building Code and the City of Bellevue. Detailed inspections are required by Code to be performed by an independent “special inspection” agency."
