The above fees are fees for complete structural engineering services for the project, including all structural engineering design, all structural engineering working drawings for construction purposes, and all inspections required by the building authority. 

Of the foregoing fees, all preliminary work will be charged on an Hourly Basis in accordance with the attached List of Hourly Charge Out Rates, however, please note that all hourly charges for preliminary work are included in the above fixed fees. 



Reimbursable and Non-Reimbursable Expenses


Reimbursable disbursements include courier costs and “final printing, plotting and other reproduction expenses (receipts to be provided, at actual cost, without mark-up) relating to printing of drawings for coordination and building permit purposes. (Please note that costs for mass printing including issuance for Tender and Construction are not included in our fees and are to be billed directly to Client by the printing company.) 



Reimbursable expenses will not include CAD plotting expenses related to in-house printing, and will not include the cost of printing related to in-house prints; however, John Bryson & Partners reserves the right to charge the Client for plotting of other consultants’ drawings during the consultation and design phase in the case that full-sized hard copy sets of other consultants’ drawings cannot be provided, or provided in a timely manner. Local mileage will not be considered to be reimbursable.


Capacity and Capability

To demonstrate the ability of John Bryson & Partners to provide sufficient professional competence, to meet time schedules, to accommodate cost considerations and project administration requirements, we provide the following documentation as part of the Appendix Section attached to this Fee Proposal, which includes the following:

List of Recent and Current Similar Projects
Resumes for John A. Markulin, Struct.Eng. and John Bryson, P.Eng
List of References
Introduction to John Bryson & Partners brochure

We also refer you to our website (www.jbp.ca) for an extensive photo profile of past, recent, and current projects by type and geographic location ranging from the Western Canada; Washington, Arizona, and California; and Mexico.

Structural Design and Management Team: John Markulin will be the Engineer of Record and the primary contact for this project during both the design and construction phases. John Markulin is a senior partner with John Bryson & Partners and has over 16 years’ experience in the design of residential, commercial and industrial buildings utilizing a wide variety of structural materials, and he recently was involved with the CSA Clause 21 committee regarding the updating of Concrete Code Seismic Design Requirements. John Bryson, who will be the back-up engineer for this project, has more than 35 years’ experience and has been successfully leading the team of John Bryson & Partners based on his philosophy of the importance of the constant awareness of architectural and other project consultants’ concerns which interface with structural design, which enables the consultant team to produce an economical design well co-ordinated to the needs of the client. 


Resources and Availability: We have reviewed your anticipated schedule and milestones for Phase 1 of the development. We wish to assure you that we have the engineering and drafting resources to meet your project schedules as outlined in your RFP. 




Past and Current Projects of Similar Nature:

Some of our recent projects similar to the subject proposed Phase 1 development include:
Madison Centre, Lougheed & Willingdon, Burnaby. For Appia Developments. Mixed use development, including a 7 storey retail and officebuilding, and Save-On Food Store.
Highgate Village, mixed use development, Middlegate, Burnaby. For Bosa Ventures Inc. Includes a Save-On Food Store.
Ocean Pointe and Suncliffe Place, 152 St/17 Ave., Surrey. For V1500 Holdings. A 4- storey office/retail building and 4-storey condominium apartment building.
Newport Village, Port Moody. For Bosa Developments Corp. Mixed use community development including a 7 storey retail and office building, plus multiple 4 storey multi-residential containing commercial/retail space on the ground floor.
The Alda – 1275 Hamilton Yaletown – 6 storey residential condominium building and 1250 Homer office building, both with retail/commercial uses on the ground floor.

Some of our current projects which contain components similar to the subject proposed development, which are either in the design stage or under construction, or almost completed construction, include:
Suterbrook, mixed use development, Port Moody. For The Onni Group. Includes midrise residential buildings with retail/commercial use on ground level.
Centrepoint, at 4800 Kingsway, Metrotown, Burnaby - mixed use development.. For Intracorp.
King Edward Village mixed use development, Kingsway & Knight, Vancouver.
North Road & Cameron, mixed use development, Coquitlam. For Ledingham McAllister. Includes a Save-On Food Store.
222 Riverfront Ave. S.W. mixed use development, Calgary. Alberta. For Anthem Properties.
Glen Drive @ Pacific, Coquitlam. Residential highrise and lowrise with retail/commercial on ground floor. For The Executive Group.

Past Record of Performance

References: With respect to our ability to meet schedules and budgets, and demonstrate the quality of our working relationships with clients and other consultants, we provide the following references:
Intracorp Developments Ltd., - Mr. Noel Richardson Tel: (604) 801-7000
Onni Group – Mr. Morris DeCotiis Tel: (604) 502-7711
Polygon Developments – Mr. Andre Chilcott Tel: (604) 877-1131
Bosa Development Corp. – Mr. Eric Martin Tel: (604) 294-0666
