Dear Sirs:

Re: REVISED Fee Proposal for Structural Engineering Services
 Abby Lane Shopping Centre 
Buildings A to J Inclusive – Shell Buildings Only; 
Building A2 – Drugstore, Only, to include T.I. Works
 Mount Lehman Road and Highway #1, Abbotsford, B.C.

This is our fee proposal for structural engineering services for the above project. The project is described in Shape Properties’ Request For Proposal dated July 23, 2009 and MCMP’s request for a fee proposal. The project is based on the “full parkade option” and consists of:
522,562 sq.ft. gross retail area contained in 15 separate commercial pad shell buildings
Ground Level: Anchor retail tenant Building A is 153,662 sq. ft. 
Note: Fee proposal revised: Building A to not include T.I. works.
Note: Building B Drug Store to include T.I. works.
Podium Level: Balance of Pad Buildings - gross retail area of 279,900 sq.ft. podium CRUs 
Second Floor of Buildings A3, A4, C and I - total 89,000 sq.ft. 2nd floor CRU gross retail area
Parking: Ground level parking 1,126 stalls; Podium level parking 335 stalls
Total structural area estimated to be approximately 1,000,000 sq. ft. 

Construction is assumed to be structural steel for the pad buildings. This fee proposal assumes conventional strip and pad footings. 

We understand that you will be targeting for LEED certification. We provide on page 3 of this proposal a description of our experience with LEED-certified projects. LEED certification documentation relating to the structure is dependent only upon recycled material content and chemical adjustments to concrete mixes. Such documentation is provided, supplied and organized by the Contractor. Therefore (as described on our attached Fee Summary & Breakdown), there are no additional fees charged within or over and above our structural fees for LEED design of the project. 


Abby Lane Shopping Centre is to be phased, as follows: 
Phase 1: Building A1 and podium, Buildings A2, A3, A4, A5, B, D, H, J
 Detailed Design to commence January, 2010
 Construction to commence for parkade August, 2010 or thereabouts
Phase 2: Buildings C, E, F, G1, G2, and I. 
 Detailed Design to commence June 15, 2011
 Construction to commence November 2011 or thereabouts.

Our proposed fixed fees for the structures of Phase 1 and Phase 2 are contained in the attached “Fee Summary and Breakdown” attached hereto. Please note that the Fixed Fee 2 Total for the parkade/base box structure/podium include a breakdown of the fee to provide for a primary design scheme and an additional alternative design scheme for either/or/and: (1) Cast-in-place concrete design, and (2) Precast concrete design.

The attached proposed fees are fees for complete structural engineering services for the project, including all structural engineering design, all structural engineering working drawings for construction purposes, and all inspections required by the building authority.

Breakdown of Fees:

Please find attached hereto our breakdown of fees, “Fee Summary & Breakdown” which provides the Design and Construction Phase Fees and for Disbursements, separate and combined.

Additional Services: 

Please find attached hereto our List of Hourly Charge Out rates. 

Disbursements

All normal disbursements including normal plotting of other consultants drawings, printing, and courier costs, and travel costs to Abbotsford, are included in the ‘Disbursements” column in the attached “Fee Summary & Breakdown”. 

Insurance Coverage

John Bryson & Partners carries the following insurance coverage:
Professional Liability Insurance: $1 million each claim and in aggregate annually.
Commercial General Liability Insurance: $3,000,000 limit .


Experience & Expertise of Structural Project Team and Individual Qualifications

We attach hereto “Section A: Individual Qualifications” which provides evidence of the expertise and experience of our structural team, of which the structural design project leader and Engineer-of-Record will be John Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng, Struct.Eng., backed up by John Bryson, M.Sc., P.Eng., Struct.Eng., and John Zickmantel, M.Eng., P.Eng. The list also includes lists of projects completed within the past five years for which the team members provided services comparable to the services contemplated in the project, with reference contact information, plus, a List of References. 

Demonstration of Experience in LEED-Certified and LEED-Equivalent Projects:

LEEDS-certified projects for which John Bryson & Partners are providing full structural engineering design and construction phase services include:

Atira Womens Resource Society Social Housing, 505 Abbott St, Vancouver. 12 storey LEED GOLD STANDARD-certified.

Lookout Emergency Aid Society Social Housing, 188 E 1st Avenue, Vancouver. 12 storey LEED GOLD STANDARD-certified.

Pender Place, 1409 W. Pender Street, Vancouver. 37 storey and 11 storey highrise development, LEED SILVER STANDARD-certified.

B.C. Paraplegic Association, 2304 W 8th Avenue & Vine St, Vancouver. 4 Storey woodframe multifamily special needs housing development. LEED GOLD STANDARD-certified. In design phase June 2009.

John Bryson & Partners has provided structural engineering services for a number of projects which have been designed to conform to LEED standards but which were not certified. 


The foregoing proposed fees are for normal basic structural engineering services as follows:"
