This is our fee proposal for structural engineering services for the above project. The project is described in Shape Properties’ Request For Proposal dated July 23, 2009 and MCMP’s request for a fee proposal. The project is based on the “full parkade option” and consists of:
522,562 sq.ft. gross retail area contained in 15 separate commercial pad shell buildings
Ground Level: Anchor retail tenant Building A is 153,662 sq. ft. 
(Fee proposal to include Landlord’s Tenant Improvements for Building A only.)
Podium Level: Balance of Pad Buildings - gross retail area of 279,900 sq.ft. podium CRUs 
Second Floor of Buildings A3, A4, C and I - total 89,000 sq.ft. 2nd floor CRU gross retail area
Parking: Ground level parking 1,126 stalls; Podium level parking 335 stalls
Total structural area estimated to be approximately 1,000,000 sq. ft. 

Construction is assumed to be structural steel for the pad buildings. This fee proposal assumes conventional strip and pad footings. 

Project to be phased:
Phase 1: Building A1 and podium, Buildings A2, A3, A4, A5, B, D, H, J
 Detailed Design to commence October 1, 2009
 Construction to commence for parkade April 10, 2010 or thereabouts
Phase 2: Buildings C, E, F, G1, G2, and I. 
 Detailed Design to commence June 15, 2011
 Construction to commence November 2011 or thereabouts.
Our proposed fixed fees for the structures of Phase 1 and Phase 2 are contained in the attached “Fee Summary and Breakdown” attached hereto. Please note that these fees include two complete designs of the base box structure for each of: (1) Cast-in-place concrete design, and (2) Precast concrete design.

The attached proposed fees are fees for complete structural engineering services for the project, including all structural engineering design, all structural engineering working drawings for construction purposes, and all inspections required by the building authority.

Breakdown of Fees:

Please find attached hereto our breakdown of fees, “Fee Summary & Breakdown”.

Additional Services: 

Please find attached hereto our List of Hourly Charge Out rates. 

Site Reviews

The cost of site reviews are included in the fixed fees quoted above. 

Although the project is located in Abbotsford, all site visits will be conducted by personnel located in our Vancouver office. 

Disbursements

All normal disbursements including normal plotting of other consultants drawings, printing, and courier costs, and travel costs to Abbotsford, are included not in the above proposed fees. 

Insurance Coverage

John Bryson & Partners carries the following insurance coverage:
Professional Liability Insurance: $1 million each claim and in aggregate annually.
Commercial General Liability Insurance: $3,000,000 limit .

Experience & Expertise of Structural Project Team and Individual Qualifications

