 Paladion, 777 Front Street, San Diego, California, 92101


Enclosed is our proposal for preparation of Probable Maximum Loss (PML) Report for the above noted project. 

This proposal is based on information shown on the following documents:

Structural Drawings of the original project (37 sheets) prepared by Albert G. Presk and approved for Building Permit on Sept 27, 1990
Structural Drawings for the Façade Replacement Shell (9 sheets) prepared by BMZ Structural Engineers approved for building plan check on November 13, 2018.
Architectural Drawings for the Façade Replacement Shell (40 sheets) prepared by Joseph Wong approved for building plan check on November 10, 2018.
Cladding Drawings for the Façade Replacement Shell (48 sheets) prepared by Mark Bird on November 7, 2018.
Mechanical Drawings (8 sheets) prepared by RB Consulting Engineers, Inc., provided by JWDA on Jan 31, 2019.

Proposed Fees

The fee for structural engineering services for the project is $12,000 as noted in the following Scope of Structural Services. 


Scope of Structural Services

BMZ US will perform a probable maximum loss (PML) evaluation for earthquake due diligence assessment in conformance with the scope and limitations of ASTM Guide E2026 and Practice E2557 for a Level 2 assessment of The Paladion building at 777 Front Street, San Diego, California.. 

Assumptions

We understand the existing base building structure is expected to remain unchanged. Upgrading of the base building lateral load resisting structure for seismic or wind loading is not being planned at this time. The building is currently under renovations which is be limited to replacement of the exterior wall assemblies and enclosure of some internal circulation corridors as well as interior design upgrades. 
Work Not Included in Scope of Services

Cost Estimating Services.
Normal disbursements, which include travel expenses, courier costs, plotting and printing, etc. We do not markup disbursements.
Government tax on professional fees.

I trust the foregoing proposal meets your expectations. I wish to thank you for consideration of Bryson Markulin Zickmantel Structural Engineers for this project, and we look forward to working with you.

Yours truly,

Bryson Markulin Zickmantel Structural Engineers





