INTRODUCTION

Bristol Square, San Diego, California
Date: September 29, 2026
To: Clark Lee
Bristol Square, 185 West F Street, San Diego, California – PML Report
We are pleased to submit our fee proposal for structural engineering services for the above-referenced project, based on the information provided in the email.
Regards,
Jim DesRoches, P.Eng., PE, Principal, Senior Structural Engineer














Project Description
This proposal is based on information shown on the following documents:
Structural Drawings of the original building prepared by Deardorf & Deardorf issued Feb 19,1988.
Architectural Drawings for Bristol Square by Austin Hansen Fehlman Group dated January 25, 1988.
Mechanical /Plumbing Drawings by West Coast Air stamped by Building Inspection Dept February 1, 1988.
Tier 1 – Seismic Assessment Report by BMZ Structural Engineers dated October 31, 2018.
Structural Assessment Update Letter by KOR Structural September 18, 2026
Seismic Risk Assessment Questions / Geotechnical Responses letter by Verdantas dated September, 18,2026
Proposed Fees
The fee for structural engineering services for the project is $15,000 as noted in the following Scope of Structural Services.
Scope of Structural Services
Kor Structural USA will perform a probable maximum loss (PML) evaluation for earthquake due diligence assessment in conformance with the scope and limitations of ASTM Guide E2026 and Practice E2557 for a Level 2 assessment of The Bristol Square building at 185 West F Street, San Diego, California.
Assumptions
We understand the existing base building structure is expected to remain unchanged. Upgrading of the base building lateral load resisting structure for seismic or wind loading is not being planned at this time.
Summary of Excluded Services
Cost Estimating Services.
Normal disbursements, which include travel expenses, courier costs, plotting and printing, etc. We do not markup disbursements.
Government tax on professional fees.

OUR COMPANY
The Firm
Headquartered in Vancouver, B.C., with satellite offices in Kelowna and Nanaimo, Kor Structural (""KOR"") provides structural engineering, consultation, design, and inspection services throughout British Columbia and across North America. We specialize in delivering efficient, creative, and buildable solutions for projects of all sizes and types, including residential, commercial, institutional, and light industrial structures. Our expertise spans all forms of concrete, structural steel, wood-frame, and masonry.
Our Services
At KOR, structural engineering is a harmonious blend of creative design and practical solutions, guided by rigorous discipline and adherence to engineering principles and codes. Our services include:
Design of high-rise reinforced concrete structures
Performance-based structural analysis and design
Analysis and design of unique, complex structural systems using materials such as reinforced concrete, structural steel, heavy timber, and masonry
Structural Assessments 
Structural Seismic upgrading 
Project Personnel and Experience
Project Manager:
Jim DesRoches, P.Eng., PE
A licensed professional engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, Ontario, and Washington, Jim brings over 30 years of experience in structural design and quality management, as well as more than 20 years’ experience designing, permitting, and directing construction of projects in Southern California. His collaborative and client-focused approach ensures creative solutions tailored to project needs.
