• 
Location: Toronto, ON 
• 
Start Date: June 2021 
• 
Completion Date: Oct. 2021 
• 
Contract Value: $4,322,617 
 
Project Description: The new iconic dual tower residential 
building in Downtown Toronto required a variety of design-build 
structural strengthening solutions resulting from unforeseen 
conditions. The six (6) level below-grade parking garage had 
numerous structural elements including: beams, columns, 
shear walls, footings, and slabs that required a variety of 
strengthening solutions. 
 
PULLMAN was engaged as a specialty contractor to undertake 
the structural strengthening work related to the critical portions 
of the project. 
 
The project involved the use of our innovative form-and-pump 
pressurized placement technique within a myriad of concrete 
enlargements. PULLMAN, in concert with STRUCTURAL 
TECHNOLOGIES, was able to work with consultant team to 
design-assist and design-build several solutions within the 
parking garage, including beam enlargements, 60+ column 
enlargements, temporary support of the tower crane, external 
post tensioning systems, CFRP and pre-stressing using hydraulic grout jacking. 
 
On-time completion of the structural strengthening work was critically important as the building was limited 
in terms of vertical construction at level 7 if our work was not complete. PULLMAN led a team of 30+ craft 
technicians working 12 hours per day, 7 days per week, for over 4 months to complete the project on-time. 
PULLMAN was able to meet and/or exceed every schedule milestone and completed the project without a 
single safety-related incident. 
