7f7413f3c8d9,01633-01,01633-01,Kerkhoff Construction Ltd.,Springfield & Ambrosi Kelowna L1 Slab,KOR,proposal,,,2023-02-21,projects,Projects\Projects\01 Small Jobs\01633-01 (1994 Springfield 1946 Ambrosi Rd Kelowna)\Documents from Kerkhoff\OneDrive_1_2-21-2023\641344 - PULLMAN Proposal 1994 Springfield_Rev01.pdf,,1,St. Joseph’s Hospital – Parking Garage,dispute,283,"1 St. Joseph’s Hospital – Parking Garage 
 
• 
Location: Hamilton, Ontario 
• 
Start Date: Sept. 2020 
• 
Completion Date: Dec. 2020 
• 
Contract Value: ~$250,000 (CAD) 
 
Project Description: The seven (7) – level exterior parking 
structure at St. Joseph’s Hamilton Healthcare (SJHH) James 
Street Campus was in a desperate state of repair. The parking 
garage was deemed unsafe in early 2019 by a consulting 
engineer performing a yearly
assessment. The 
structure was immediately closed to public use and emergency 
shoring installed. 
 
PULLMAN was engaged to complete a variety of structural 
strengthening work related to the critical portions of the project. 
 
The project involved the replacement and repair of numerous 
post-tensioning strands (singles, and pairs) in both the banded 
and uniform directions. Additionally, all 84 circular columns 
within the structure were strengthened using an external 
Carbon Fibre Reinforced Polymer (CFRP) fabric. 
 
PULLMAN, in concert with STRUCTURAL TECHNOLOGIES, 
was able to work with consultant team to propose value-
engineered solutions to a variety of complications on the project 
which amounts to $50,000+ in savings and weeks removed 
from the project schedule. 
 
On-time completion of the project was incredibly important to SJHH since the parking garage was 
completely closed. The downtown location of the parking structure forced all parking traffic to be diverted 
off-site with a shuttle service. By developing a very detailed project schedule, the team was able to leverage 
efficiencies and reduce risk for all parties. The project was completed on-time, below budget with zero 
safety-related incidents. 
