Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be John Zickmantel, M.Eng., P.Eng., 
Struct.Eng., PE, SE. John Zickmantel is a licensed Structural Engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, 
Manitoba, Nova Scotia, and Washington, with more than 30 years of consulting structural engineering 
design experience designing a wide variety of building types. John will scheme the entire structural 
system of all his projects, including the seismic force resisting system, and he is particularly skilled at 
finding structural solutions for complicated building arrangements that are both simple and efficient. In 
every project he also aims to balance the original design intent of the Architect, yet always taking into 
consideration the Client’s needs and desires. 
 
After the initial stages of design are complete, John Zickmantel will be assisted by Senior Structural 
Designer Conor Murtagh, B.A.Sc., P.L.Eng., who has more than 15 years of experience of working for 
firms in Ireland, Australia, and Canada and extensive knowledge of wood design systems and provides 
effective and innovative solutions, he is particularly skilled at finding structural solutions for complicated 
building arrangements that are both simple and efficient. In every project he also aims to balance the 
original design intent of the Architect, yet always taking into consideration the Client’s needs and desires. 
 
John Zickmantel and Conor Murtagh will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will 
include preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Both John Zickmantel 
and Conor Murtagh will be available and remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
Additional staff dedicated to this project will include: 
 
 Jason Stuart, Senior Structural Designer 
 Kate Reid, B.A.Sc., EIT 
 Simon Szarkiewicz, Senior Structural CAD Manager 
 Sadi Ghaffari, Structural CAD Technologist 
 Nelson Yu, Structural CAD Technologist 
 
For further information on key project personnel and an introduction to Kor Structural, please visit our 
website at www.korstructural.com. 
 
