Exclusions
The ﬁxed fee excludes any service not listed above, including: geotechnical engineering; architectural 
design; building code or zoning review; permit application services; cost estimating; contractor means, 
methods, techniques, sequences, or site safety; temporary works and shoring; shop drawing, truss, and 
engineered wood product supplier review; specialty component design; site visits; and ﬁeld reviews or 
construction-phase services of any kind. The Reviewer is not required to issue a Schedule B, Schedule S, or 
any other letter of assurance for the Project. 
Review Cycles
The ﬁxed fee includes one review and one back-check, being the re-check required before the Reviewer 
signs the “all issues resolved and re-checked” conﬁrmation on Appendix G. Further cycles are Additional 
Services at the rate below. 
Fee
Fixed fee of $1,000 plus GST for the scope above, invoiced on delivery of the Independent Review record 
and payable net ﬁfteen (15) days. Additional Services are billed hourly at $225/hr. Disbursements are billed 
at cost. 
Professional 
Responsibilities
Westwind remains the Engineer of Record and retains responsibility for the structural design. Mathieu 
Henry determines the disposition of each comment and signs the Professional of Record acknowledgement 
on Appendix G. 
Reviewer 
Declaration
- They are a professional registrant of Engineers and Geoscientists BC in good standing, practising under a 
valid Permit to Practice 
- They hold the experience and knowledge appropriate to a design check and Independent Review of a 
structure of this type 
- They have had no previous involvement in the structural design being reviewed 
Records
Both parties retain their records of the Independent Review for ten (10) years and will cooperate with any 
Engineers and Geoscientists BC audit or request relating to the Project. 
Insurance
The Reviewer maintains professional liability insurance for structural engineering services. Certiﬁcate 
available upon request. 
Acceptance of 
Proposal
This Engagement and the attached Terms of Engagement may be accepted by returning a signed copy, or by 
an email instruction to proceed that references and accepts them. 
