PURPOSE OF THIS REQUEST FOR PROPOSAL 
 
Urban West (the Development Manager) is requesting an Upset Maximum Fee proposal to perform the scope of 
work described in this RFP. 
 
I. 
CONFIDENTIALITY 
 
The information contained in this request is confidential. 
 
II. 
SUMMARY SCOPE OF WORK 
 
The subject site consists of Legal Lots 1-6 of Block 2, Plan 2169. The assembled properties are located on East 
Boulevard between 47th and 48th Avenue and are currently improved with four, low-rise residential, rental buildings. 
The site slopes gradually from North to South. 
 
East and West Boulevard are separated by the Arbutus Greenway. A four-story mixed-use development is nearing 
completion at 49th & West Boulevard; similar C-2 zoned developments are proceeding to the North of the subject 
site on both East and West Boulevard. Neighboring properties to the East are primarily detached, single-family 
homes. 
 
The new building will include 1.5 levels of below grade parking with 15,000 sf of retail and 3 residential units at 
street level. The 3 floors above will have an additional 42 residential units with a total combined FSR of 2.5. An 
elegant and classic design will complement the urban context in the Kerrisdale community and provide new and 
modern homes. Ground landscaping along East Boulevard will further enhance the pedestrian experience and 
complement the neighboring greenway. 
 
The scope of services and design information requirements are outlined below. The Scope of Work shall 
contain the following key elements: Schematic Design, Design Development, Construction Documents, 
Bidding and Construction Administration. Consultation and coordination with other consultants is expected to 
minimize changes and drawing coordination errors and omissions. 
 
The consultant will prepare documents for coordination and review for Schematic Design, 50% and 100% 
Design Development, 50% Construction Documents, 80% Building Permit Set and 100% Final Construction 
Documents. The consultant will confirm cost estimates at the completion of each phase and at each of the 
milestone submissions during the construction document phase, based on the drawings and specifications 
and pricing provided by the cost consultant and/or pre-construction contractor. In the event that the estimate 
exceeds the budget, the consultant shall be responsible to redesign the work within the original fee until it is 
within the budget. The consultant is expected to interact and coordinate ""seamlessly"" with the Development 
Team, Pre-Construction Contractor, Construction Manager, Cost Consultant, and all other consultants to 
provide coordination and assistance as may be required of their discipline. 
 
General design scope to include but not limited to the following: 
 
1) 
Meet with development team and jurisdictional authorities as required. 
2) 
At the conclusion of each phase, participate in multi-consultant drawing exchange and quality 
control review. 
3) 
Participate in developing and updating the project schedule. 
4) 
Assist as required in cost analysis during all phases and provide ""alternate"" solutions, suggestions 
and material quantities as may be required. 
5) 
Provide in each phase an on-going written list of information required of the other consultants and 
the Developer. 
Request for Proposal: 6310-6386 East Blvd 

6) 
Review and respond to comments provided by jurisdictional agencies as a result of permit applications. 
7) 
Provide written interpretations, clarifications, addenda and change orders (to be issued by others) as 
required during the Construction Administration phase. 
8) 
Observe the quality and progress of the work and its conformance with the contract documents 
during the construction phase of the work, attend bi-monthly construction coordination meetings and 
provide written field observation reports as a result of each site visit. 
9) 
Provide as-designed documentation as may be required per Building Department requirement or 
request."
