The Consultant should not proceed from phase to phase unless directed by the Developer. 
 
 
III. 
SPECIFIC SCOPE BY PHASE 
 
Phase 1 
Schematic / Preliminary Design 
 
This phase is an exploratory stage wherein alternatives and options are studied and compiled for presentation 
and review. Several alternatives should be developed for the items contained in each task for analysis, 
comment, and direction prior to moving into the next phase. The options should be developed in keeping with 
the budget parameters and presented in enough detail as to develop clear understanding of the design's intent 
and outcome. 
 
 Based on the drawings provided by email along with this RFP: 
 
a.) Review the plans and provide preliminary structural input to enable further architectural design 
development. 
 
c.) Review the Development Calendar indicating milestones and obligatory commitment dates to complete 
the Development Process 
 
Phase 2 
Design Development 
 
Based on the approved Schematic Design, the Consultant shall commence Design Development to further refine 
the scope and nature of the project. Design should now be studied more completely towards presentation and 
approval in its final state. The budgetary impacts of each design should be sharpened along with the details 
and technical interface associated with a design's final development. Final design selection will take place in 
this phase. Detailed coordination of design between the Architect, other Consultants and the Developer shall 
continue along with development of preliminary fabrication details and layout. A detailed budget will be required. 
 
a.) Prepare an outline specification for Design Development. 
b.) Work with Developer, Cost Consultant and Contractor on an on-going basis to identify, document (for 
current or future consideration) and incorporate value engineering. 
c.) Consult with the Architect in preparing Development Permit drawings based on Phase 1 approval. 
d.) Meet with necessary authorities as required for DP Approval. 
e.) Coordinate Development Calendar with Development Manager. 
f.) When final Developer approval is reached on each item, it will move into the Contract Document 
Phase. 
 
 

Phase 3 
Construction Documents. 
 
a.) Based on the approved Design Development documents, the Consultant shall commence 
Construction Documents to fully illustrate the project. 
b.) Prepare an outline specification. 
c.) Consultant is responsible for producing all documentation necessary to effectively bid, fabricate, and 
install the project. To assure a fully integrated design, coordination between the Development 
Manager, Architect and other Consultants shall continue throughout this phase. 
d.) Prepare Construction Documents and Specifications for Building Permit Submission and issuance. 
e.) Assist the Architect, Development Manager and Pre-Con Consultant in material and product selection 
and proposed cost savings. 
f.) Participate in Ready Check meetings. 
g.) Issue drawings for Pricing and Issued for Construction. 
h.) Update Development Calendar 
i.) At completion of this phase, the consultant shall prepare a final cost estimate. Design must meet 
budget guidelines. 
 
Phase 4 
Construction Administration 
 
a.) Visit the site during the progress of construction in order to observe the quality and progress of the work 
and its conformance with the contract documents, attending bi-monthly construction coordination 
meetings, and provide written field observation reports as a result of each site visit. 
b.) Review and approve shop drawings, samples, revisions, and substitutions. 
c.) Consult with contractor/fabricator or other consultants for clarification of documents. 
d.) Provide written interpretations, clarifications, addenda and change orders as required during the bid 
period and Construction Administration phase. 
e.) Provide responses to RFIs within 5 days or sooner as required for critical path. 
f.) Review progress of the work to ensure proper installation/fabrication. 
g.) Prepare punch lists. 
h.) Review requests for information, and any applicable change order requirements. 
l.) 
Meet with Jurisdictional Authorities as necessary to resolve open issues as they affect progress. 
 
Provide a proposed schedule based on this information, along with a cost breakdown for each of the 
Phases. 
 
IV. PROJECT CONTACT 
 
All questions or clarifications are to be e-mailed to the Development Manager, Larry Kerr at Urban West; 
l.kerr@urbanwestprojects.com 
