Dear Sir: 

Re: Fee Proposal for Structural Engineering Services
 Presidia, 520 Cottonwood Avenue, Coquitlam, B.C.

This is our fee proposal for structural engineering services for the above project. The project is shown on IBI Group’s preliminary architectural drawings dated November 15, 2017, included with your Request for a Proposal dated November 15, 2017, and comprises the following:

One 28-storey concrete residential high-rise tower with a six-level rental podium structure, built on a gently sloping site.
The project includes approximately 83 rental residential units in the six-level podium and approximately 162 market residential units in the tower above.
The total gross buildable area is estimated to be 214,902 sq.ft.
Built over roughly four levels of below grade parking structure for approximately 303 vehicles.

Project Personnel

The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be John Zickmantel. John Zickmantel will participate heavily in the preliminary stages of the work, which will include preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. After the initial stages of design are complete, John will be assisted by Mark S. Bakhtavar, M.A.Sc., P.Eng., Rory Beirne, M.Eng., P.Eng., and Jeremy Atkinson, M.A.Sc., EIT; however, John Zickmantel will remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. Additional staff dedicated to this project will include Simon Szarkiewicz, CAD technologist; and Kyle Frank, production manager. All personnel listed have extensive experience with similar projects.

For further information on key project personnel and an introduction to Bryson Markulin Zickmantel Structural Engineers, please visit our website at www.bmzse.com.

Proposed Fees

The following fees are fees for complete structural engineering services for the project, including all structural engineering design, all structural engineering working drawings for construction purposes, review of applicable shop drawings, all inspections required by the building authority, and, if required, Professional Letters Assurance (Schedules B and C-B) as per the 2012 BC Building Code to the City of Coquitlam in support of the Building Permit application and project completion. Over and above the following fixed proposed fees, we recommend a budget of a maximum of $1,000.00 for normal disbursements (e.g. courier costs), not including printing and plotting.

The proposed fixed fees for our services, provided all structural drawings are done in AutoCAD, are as follows:


We propose an additional $15,000.00 to produce structural drawings in Revit, if required.

All preliminary work and preliminary consultations with the Architect will be charged on an hourly basis in accordance with the attached list of hourly charge out rates, however, please note that all charges for preliminary work are included in the above fixed fees.

Please note, we propose to charge for any additional services outside the original scope of work on an hourly rates basis in addition to the above fixed fees.

The foregoing proposed fees are for normal basic structural engineering services as follows:

Engineering Design, Drafting of Working Drawings and Specifications 
 
All structural engineering design and specifications and working drawings for all structural elements of the project.

Attendance at design meetings as required by the Architect and/or Client.

Shop Drawing Review and Construction Inspections

Site visits by qualified personnel, with such frequency as is necessary to observe the various stages of structural work, and to ascertain that it is being done in general conformance with the structural drawings and Code requirements. 

Review of structural shop drawings. 

Review of testing reports from testing and inspection agencies to determine compliance with the structural drawings and Code requirements.

Responding to Request for Information (RFI) and issuing structural site instructions and details to Contractor during construction.

Please note that the inspection services outlined above does not make us guarantors of the contractor's work. The contractor will remain responsible for safety in and about the jobsite, and for the adequacy of any construction equipment, scaffold, shoring, form, or other work aid used by him.

Please note that we carry sufficient professional liability insurance.

Summary of Typical Services and Exclusions

Our services would not include any of the following:

Subsurface soil investigation and report, and inspection of the geotechnical aspects of foundation construction; sampling, testing and reporting on materials used in construction; and retaining specialist consultants such as geotechnical engineers and testing engineers.
Design and construction review of concrete formwork and design changes to accommodate temporary construction conditions.

Design and supervision of excavation shoring and underpinning of adjacent buildings.

Design and supervision of nonstructural components. Normal current practice is that nonstructural components are designed and certified by subtrades' engineers. For example, exterior windows are commonly designed and certified by the window subcontractor's professional engineer. Please note that we will provide the architect with all necessary advice and specification requirements for such items as he may request.

Normal disbursements, which include courier costs, plotting of other consultants’ drawings, and printing, etc. We do not markup disbursements.

Government tax on professional fees.

We propose to invoice on a monthly basis. It is our policy to state that we reserve the right to discontinue our work if the client fails to meet his commitments, and we will not be responsible for any damages arising therefrom.

I trust the foregoing proposal meets your expectations. I wish to thank you for consideration of Bryson Markulin Zickmantel Structural Engineers for this project, and look forward to working with both you and IBI Group again.

Yours truly,

Bryson Markulin Zickmantel Structural Engineers




John Zickmantel, M.Eng., P.Eng., Struct.Eng., P.E., S.E. 




