Regarding: 
Plan Check Services for 220 W. Broadway, San Diego, California 
 
Structural Engineering Fee Proposal 
 
 
Dear Mr. DesRoches: 
 
Englekirk is pleased to submit this proposal to provide plan check services for the above referenced project. 
It is our understanding that our services will be contracted through Holland Partners (SDCC South Block 
LLC) but we will be under the direction of the City of San Diego Department of Building and Safety. 
 
The proposed project consists of an approximately 420 ft. tall, 37-story residential tower with five levels of 
subterranean construction. The lower nine levels of the tower are configured with a larger floor plate than 
the typical tower level and is considered the podium. The building’s seismic force resisting system consists 
of reinforced concrete shear walls and, due to its height, an alternative design procedure will be utilized. It 
is proposed to base the design using a seismic response modification factor, R, of 6. Project-specific 
seismic design criteria have been developed for this project as summarized in a January 16, 2020 report 
from the structural engineer of record and approved on January 22, 2020 by the Peer Review Committee 
(PRC) formed by the City of San Diego. These criteria, in addition to the 2016 California Building Code, will 
form the basis of the plan check 
 
BMZ Structural Engineers is the structural engineer of record. Naeem Nemati-Raad is the assigned City 
proxy reviewer on this project. We have been asked to copy Mr. Nemati-Raad and Mr. Ali Fattah on all 
correspondence related to the plan check. Cecilia Ponce is the assigned Development Project Manager 
and will coordinate permit processing and will be the point of contact when sending hard copies of the 
approved plans and the other documents relied on in the review for permit issuance. 
 
The structural engineer has requested that the review of the seismic force resisting system by the PRC and 
the structural plan check run concurrently. It is understood that the normal four- to six-week time frame for 
the structural plan check may be lengthened by this approach due to revisions to the structural plans to 
address comments from the PRC or as a result of plan check comments. We have attempted to account 
for the iterative nature of the plan check due to this approach in our fee. We have also included an allowance 
in our fee for communication with the PRC. 
 
Prior to initiating the plan check we will require a complete set of the structural drawings and calculations 
as well as the architectural and MEP drawings for anchorage review. A copy of the final geotechnical report 
will also be required. 
 
 
