CONSULTANT'S BASIC SERVICES 
A. 
Consultant shall furnish Services to Company as described in Exhibit A, ""Services"" attached and made a part hereof. 
B. 
Consultant agrees to render the Services in a proper, timely, competent, and efficient manner in accordance with that degree of 
care and skill ordinarily exercised by members of the same profession currently practicing under similar circumstances using only 
qualified personnel. Consultant understands and agrees that time is of the essence with respect to Consultant’s obligation to 
provide the Services in accordance with the agreed upon schedule between Company and Consultant. Subject to Section II.A. 
below, Consultant shall devote as much of Consultant’s productive time, attention, knowledge and skill to the Services provided 
as may be necessary to competently discharge Consultant’s duties hereunder. 
C. 
Consultant understands and agrees that Company has entered into this Agreement in reliance on the skills, experience, and 
qualifications of the following personnel: Jim DesRoches (“Key Personnel”). Consultant agrees that the Key Personnel shall be 
and remain primarily responsible for rendering the Services. If any of the Key Personnel should no longer be employed by the 
Consultant and/or are unable to work on the Project for any other reason, Consultant must notify Company of the same. In 
addition to any other basis for termination, should two or more of the Key Personnel no longer be available to work on the Project, 
the Company will have the right to terminate this Agreement in accordance with Section IX below. Company shall reserve the 
right to compel Consultant to replace Key Personnel if Company is not in any way satisfied with any such person. 
D. 
Consultant shall meet with Company from time to time as requested by Company to discuss the progress of the Services 
rendered to date and to ensure that Company is satisfied with the scope and quality of the Services. Company may have a 
representative present at any meeting of Consultant concerning the Project. 
E. 
Consultant shall not engage the services of any other consultant, person, or entity in connection with the Services to be provided 
to the Company by Consultant without prior written consent of Company."
