IX. 
TERMINATION OF AGREEMENT 
A. 
If Consultant commits any of the acts specified in this paragraph, Company may, by giving two days written notice to Consultant, 
without prejudice to any other rights or remedies given Company by law or by this Agreement, terminate the Services of 
Consultant under this Agreement. Upon termination, the Company may take possession of all materials, including Instruments of 
Service, and may complete the Scope of Work by whatever method Company may deem expedient. To the extent the Company 
reasonably estimates that completing the Scope of Work may cost more than it would have cost for Consultant to complete the 
work, the Company may, in addition to any other rights and remedies available under the Agreement, withhold the estimated 
additional costs from any amounts otherwise due to the Consultant. Subject to the foregoing, the Consultant shall be paid in full 
for service rendered up to the date of termination in accordance with Exhibit B. In no event will Consultant be paid for services 
not rendered as of the date of termination, including without limitation any anticipated or potential profits. 
