EXHIBIT A 
SERVICES 
 
I. 
General Requirements 
Throughout the course of the Consultant's services under this Agreement, the Consultant shall: 
A. 
Keep the Company informed of its services by submitting to the Company, at appropriate intervals as established by the 
Company, oral or written reports and progress drawings which appropriately monitor the progress of the Consultants services 
and the work. 
B. 
Attend meetings as required by the Company relative to the design and construction of the Project. 
C. 
Coordinate its services hereunder with the other consultants, if any, including those engaged by the Consultant or those 
separately engaged by the Company. This shall include, however shall not be limited to, meetings, conference calls, 
correspondence, and transmitting various information. 
D. 
The Consultant shall review and evaluate the information provided by the Company and advise the Company of any 
additional information required by the Consultant for completion of the Project. 
E. 
The Consultant shall investigate existing conditions or existing facilities at the Project. 
F. 
The Consultant shall review and approve or take other appropriate action upon Contractor’s submittals such as Shop 
Drawings, Product Data, and samples for the purpose of checking conformance and design concept as expressed in the 
contract documents. The Consultant’s action shall be taken with promptness as to cause no delay in the work or in the 
construction of the Company or separate contractors. 
G. 
 Duties, responsibilities and limitations of authority of the Consultant under this Section shall not be restricted, modified or 
extended without written agreement of the Company and Consultant with consent of the Contractor. 
H. 
The Consultant shall advise and consult with the Company during the administration of the Contract for Construction. 
I. 
The Consultant shall visit the site at intervals appropriate to the stage of the Contractor's operations, or as otherwise agreed 
by the Company and the Consultant 
J. 
The Consultant shall report to the Company known deviations from the Contract Documents and from the most recent 
construction schedule submitted by the Contractor. However, the Consultant shall not be responsible for the Contractor's 
failure to perform the Work in accordance with the requirements of the Contract Documents. The Consultant shall be 
responsible for the Consultant's negligent acts or omissions, but shall not have control over or charge of and shall not be 
responsible for acts or omissions of the Contractor, or its agents or employees, or of any other persons or entities performing 
portions of the Work. 
K. 
Consultant agrees to comply with all policies, procedures and directives issued by the Company with respect to the subject 
matter of this Agreement. 
II. 
Scope of Work 
Scope of work shall include, but is not limited to: 
 
 
Our basic scope of services will be provided as described in the following stages of the project development:"
6d316d0c63c9-844cf9,30921-01,30921-01,J16SD LLC,The Fellow J16 Lofts San Diego,client,draft,5/5,yes,2020-08-19,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30921-01 (J16 Lofts, San Diego)\Newforma\email\2020-01\2020-01-02-2201-49-R5WC jdesroches@b m9v RE- Contract.msg",J16SD Inc. contract BMZ marked up 2019-12-16.pdf,3,Construction Document Phase:,permits_approvals|dispute,134,"3 Construction Document Phase: 
 
a. Finalize the preparation of the following documentation: 
i. 
Structural Drawings. 
ii. 
Structural Specifications. 
iii. 
Structural Calculations. 
iv. 
Typical and custom details. 
b. Coordinate documents with Client and other affected disciplines. 
c. Attendance at design meetings as required by the Architect and/or Owner. 
d. Incorporate the recommendations of any specialist consultants if required. 
e. Assist in obtaining structural permitting approvals from the local approving authority or government agency having 
jurisdiction. 
f. Respond to plan check comments and make revisions to structural construction documents as required by the local authority 
or government agency. 
g. Assist in establishing testing and inspection requirements for concrete and other materials to be carried out by the Owner or 
by its representatives. 
h. Provide structural addenda or clarifications during Owner bidding or negotiating with construction contractors."
