Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be John Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng., Struct.Eng. 
John Markulin is a licensed structural engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, California, Washington, 
Arizona, and Texas, with more than 28 years of experience designing a wide variety of buildings, including 
tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, and 
institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, and office 
buildings. 
 
John Markulin will participate heavily in the preliminary stages of the work, which will include preliminary 
design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. He will be assisted and backed up directly 
by Rory Beirne, M.Eng., P.Eng., who has more than 11 years of consulting structural engineering design 
experience; however, John Markulin will remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
Additional staff dedicated to this project will include Jeremy Atkinson, M.A.Sc., P.Eng.; Simon Szarkiewicz, 
Senior CAD Technologist; Griffin Dow, Junior Engineer; Helena Trajic, B.A.Sc., EIT; and Kyle Frank, Senior 
Production Manager. All personnel listed have extensive experience with similar projects. 
 
All design and drafting for the project will be done in Vancouver. Routine aspects of the construction of the 
structure will be inspected by our Victoria partner, Stefan Alexander, P.Eng., LEED AP BD+C, GSC, a 
structural engineer of SR Alexander Engineering Ltd., with whom we have been working with for the past 
several years; however, critical aspects of the structural work will be inspected from Vancouver on an as 
needed basis. 
 
Following this proposal is an illustrated sample of some of our most recent projects. For further information 
on key project personnel and an introduction to Bryson Markulin Zickmantel Structural Engineers, please 
visit our website at www.bmzse.com. 
 
Experience within the City of Victoria 
 
We also have extensive experience with residential and commercial projects in and around Victoria, B.C., 
and the following is a sample of projects we have recently completed, or are currently under construction: 
 
HUDSON WALK (Phase 2), 785 Caledonia Avenue, Victoria B.C. with Townline Group of Companies and 
Rafii Architects. This project comprises a 16-storey mixed-use commercial and residential tower built with 
some commercial/retail space at grade level, and residential space above, all built over two levels of below 
grade parking. The total gross buildable area is estimated to be 81,556 sq.ft. Currently in the design phase. 
 
HUDSON PLACE (Phase 1 & 2), Blanshard Street & Herald Street, Victoria, B.C. with Townline Group of 
Companies and Rafii Architects. This project comprises two phases as follows: 
 
o 
Phase 1: One 28-storey concrete mixed-use commercial and residential tower with some 
commercial/retail space at grade level and 167 residential units above, all built over five levels of 
below grade parking structure. The total gross buildable area is estimated to be 198,638 sq.ft. This 
tower is tallest building currently planned for downtown Victoria. 
 
o 
Phase 2: One 10-storey concrete mixed-use commercial and office building with an estimated gross 
buildable area of 164,000 sq.ft., all built over five levels of below grade parking structure. 
 
1002-1008, 1012 Pandora Avenue, Victoria, B.C. with BlueSky Properties and Chris Dikeakos Architects. 
This project comprised one five-storey wood-frame building and one three-storey wood-frame building all 
over a shared two-level concrete commercial building with two levels of below grade parking. The total 
gross buildable area is 200,144 sq.ft. 

