Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be Jim DesRoches, P.E. The Engineer of 
Record for this project will be John A. Markulin, P.E., S.E. John Markulin is a licensed structural engineer 
in California, Washington, and Arizona, with more than 28 years of experience designing a wide variety of 
buildings, including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, 
and institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, and office 
buildings. Jim DesRoches is a licensed professional engineer in Washington State and Nevada and has 
more than 30 years of experience designing similar buildings, as well as 20 years of experience designing, 
permitting, and directing construction of projects in Southern California. Please refer to the attached 
resumes following this document for further background information on John Markulin and Jim DesRoches. 
 
Jim DesRoches and John Markulin will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will include 
preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Additional staff dedicated to 
this project will include Michael Li, Senior Revit Technologist; and Kyle Frank, Senior Production Manager. 
All personnel listed have extensive experience with similar projects. 
 
Established in 1998, BMZ provides structural engineering, consultation, design, and inspection services 
throughout across Canada, the Western United States, Mexico, and Asia. Our portfolio includes: low-rise 
to high-rise residential (as tall as 63-storeys); large mixed-use projects; commercial/retail buildings; office 
buildings; light industrial warehouses; institutional and public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, 
and extended care facilities; and seismic upgrading, addition, and renovation projects 
 
Following this proposal is an illustrated sample of some of our most recent projects. For further information 
on key project personnel and an introduction to Bryson Markulin Zickmantel Structural Engineers, please 
visit our website at www.bmzse.com. 
 
