This CONSULTING SERVICES AGREEMENT (this ""Agreement"") is made and 
entered into as of the __ day of May 2020, by John W. Wallace, Inc. (""Consultant"") and CA 
Residential 800 Broadway, LLC (""Owner"") 
 
RECITALS 
 
WHEREAS, the Owner wishes to retain the Consultant to perform certain services 
pertaining to the construction of 800 Broadway (the ""Project"") on the real property located at 
800 Broadway, San Diego, CA 92101 (the “Project Site”); 
 
WHEREAS, the Consultant wishes to perform for the Owner those certain services 
described in Exhibit A attached hereto and in accordance with the terms and conditions set 
forth in this Agreement; and 
 
 
WHEREAS, each party represents that it is ready, willing and able to undertake the 
duties, responsibilities and obligations set forth in this Agreement. 
 
 
NOW THEREFORE, in consideration of the terms and covenants contained herein, 
and other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby 
acknowledged, the parties agree as follows: 
 
AGREEMENT 
 
I. 
Incorporation of Preambles. 
 
The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated by reference as if set forth fully herein. 
 
II. 
Services To Be Performed. 
 
 
A. 
The services to be performed by the Consultant (the ""Services"") are set forth in 
Exhibit A, attached hereto and made a part hereof (the ""Scope of Services""). It is understood 
and agreed that Exhibit A is intended only as a description of the Scope of Services to be 
performed by the Consultant under this Agreement and, therefore, to the extent that Exhibit A 
consists of terms and conditions that do not define the Scope of Services to be provided by the 
Consultant under this Agreement (e.g., payment terms, limitations of liability, dispute 
resolution, client obligations, etc.), such terms and conditions are not to be deemed a part of 
this Agreement and shall be of no force or effect. Further, to the extent that Exhibit A consists 
of terms and conditions that conflict with the terms and conditions contained in the remainder 
of this Agreement, the terms and conditions contained in the remainder of this Agreement 
shall govern and control. 
 
 
B. 
Owner-Provided Information. 
 
(1) 
The Owner shall provide full information about the objectives, 
schedule, constraints and existing conditions of the Project, and shall establish"
