B. 
Partial Payment. The Consultant shall submit monthly invoices to the Owner 
for Services performed in accordance with this Agreement. Said invoices shall be 
accompanied by the following: 
 
(1) 
the Consultant's lien waiver for work performed to date accompanied by 
the Consultant's sworn statement setting forth in detail all subcontractors and 
material suppliers with whom the Consultant has contracted, their addresses, 
work or materials to be furnished, amounts of the contracts, amounts paid to 
date, amounts of current payments and balances due; 
 
(2) 
lien waivers to date from all subconsultants who performed any portion 
of the Services for which payment is requested. 
 
Payment of the undisputed portion of the Consultant’s invoice shall be made no later than 
thirty (30) days after the Owner’s receipt of such invoice. 
 
 
C. 
Final Payment. Upon completion of all Services hereunder, the Consultant 
shall submit its request for final payment which shall be accompanied by the Consultant's 
final lien waiver and all subconsultants' final lien waivers not previously provided to the 
Owner. Final Payment shall be due within thirty (30) days after Owner’s receipt of 
Consultant’s invoice. In the event that the Owner reasonably and timely determines the 
Services are not fully and finally complete, the Owner shall pay the Consultant such portion 
of the final invoice that may be due for Services performed. The remaining amount of such 
invoice shall be payable upon the Owner’s reasonable determination that the Services are 
fully and finally complete. 
 
 
 
Reasonable documentation will be provided by the Consultant in connection 
with each such invoice. The Owner may require such additional supporting information and 
documentation as the Owner reasonably deems necessary or desirable. Payment shall be 
made after the Owner's receipt of an invoice and all necessary supporting information and 
documentation. No payment shall be due and/or payable by the Owner hereunder unless and 
until the Consultant complies with the provisions of this Section IV. Payment shall not 
become due and payable to the Consultant until forty-five (45) days after the date of the 
Owner's receipt of the invoice and all other documents required by this Section IV. 
Notwithstanding the foregoing, if the Owner contests all or any portion of such invoice, 
Owner shall be required to pay only the portion of such invoice not contested by Owner. Any 
contested portion of such invoice shall not be payable by the Owner until any disagreement 
between the Owner and the Consultant with respect thereto is resolved and a revised invoice 
is submitted to the Owner by the Consultant reflecting the appropriate adjustments agreed to 
by the parties. 
 
 
The Consultant will keep and make available for the inspection, examination 
