F. 
WAIVER OF RIGHTS UNDER PROMPT PAYMENT STATUTE 
TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE CONSULTANT AGREES 
THAT THE TERMS OF THIS AGREEMENT SHALL GOVERN AND CONTROL THE 
RIGHTS AND OBLIGATIONS OF THE PARTIES WITH RESPECT TO PAYMENT AND, 
THEREFORE, THE CONSULTANT HEREBY WAIVES ANY AND ALL RIGHTS AND 
PROTECTIONS AFFORDED BY THE PROVISIONS OF ANY APPLICABLE PROMPT 
PAYMENT ACT TO THE EXTENT INCONSISTENT WITH THE REQUIREMENTS 
FOR PAYMENT HEREUNDER. 
 
V. 
Termination. 
 
 
A. 
The Owner may terminate this Agreement at any time without cause and 
without prior notice to the Consultant and in such event the Owner will pay the Consultant for 
payments owed the Consultant under the Agreement, less the aggregate of previous payments, 
allocable to the Consultant's Services completed as of the date of termination. The Owner 
will not be responsible for reimbursing the Consultant for any continuing contractual 
commitment to Subcontractors or penalties or damages for canceling such contractual 
commitments inasmuch as the Consultant shall make all subcontracts and other commitments 
subject to this provision. In the event of termination by the Owner, the Owner may require 
