The proposed project schedule of roughly 6 to 8 month is mentioned in the email from Ali Fattah. 
An approximately 9-month review schedule is reasonable. Meeting the proposed project will 
depend on a number of items, such as the completeness and organization of submittals, 
the significance of the issues that arise during the review, and responsiveness of the 
design team to the SD-PRC comments. Based on prior experiences on peer review 
projects in other jurisdictions and with the SEOR, a project duration of 9 to 12 months 
proposed schedule is reasonable. However, it is noted that the overall schedule may 
increase if there are project delays that are beyond the control of the PRC."
abeaa079958e,30940-01,30940-01,JWDA Inc.,800 Broadway San Diego CA,KOR,proposal,,,2020-05-07,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30940-01 (800 Broadway, San Diego, CA)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Peer Review Panel\San_Diego_800_Broadway_BMZ_WallaceProposal_May_07_2020.pdf",,3,4. PURPOSE OF THE REVIEW,permits_approvals,135,"3 4. PURPOSE OF THE REVIEW 
The purpose of our review is to verify, to an extent consistent with our scope, that the structural 
design of the building is expected to provide an overall level of seismic performance at least 
equivalent to that expected for a building meeting prescriptive requirements of the governing 
building code for seismic structural design. Our professional opinion on this issue will be described 
in a findings letter to you at the completion of our review. 
The focus of our review is on the SEOR's seismic design criteria and key assumptions, and spot 
checks of submitted calculations and drawings to determine how the design criteria are applied. 
We will prepare a log, which we will regularly update, in which we will record our SPRP comments 
and the responses of the SEOR."
abeaa079958e,30940-01,30940-01,JWDA Inc.,800 Broadway San Diego CA,KOR,proposal,,,2020-05-07,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30940-01 (800 Broadway, San Diego, CA)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Peer Review Panel\San_Diego_800_Broadway_BMZ_WallaceProposal_May_07_2020.pdf",,5,5. SCOPE OF SERVICES,permits_approvals,346,"5. SCOPE OF SERVICES 
The initial review is to be performed at the beginning of the project when project-specific seismic 
design criteria are developed, and further reviews will be conducted for the SEOR’s submittal of 
the Basis of Design, the Service-Level Evaluation (SLE), the Maximum Considered Earthquake 
evaluation (MCE), and permit set of drawings. The overall scope of services related to structural 
engineering generally includes the following tasks: 
a) Review initial project-specific seismic design criteria. 
b) Review initial elastic analysis results and schematic design drawings. 
c) Review of key issues, which may include the following: 
i. 
Interaction of the core wall with supplemental shear walls, if they exist, and the 
gravity system, 
ii. 
Plan torsion of the tower, 
iii. 
Evaluation of podium and the below-grade structure, 
iv. 
Evaluation of transfer diaphragm(s) and the impact of diaphragm flexibility on the 
foundation and diaphragm design, 
v. 
Design and detailing of the lateral-force resisting elements of the building, 
including any supplemental systems, 
d) Review the nonlinear response history analysis input and output for project-specific 
seismic design issues, including use of available test data and research findings 
published in available research reports, papers, and communications that are used as a 
basis for developing the computer model and interpreting the computer results. 
e) Conduct independent verification calculations as needed to spot check the acceptability 
of the design. 
f) Review of permit drawing sets for all permits (if phased). 
g) Prepare written list of comments and be available for questions arising from the City or 
design team regarding comments, throughout plan review process. 
h) Attend meetings in Los Angeles, as needed, and participate in conference calls. 
i) Provide written report to the City including a findings letter describing the Panel’s 
recommendations to the City, and final comment log. 
 
As the academic member of the SD-PRC, my scope of work is to focus on issues related to the 
above overall tasks related to: 
 
a) Evaluate assumptions and acceptance criteria for linear and non-linear elements in the 
structural system for the three-dimensional model used for assessing building 
behavior/performance for the given hazard levels considered,"
