221673662904-be9bfe,30940-01,30940-01,JWDA Inc.,800 Broadway San Diego CA,KOR,proposal,,,2020-03-04,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30940-01 (800 Broadway, San Diego, CA)\Newforma\email\2020-03\2020-03-04-1852-13-ZEVS Jon.Barratt@ tl3 RWDI Proposal - 80.msg",200304 RWDI Proposal 2002869 800 Broadway San Diego.pdf,10p4,Structural wind loading services provide predictions of the wind-induced  ,dispute,350,"Structural wind loading services provide predictions of the wind-induced 
structural responses for design for strength and occupant comfort. 
WIND TUNNEL MODELING
Wind tunnel testing is the most accurate means of predicting project-specific wind loads and responses, including wind-
induced motions. A scale replica of the project and the immediate surroundings will be tested in a wind tunnel which 
simulates wind speeds and turbulence levels appropriate for the site. 
Scale Model Construction & Wind Tunnel Testing
A scale model of the project site will be constructed, and one of two 
well-established rigid model techniques will be used to predict the 
peak responses. While both techniques are generally equivalent, 
RWDI will select the approach based on the needs of the project: 
High Freqency Force Balance (HFFB): The building is mounted on 
a balance capable of measuring base bending moments, shears 
and torsion from which modal forces can be calculated. This 
technique tends to be faster, but it is also better suited to 
situations with details such as balconies, screens or trellises. It is 
also well suited to shaping workshops. 
High Frequency Pressure Integration (HFPI): Taps, which measure wind pressure, will be installed on the surface of 
the model. Instantaneous pressures over the building surface will be integrated to form the base bending moments, 
shears, torsion along with the modal forces. This approach is best suited to simple façades but it also allows more 
flexibility to deal with peak loading on portions of complex structures as well as inclusion of higher order modes. 

Analysis & Deliverables
The test data will be analysed with the building’s structural 
properties (i.e., dynamic mass, stiffness and damping) and 
the wind climate model to determine the peak responses of 
the structure as a function of return period. Wind force 
and torque distributions will be provided along with 
appropriate combinations of sway and torsion for the 
design return period(s) of interest. The accelerations at the 
top occupied floor will also be predicted and compared to 
motion criteria for human comfort. Parametric runs will 
also be included to gauge the sensitivity of the responses to 
changes in key structural parameters."
221673662904-be9bfe,30940-01,30940-01,JWDA Inc.,800 Broadway San Diego CA,KOR,proposal,,,2020-03-04,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30940-01 (800 Broadway, San Diego, CA)\Newforma\email\2020-03\2020-03-04-1852-13-ZEVS Jon.Barratt@ tl3 RWDI Proposal - 80.msg",200304 RWDI Proposal 2002869 800 Broadway San Diego.pdf,10p5,Cladding wind pressure services provide predictions of local wind ,dispute,328,"Cladding wind pressure services provide predictions of local wind 
pressures acting on the skin of any structure for designing the 
cladding & components, including facade, curtainwall, and roof systems. 
WIND TUNNEL MODELING
Wind tunnel testing is the most accurate means of predicting project-specific wind pressures. A scale model replica of the 
project and the immediate surroundings will be tested in a wind tunnel that simulates wind speeds and turbulence levels 
appropriate for the site. 
Scale Model Construction
A scale model of the project site will be constructed at a scale 
appropriate for the size of the structure, to capture the relevant 
architectural details. Taps, which measure wind pressure, will 
be installed on the surface of the model and will be located to 
capture possible regions of high wind loads. 
 Wind Tunnel Testing
A boundary-layer wind tunnel, equipped with spires and floor roughness, will 
be used to simulate the natural wind speed and turbulence profiles 
approaching the site. Time series of the instantaneous wind pressures at 
each pressure tap will be collected for 36 wind directions. The mean, root-
mean-square (RMS) and the peak maximum and minimum pressure 
coefficients will then be derived from the wind tunnel data. 
 Analysis & Deliverable
s
The pressure coefficients from the wind tunnel will be combined with the 
statistical model of the local wind climate, which includes the strength and 
directionality of severe winds. The results of this analysis are the predicted peak 
external pressures for the return period of interest. To determine the differential 
pressures applicable for design, the internal pressures will be estimated and 
added to the external pressures. The differential pressure across elements 
exposed to wind on opposite sides will be directly measured. The predicted 
design wind pressures will be presented in the form of block diagrams 
superimposed on the project’s elevations and roof plan. 

PEDESTRIAN LEVEL WINDS 
Pedestrian level wind services evaluate wind speeds and 
 frequencies and how they impact the comfort and safety of 
people in outdoor spaces."
