All preliminary work and preliminary consultations with the Architect will be charged on an hourly basis in 
accordance with the attached list of hourly charge out rates, however, please note that all charges for 
preliminary work are included in the above fixed fees. The proposed fixed fee does include for attending 
site meetings; however, we are on site regularly once construction begins (inspecting rebar), so attending 
these meetings only when we are required is appreciated. 
 
Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be John Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng., Struct.Eng. 
John Markulin is a licensed structural engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, California, Washington, 
Arizona, and Texas, with more than 28 years of experience designing a wide variety of buildings, including 
tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, and 
institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, and office 
buildings. 
 
John Markulin will participate heavily in the preliminary stages of the work, which will include preliminary 
design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. After the initial stages of design are 
complete, John will be assisted by senior partner Jason Stuart, who has more than 19 years of experience 
in the design of four to six level low-rise wood-frame residential buildings; however, John Markulin will 
remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
Additional staff dedicated to this project will include Conor Murtagh, B.Sc., AScT, Eng.L.; Nelson Yu, 
Structural CAD Technician; and Kyle Frank, Senior Production Manager. All personnel listed have extensive 
experience with similar projects. 
 
We wish to confirm that we have the resources to start working on this project right away, and we are able 
to meet the proposed timeline as indicated in your May 19, 2020 email. 
 
Scope of Structural Services 
 
Our scope of services includes detailed coordination with the Architect and other consultants, as well as 
developing the project in Revit/BIM or AutoCAD. We will assist the Architect in completing Schematic 
Design Documents along with providing local technical expertise and participate in local engineering/sub-
consultant coordination in support of this phase of the work. Sketches of the structure will be provided, 
defining dimensions of the structure in detail, so Architect's drawings can reflect real structural member 
sizes. Preliminary drawings of the structure will be provided in sufficient detail for preliminary pricing of the 
structure. The preliminary structure will be coordinated with the needs of the Architect and other consultants 
(mechanical and electrical). Based on the DP submission, we will create and coordinate construction 
documentation (drawings and specifications) as required to issue for tender, building permit and 
construction. We will coordinate with the Architect and other consultants in the development of the 
construction documentation. We are able to change structure as needed to meet final needs of Architect 
and other consultants and keep the structure on budget, as well as to incorporate the recommendations of 
any specialist consultants if required. 
 
The foregoing proposed fees are for normal basic structural engineering services as follows:"
