Proiect Personnel & Experience
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be John Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng., Struct.Eng.
John Markulin is a licensed structural engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, California, Washington,
Arizona, and Texas, with more than 28 years of experience designing a wide variety of buildings, including
tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, and
institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, and office
buildings.
John Markulin will participate heavily in the preliminary stages of the work, which will include preliminary
design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. After the initial stages of design are
complete, John will be assisted by senior partner Jason Stuart, who has more than 19 years of experience
in the design of four to six level low-rise wood-frame residential buildings; however, John Markulin will
remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. Additional staff dedicated to this project
will include Conor Murtagh, B.Sc., AScT; Simon Szarkiewicz, Senior CAD Technologist; Nelson Yu,
Structural CAD Technician; and Kyle Frank, Senior Production Manager. All personnel listed have extensive
experience with similar projects.
For further information on key project personnel and an introduction to Bryson Markulin Zickmantel
Structural Engineers, please visit our website at www.bmzse.com.
Scope of Structural Services
Our scope of services includes detailed coordination with the Architect and other consultants, as well as
developing the project in AutoCAD. We will assist the Architect in completing Schematic Design Documents
along with providing local technical expertise and participate in local engineering/sub-consultant
coordination in support of this phase of the work. Sketches of the structure will be provided, defining
dimensions of the structure in detail, so Architect's drawings can reflect real structural member sizes.
Preliminary drawings of the structure will be provided in sufficient detail for preliminary pricing of the
structure. The preliminary structure will be coordinated with the needs of the Architect and other consultants
(mechanical and electrical). Based on the DP submission, we will create and coordinate construction
