† Please note: This fixed fee allows for 60 site inspections. Additional field reviews will be billed at a rate 
of $300.00/visit, covering up to 2.0 hours, at which point hourly rates will apply. 
 
All preliminary work and preliminary consultations with the Architect will be charged on an hourly basis in 
accordance with the attached list of hourly charge out rates, however, please note that all charges for 
preliminary work are included in the above fixed fees. The proposed fixed fee does include for attending 
site meetings; however, we are on site regularly once construction begins (inspecting rebar), so attending 
these meetings only when we are required is appreciated. 
 
Over and above the noted proposed fixed fees, we recommend a budget of a maximum of $1,000.00 for 
normal disbursements (e.g. courier costs), per building, not including printing and plotting. 
 
Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be John Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng., 
Struct.Eng. John Markulin is a licensed structural engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, California, 
Washington, Arizona, and Texas, with more than 28 years of experience designing a wide variety of 
buildings, including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, 
and institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, and 
office buildings. 
 
John Markulin will participate heavily in the preliminary stages of the work, which will include preliminary 
design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. He will be assisted and backed up directly 
by Kevin Wurmlinger, P.Eng., who has more than 12 years of consulting structural engineering design 
experience, and Jim DesRoches, P.Eng. who has more than 30 years of experience in the design of mixed-
use projects; however, John Markulin will remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
Additional staff dedicated to this project will include Adrian Crowder, M.A.Sc., EIT; Lindsay Finnigan, 
Senior Structural BIM Technologist; and Kyle Frank, Senior Structural Drafting Manager. All personnel 
listed have extensive experience with similar projects. 
 
For further information on key project personnel and an introduction to Kor Structural, please visit our 
website at www.korstructural.com. 
 
Scope of Structural Services 
 
Our scope of services includes detailed coordination with the Architect and other consultants, as well as 
developing the project in Revit/BIM or AutoCAD. We will assist the Architect in completing Schematic 
Design Documents along with providing local technical expertise and participate in local engineering/sub-
consultant coordination in support of this phase of the work. Sketches of the structure will be provided, 
defining dimensions of the structure in detail, so Architect's drawings can reflect real structural member 
sizes. Preliminary drawings of the structure will be provided in sufficient detail for preliminary pricing of the 
structure. The preliminary structure will be coordinated with the needs of the Architect and other 
consultants (mechanical and electrical). Based on the DP submission, we will create, and coordinate 
construction documentation (drawings and specifications) as required to issue for tender, building permit 
and construction. We will coordinate with the Architect and other consultants in the development of the 
construction documentation. We can change structure as needed to meet final needs of Architect and 
other consultants and keep the structure on budget, as well as to incorporate the recommendations of any 
specialist consultants if required. 
The foregoing proposed fees are for normal basic structural engineering services as follows: 

 
 
 
 
