Phase 2 Redesign 
 
Dilworth Shopping Centre – 2339 Highway 97, Kelowna, B.C. 
 
Kor Reference Number: 30978-01 X.4 \12 
 
This is an addendum to our original fee proposal for structural engineering services for the project located 
at Dilworth Shopping Centre – 2339 Highway 97, Kelowna, B.C. (the “Project”). Our original fee proposal 
dated January 6, 2021, assumed the project comprised of four 6-storey mixed-use development with 475 
rental units to be built over one level of below grade parking structure. The estimated gross buildable area 
was 582,000 sq.ft. 
 
Based on recent architectural changes provided by Arcadis and at your direction, additional structural work 
will be required for the proposed redesign of phase 2. 
 
We propose an additional fixed fee of $35,000 for these changes. This includes: 
• 
Coordinating the new column and wall locations in the parkade. 
• 
Redesigning and re-detailing the L1 slab, basement walls and revising the foundations to suit. 
• 
Coordinating new L1 slab step locations. 
• 
Moving and redesigning the elevator cores and stairs in building 2B. 
• 
Coordinating new L1 commercial area column layout. 
• 
Redesigning the concrete seismic system. 
• 
Moving and redesigning steel canopies. 
• 
Updating framing due to unit changes. 
• 
Coordinating new shearwall locations in both buildings due to unit changes. 
• 
Incorporating any miscellaneous items from Phase 1 in Phase 2 drawings. 
• 
Pool shell structure design. 
 
All other Scope of Structural Engineering Services and Summary of Typical Services and Exclusions remain 
as per our original fee proposal dated January 6, 2021 
 
Approval to Proceed: 
 
We will proceed with our work upon receipt of a signed copy of this fee proposal. If you have any questions 
or need additional information, please contact the undersigned. 
 
We propose to invoice on a monthly basis. It is our policy to state that we reserve the right to discontinue 
our work if the client fails to meet his commitments, and we will not be responsible for any damages arising 
therefrom."
