Re: Additional Structural Engineering Services
 Reduction in Building Height
 Quince @ Bankers Hill, San Diego, California 
KOR Reference Number: 30997-01X.4 05

As you know, we have been asked by Cast Development LLC to provide additional structural engineering services to reduce the height of the building and add an additional penthouse suite at level 15 & 16. This has resulted in changes to structure as shown on the updated architectural drawings by Works Progress Architecture dated January 10, 2024, as follows:

Revised Design of the Lateral Load Resisting System

Reduction in floor-to-floor height above grade reduces the building height and header depths with changes the performance of the structure for lateral resistance for wind and seismic loading.
This requires a full redesign of the lateral load resisting system which includes shearwalls, header beams, foundations, and columns.
Updating structural calculations for submittal to the city.
Further plan check review time spent to respond to city plan check comments.

Addition of Penthouse Suite at Level 15 & 16

Addition of 2 story penthouse unit at levels 15 & 16 expanded the floor plate at these two levels and added an interconnecting stair.
This required repositioning of several columns and redesign of the slabs at levels 15 through 17.
Lateral design was also adjusted to accommodate the increase in mass at these expanded levels.


Our proposed fee for these additional services is $20,000.

In order to keep the project on schedule - we have proceeded with this work in good faith.

Please return a signed copy of this proposal with your approval.

We expect to bill for these services in our next monthly billing cycles as the work is completed.

We trust the above information is satisfactory, please do not hesitate to contact us if you have any questions. 

Yours truly,

Kor Structural 
EGBC Permit #1000378


