4b887b093af5,30997-01,30997-01,Cast Development LLC,The Quince @ Bankers Hill San Diego CA,client,draft,1/4,,2024-10-15,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\30997-01 (The Quince – Bankers Hill, San Diego CA)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\KL3-#3718442-v2-MFA___Quince_-_Comments_to_Collateral_Assignment_of_Engineering_Agreement_(Structural).docx",,0p2,W I T N E S S E T H :,indemnity|termination|payment|permits_approvals|dispute|warranty_reperform|assignment_subconsultants|lien,2144,"W I T N E S S E T H :
WHEREAS, Assignor, the lenders party thereto (each a “Lender” and collectively, the “Lenders”) and Administrative Agent have entered into a Loan Agreement dated as of the date hereof (as amended, modified, restated, consolidated, replaced or supplemented from time to time, the “Loan Agreement”), pursuant to which the Lenders have agreed to make a loan to Assignor in the maximum principal sum of up to [One Hundred Ten Million Four Hundred Forty-Nine Thousand Eighty and No/100 Dollars ($110,449,080.00)] (the “Loan”). Capitalized terms used but not defined herein shall have the respective meanings given such terms in the Loan Agreement; and 
WHEREAS, the Loan is secured, inter alia, by that certain Deed of Trust, Assignment of Leases and Rents, Security Agreement and Fixture Filing, dated as of the date hereof (as amended, modified, restated, consolidated, replaced or supplemented from time to time, the “Security Instrument”), made by Assignor to [ ], as trustee, for the benefit of Administrative Agent, encumbering the Property; and 
WHEREAS, pursuant to that certain Quince Commercial Consultant Agreement, dated as of January 23, 2021, between Assignor (as successor-in-interest to Quince Commercial LLC, a California limited liability company, as “Company” therein) and KOR Structural, a British Columbia general partnership (“Engineer”), as consultant, as assigned to Assignor by Company pursuant to that certain Bill of Sale, Assignment and Assumption of Leases and Contracts dated as of July 12, 2024, by and between Company, as assignor, and Assignor, as assignee (as the same may be further amended, modified, restated, consolidated, replaced or supplemented from time to time, the “Engineer Agreement”, a true, correct and complete copy of which is attached hereto as Exhibit A), Assignor has engaged the services of Engineer to perform services in connection with the design and construction of the Improvements; and 
WHEREAS, in order to induce Lenders to make the Loan and to further secure the payment of the Debt, Administrative Agent has requested that Assignor execute and deliver this Assignment; and
WHEREAS, Assignor has agreed to the execution and delivery of this Assignment.
NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the sum of Ten Dollars ($10.00) and other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and legal sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the parties hereto agree as follows: 
1. Assignor hereby absolutely grants a first lien on and security interest in, and hereby assigns, transfers and sets over to Administrative Agent as additional security for the Debt, all of the Assignor’s right, title and interest in, to and under the Engineer Agreement, including all conditions, riders and exhibits, if any, forming a part thereof and supplements, modifications and amendments thereto, and any other agreements between Assignor and Engineer pertaining to design and construction of the Improvements, together with all rights, powers, privileges, claims, remedies and causes of action of every kind which Assignor now has or may in the future have with respect to or by reason of its interest in the Engineer Agreement.
2. This Assignment is given to secure the Debt pursuant to the terms of the Loan Agreement and the Security Instrument. The parties intend that this Assignment shall be a present, actual, absolute and unconditional assignment and shall, immediately upon execution, give Administrative Agent the right to assume Assignor’s interest in the Engineer Agreement; provided, however, that so long as no Event of Default shall have occurred and be continuing, Assignor shall have a license to utilize the Engineer Agreement in accordance with the terms thereof and exercise all rights and remedies with respect thereto. If an Event of Default shall have occurred and be continuing, Assignor’s license mentioned in the immediately preceding sentence shall cease and terminate, without the execution of any further instrument or document or the taking of any other act on the part of Administrative Agent, and in such event, Administrative Agent shall be entitled, but not required, to exercise every right, option, power or authority inuring to Assignor under the Engineer Agreement; provided, however, (i) Administrative Agent shall endeavor to give Assignor prompt notice following such automatic revocation and (ii) the license granted to Assignor herein shall automatically be reinstated if there are no then-existing Events of Default. 
3. Assignor hereby irrevocably directs Engineer, upon demand and after notice from Administrative Agent of the occurrence of an Event of Default under any of the Loan Documents, to recognize and accept Administrative Agent as the holder of the Engineer’s rights allowed under the Engineer Agreement for any and all purposes as fully as it would recognize and accept Assignor and the performance of Assignor thereunder, subject however to the reinstatement provisions in Section 2 hereof. Assignor does hereby constitute and appoint Administrative Agent, while this Assignment remains in force and effect, irrevocably, and with full power of substitution and revocation, its true and lawful attorney-in-fact coupled with an interest for and in its name, place and stead, after the occurrence and during the continuance of such an Event of Default, to demand and enforce compliance with all the Assignor’s rights under terms and conditions of the Engineer Agreement and all benefits accrued thereunder, whether at law, in equity or otherwise, subject however to the reinstatement provisions in Section 2 hereof. 
4. Neither this Assignment nor any action or inaction on the part of Administrative Agent shall constitute an assumption on the part of Administrative Agent of any duty or obligation with respect to the Engineer Agreement, nor shall Administrative Agent have any duty or obligation to make any payment to be made by Assignor under the Engineer Agreement, or to present or file any claim, or to take any other action to collect or enforce the payment of any amounts or the performance of any obligations which have been assigned to Administrative Agent or to which it may be entitled hereunder at any time or times. No action or inaction on the part of Administrative Agent shall adversely affect or limit in any way the rights of Administrative Agent hereunder or under or with respect to the Engineer Agreement, and Administrative Agent shall not incur any liability on account of any action taken (or not taken) by it or on its behalf in connection with the Engineer Agreement in good faith, provided as to the Engineer such acts or omissions are lawful and consistent with Assignor’s rights contemplated under this Assignment.
5. Assignor hereby covenants and agrees that Assignor shall not, without the prior written consent of Administrative Agent, modify, amend, change or terminate the Engineer Agreement, except as required by any Governmental Authority or otherwise expressly permitted in the Loan Agreement. Except as pursuant to this Assignment, Assignor will not assign or create any further encumbrance or hypothecation of Assignor’s interest in the Engineer Agreement, other than Permitted Exceptions. 
6. Assignor hereby agrees to indemnify and to defend and hold Administrative Agent and the Lenders harmless against and from all liability loss, damage and expense, including reasonable attorneys’ fees, which they may or shall incur by reason of this Assignment, or by reason of any commercially reasonable action taken in good faith by Administrative Agent hereunder or with respect to the Engineer Agreement, and against and from any and all claims and demands whatsoever which may be asserted against Administrative Agent or any Lender by reason of any alleged obligation or undertaking on its part to perform or discharge any of the terms, covenants and conditions contained in the Engineer Agreement; provided, however, that notwithstanding the foregoing, in no event shall Assignor be liable for any Excluded Expenses, nor for Administrative Agent’s and the Lenders’ attorneys’ fees in connection with any action in which Borrower prevails on the merits, and Assignor’s reimbursement obligations hereunder shall be subject to Section 4.18 of the Loan Agreement (except to the extent such may be owed to the Engineer under the terms and conditions of this Assignment). Should Administrative Agent or any Lender incur any such liability, loss, damage or expense, the amount thereof, together with interest thereon at the Default Rate of interest under the Note, shall be payable by Assignor to Administrative Agent and the Lenders within ten (10) Business Days of written demand therefor, or at the option of Administrative Agent, Administrative Agent may reimburse itself therefor out of any receipts, rents, income or profits of the Property collected by Administrative Agent before the application of such receipts, rents, income or profits to any other obligations of Assignor under the Loan Documents, and such amounts and interest shall be additional indebtedness of Assignor secured by the Security Instrument and by the other Loan Documents securing all or part of the Loan. It is further understood that in the absence of a foreclosure or deed-in-lieu of foreclosure this Assignment shall not operate to constitute Administrative Agent as a lender in possession of the Property, or to place responsibility for the construction, control, care, management or repair of the Improvements upon Administrative Agent, nor shall it operate to make Administrative Agent responsible or liable (as to Assignor) for any waste committed with respect to the Property by any party, or for any Hazardous Substances placed upon or found at the Property, or for any dangerous or defective condition of the Improvements or for any negligence in the construction, management, up-keep, repair or control of the Improvements resulting in loss, injury, death or damage to any contractor, sub-contractor, licensee, invitee, employee, or other party, or for any other thing or matter whatsoever, other than, in each case, to the extent of Administrative Agent’s gross negligence or willful misconduct.
7. Assignor shall remain liable to, and shall, perform all of its obligations under the Engineer Agreement and shall, at its sole cost and expense, enforce the Engineer Agreement in a commercially reasonable manner and comply in all material respects with all of its obligations under the Engineer Agreement and all the terms thereof. Assignor shall give Administrative Agent prompt notice of any material default by any party under the Engineer Agreement. 
8. Upon the occurrence and during the continuance of an Event of Default, Administrative Agent shall be entitled to all of the rights, remedies, powers and privileges available to a secured party under the Uniform Commercial Code in any jurisdiction whose laws may apply and this Assignment shall constitute a direction to and full authority to Engineer to perform its obligations under the Engineer Agreement for the benefit of Administrative Agent without proof to Engineer of the default of Assignor. In addition, Assignor agrees that it shall, promptly upon request of Administrative Agent following such Event of Default, execute and deliver notices to Engineer directing that future performance of Engineer’s obligations be made at the direction of Administrative Agent. Assignor hereby irrevocably authorizes Engineer to rely upon and comply with any notice or demand by Administrative Agent for the performance by Engineer of its obligations under the Engineer Agreement for the benefit of Administrative Agent, and Engineer shall not have any right or duty to inquire whether an Event of Default has actually occurred, and Assignor shall have no right to countermand its authorization herein to Engineer to perform for the benefit of Administrative Agent. 
9. Assignor represents and warrants that it has full right, power and authority to assign its interests in the Engineer Agreement assigned hereby, subject to the terms thereof, and that (a) the Engineer Agreement is in existence on the date hereof and is in full force and effect in accordance with its terms, (b) Assignor has delivered to Administrative Agent true, correct and complete copy of the Engineer Agreement in existence as of the date hereof, (c) except as cited above, neither the Engineer Agreement nor any part thereof has been assigned, pledged or encumbered by Assignor except pursuant to this Assignment and the other Loan Documents (and except as otherwise permitted thereby), (d) no default or event of default by any party which remains uncured beyond the expiration of any applicable grace or notice period has occurred and is continuing under the Engineer Agreement, (e) to Assignor’s knowledge, Engineer does not have any defense, set-off or counterclaim against Assignor to the performance of any obligations of Engineer and (f) its principal place of business is its address for notices is as set forth in the preamble to this Assignment.
10. Assignor, at its expense, shall execute and deliver all such instruments and take all such action as Administrative Agent may reasonably request from time to time in order to obtain the full benefits of this Assignment and of the rights and powers herein created and to maintain and perfect the security interest granted in this Assignment. To the extent permitted by law, Assignor irrevocably authorizes Administrative Agent, at the expense of Assignor, to file financing statements and continuation statements with respect to the Engineer Agreement without the signature of Assignor."
