ENGINEER’S CONSENT

Effective as of [October ], 2024, the undersigned (“Engineer”) hereby expressly consents to the above and foregoing Collateral Assignment of Engineering Agreement (Structural Engineer) (the “Assignment”). All capitalized terms used and not otherwise defined herein shall have the meanings ascribed to each in the Assignment. 

Engineer agrees that (a) Engineer shall, simultaneously with the giving to Assignor of any notice of default or termination under the Engineer Agreement, send a copy of such notice to Administrative Agent at Administrative Agent’s address at 1251 Avenue of the Americas, 22nd Floor, New York, New York 10020, Attention: Specialty Finance Department, Commercial Real Estate, and with a copy to K&L Gates LLP, 599 Lexington Avenue, New York, New York 10022, Attention: Alan Schacter, Esq., and (i) such notice of default or termination given by Engineer to Assignor shall not be effective unless and until Administrative Agent shall have received (or refused delivery thereof) a copy thereof as provided above, and (ii) no such notice of termination given by Engineer to Assignor shall be effective until ten (10) Business Days after Administrative Agent’s receipt of a copy of such notice, during which time Administrative Agent shall have the right, but not the obligation, to cure the default or cause the default to be cured, in which case, following such cure, the termination notice shall be of no further force or effect, and (b) upon Engineer’s receipt of notice from Administrative Agent of the existence (and during the occurrence and continuance of) of an Event of Default under the Loan Agreement and a written notice by Administrative Agent that Engineer shall continue to perform its agreements, covenants and obligations under the Engineer Agreement, then Engineer shall continue to perform its services under the Engineer Agreement solely for the benefit of Administrative Agent so long as Engineer has received or continues to receive the compensation required under the Engineer Agreement. In furtherance of clause (b) above, Administrative Agent shall have the right to enforce the Engineer Agreement. 

Administrative Agent or any purchaser or transferee of the Property pursuant to a foreclosure sale, deed in lieu of foreclosure or otherwise which is affiliated with or a nominee of Administrative Agent (the foregoing collectively with Administrative Agent, the “Purchaser”) may elect in writing to: (i) have the Engineer continue or recommence performance under the Engineer Agreement for the benefit of such Purchaser, in which case the Engineer shall thereafter perform under the Engineer Agreement; or (ii) terminate the Engineer Agreement and to have the Engineer stop work (if it has not already done so) and vacate the Property, in which case the Engineer shall promptly stop all work and vacate the Property. 

If Purchaser has requested that Engineer continue or recommence work under the Engineer Agreement, Purchaser agrees to assume Assignor’s obligations, as “Company” under the Engineer Agreement and make payments to Engineer pursuant to the Engineer Agreement of all fees and costs due under the Engineer Agreement, including for all such services, work, labor and materials performed or furnished under the Engineer Agreement prior to the date Purchaser acquired title to the Property; provided that such fees and costs are due and payable in accordance with the Engineer Agreement, and provided further that Lenders had not previously funded any such amounts pursuant to an Advance made under the Loan Agreement. Purchaser shall be entitled to reimbursement from Assignor for all sums paid to the Engineer by Purchaser. 
 
If Purchaser has terminated the Engineer Agreement and has requested Engineer to stop work and vacate the Property, then (i) the Engineer will look to Assignor, and not to Purchaser, for all sums owing under the Engineer Agreement and Purchaser shall not be liable for any such amounts owing Engineer by Assignor, (ii) Engineer shall not be required to continue any work under the Engineer Agreement except work for which Engineer has been paid, (iii) the Engineer shall, within thirty (30) days of such termination, assign to or at the direction of Purchaser deliver to Purchaser or any designee thereof, all records, documents, drawings and all other tangible and intangible property in the Engineer’s possession related to or arising from the construction of the Improvements, provided that the Engineer shall not be required to deliver any items that it would not be obligated to deliver to Assignor under the Engineer Agreement or applicable law, and Engineer shall be entitled to reimbursement for any reasonable out-of-pocket costs incurred in connection with any such assignment or delivery, and (iv) in no event shall Purchaser be subject to or bound by any claim or defense which Engineer may have against Assignor, by any obligation of Assignor to Engineer or any third party or by any amendment, modification or assignment of, or supplement to, the Engineer Agreement made in contravention of the Assignment. 

Engineer hereby represents and warrants to Administrative Agent that the Engineer Agreement is in full force and effect free from default and that the undersigned has the requisite power and authority to execute and deliver this consent in the name of Engineer. Engineer shall not be deemed to consent to any amendment, modification or change to the Assignment unless its consent thereto is specifically given in writing.

All fees due to Engineer under the Engineer Agreement and all rights and privileges of Engineer to such fees are hereby, and shall at all times continue to be, subject and unconditionally and irrevocably subordinate in all respects in lien and payment to the lien and payment in full of the Security Instrument, the Note, the Loan Agreement and the other Loan Documents and to any renewals, extensions, modifications, assignments, replacements or consolidations thereof and the rights, privileges and powers of Administrative Agent or Lender thereunder.

It is expressly understood that Administrative Agent does not assume or have any obligation to Engineer to exercise its rights under the Assignment, and that the option to exercise such right rests in the sole and absolute discretion of Administrative Agent.


