All preliminary work and preliminary consultations with the Architect will be charged on an hourly basis in 
accordance with the attached list of hourly charge out rates, however, please note that all charges for 
preliminary work are included in the above fixed fees. 
 
The proposed fixed fees include our time to travel to California four (4) times during the design phases (1. 
through 4.) to meet with building officials, architects, and others as needed. Also, our proposed fixed fees 
allow for 6 site visits during the Construction Review Phase for Code required structural observations. 
 
Over and above the noted fixed fees, we will invoice monthly for normal disbursements such as: travel 
expenses, courier costs, external printing, and plotting, etc. We propose an additional fee of $1,200 USD 
per trip to cover travel expenses. This flat fee for travel expenses will be split between other projects in the 
area as appropriate. 
 
Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be Jim DesRoches, PE. The Engineer of 
Record for this project will be John A. Markulin, M.Eng., PE, SE. John Markulin is a licensed Structural 
Engineer in California, Washington, Arizona, and Texas. John brings more than 28 years’ significant project 
experience designing a wide variety of building types and materials. Jim DesRoches is a licensed 
Professional Engineer in Washington State and has more than 3 decades of experience designing similar 
buildings, as well as more than 20 years’ experience designing, permitting, and directing construction of 
projects in Southern California. Please refer to the included resumes at the end of this document for further 
background information on for John Markulin and Jim DesRoches. 
 
Jim DesRoches and John Markulin will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will include 
preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Additional staff dedicated to 
this project will include; Kyle Frank, Senior Structural Drafting Manager; Jeremy Atkinson, M.A.Sc., P.Eng.; 
Griffin Dow, B.A.Sc., EIT; Henry H.C. Xu, M.A.Sc., EIT; Serban Acosti, Structural BIM Technologist; and 
Ali Keshavarz, Structural BIM Technologist. All personnel listed are involved with the 1011 Union Street 
project have extensive experience with similar projects. 
 
Since 1998, our team has provided invaluable structural engineering, consultation, design, and inspection 
services on hundreds of projects across North America and Asia. 
 
We deliver efficient and creative designs that are buildable solutions for projects of all sizes and types, 
including low-rise to high-rise residential (as tall as 63-storeys), large mixed-use and commercial/retail, 
office, light industrial, institutional and public facilities such as ice rinks and sports facilities, extended care 
facilities, and seismic upgrading, addition, and renovation projects. We have experience working with all 
forms of concrete, structural and load-bearing steel, wood-frame, and masonry. 
 
Starting as a partnership between three seasoned professional engineers 20 years ago, we have grown 
into a family of more than 40 professionals committed to excellent client service, quality and innovative 
building solutions, and aspiring to be an industry center of excellence. 
 
Following this proposal is an illustrated sample of some of our most recent and notable projects. For further 
information on key project personnel and an introduction to Kor Structural, please visit our website at 
www.korstructural.com. 
 
 
 

