Times and Performance:
Consultant’s Services will be performed in a timely manner consistent with customary professional practice and the desire that Project proceeds as expeditiously as practical. Specifically, Consultant will use due and diligent efforts to meet the schedule provided to Consultant by Owner/Company. Consultant shall prepare a detailed time line for each task shown above. Consultant and Owner/Company shall agree upon this time line. Consultant shall respond to questions from Owner/Company regarding plans within one (1) business day.
Compensation:
Owner/Company shall compensate Consultant for the basic services set forth above as is specified in Exhibit B Payment Schedule “Compensation Schedule.” If the scope of Project changes or if Owner/Company requests additional services, Consultant shall submit a fee proposal for these services based upon the standard Hourly Rates listed below. Consultant shall not commence these additional services without prior written authorization by separated agreement or change order.
Consultant shall provide Owner/Company with monthly invoices for Services rendered and costs advanced. Hourly fees if applicable, will be billed for hours worked each month and shall include a detailed itemization of how hours were spent. Flat fees will be billed on a percentage of work-completed basis for each basic service during the month.
Reimbursable expenses include expenses incurred by Consultant in the interest of the Project for:
Reproductions requested by Owner/Company.
Postage and handling of drawings and specifications.
Renderings and models requested by Owner/Company.
Mileage (mileage $0.56/mile).
Note: Owner/Company will pay a maximum of cost plus ten percent (10%) for all applicable reimbursable items.
Agency fees paid by the Consultant on behalf of the Owner/Company for securing approval of authorities having jurisdiction over Project shall be invoiced separate from basic services and other reimbursable expenses outlined in paragraph 3.C. Owner/Company reimbursement of agency fees shall not include any overhead and profit (OH&P) markup.


