B. 
Company will reimburse Consultant for reasonable expenses, at Consultant’s cost without mark-up, incurred by Consultant in 
providing consulting services to Company, including Travel Expenses as set forth in Exhibit B . Consultant will notify Company in 
advance of the categories and estimated amounts of any expenses which Consultant expects to incur in connection with 
providing services to Company during the course of this engagement. Upon Company’s request, Consultant agrees to provide 
receipts, invoices or other reasonable proof of such expenses. No compensation shall be allowed for administrative, overhead, 
insurance, word processing (normal or overflow secretarial time or overtime, or computer time or service), telephone calls, and 
mail and delivery costs payable to the United States Postal Service. 
C. 
Consultant shall submit one application for payment per month to be accepted for processing in accordance with Schedule of 
Invoice Submittal and Payment Dates (Exhibit C). The Payment Application must be submitted prior to the 10th of each month. If 
a properly completed payment application is submitted by the last day of each month, the Company will make any payment by 
the 10th of the following month. If, however, Company has a disagreement about the amount of the payment application, the 
Company will notify the Consultant, in writing, before the last day of the following month of the reasons for Company's 
disagreement and the amount of the payment that is being withheld. If Company reasonably believes that it has suffered any 
cost, loss, damage or liability arising from any negligent act or omission of the Consultant, the Company may withhold from 
further payment 150% of the amount of the cost, loss, damage or other liability as estimated, in good faith, by the Company. 
III. 
GENERAL PROVISIONS 
A. 
The term of this Agreement shall begin on January 29, 2022 and terminate upon completion of Consultant’s Services as stated 
by the Company, unless otherwise terminated pursuant to Section IX, upon completion of the parties obligations under this 
agreement. 
B. 
This Agreement shall be binding upon the successors or assigns of the Company and Consultant. 
C. 
Neither Consultant nor Company shall be responsible for delays or damages, or declared to be in default by reason of delays in 
performance or by reason of strikes, lockouts, accidents, acts of God, and other delays unavoidable or beyond Company’s or 
Consultant’s reasonable control, delays in approval by governmental agencies, or delays in work of other consultants performing 
