The scope of the project is to produce a detailed final design of the VCD including the viscoelastic (VE) damper 
panels optimized for cost and constructability through close interaction with Kor Structural (Kor) and damper 
manufacturers. 
 
At the end of this scope of work the following will have been accomplished: 
 
i) 
EOR will have all necessary design information to be able to finalize the structural design of 
the entire building and submit drawings for permit. 
ii) 
VE damper panel design will be finalized. 
iii) 
VE damper panel drawings and VCD drawings will be finalized. 
 
BOSA Developments will have all relevant information and documents to obtain a final binding quotation 
for fabrication and delivery of the VE damper panels including all final commercial and delivery terms. 
 
 
At the end of the project, Kinetica will continue to support all parties to successfully implement the VCD in the 
project."
1dee7792613a,31030-01,31030-01,Bosa Development Corp.,4430-4488 Halifax St Burnaby,KOR,proposal,,,2024-02-14,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31030-01 (Halifax 4430 - 4488 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Kinetica Consulting Proposal for KD-23-028(4430-4488 Halifax St)_rev_2024_01_17_FINAL.(JM)pdf.pdf,,2,SCOPE OF SERVICES,field_review,682,"2 SCOPE OF SERVICES 
 
The design will be separated into three phases: i) Preliminary design assessment with EOR, ii) Detailed VCD 
design and modelling information transfer and iii) VCD and damped building performance assessment. Following 
the design phases there will be quality control and site review phase which Kinetica will participate in as well. 
Each step is described below: 
 
i) 
Preliminary Design Development with EOR 
 
When Kor has finalized the most up to date design models, Kinetica will perform the following work: 
 

Viscoelastic Coupling Dampers for 4430-4488 Halifax St. 
 
 01/17/2024 
Proposal 
Page 1 
 
 
K23-028 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
Kinetica and EOR will work closely to define the VCD configuration that achieves the damping requirements 
defined by the wind tunnel consultants. 
 
 
Kinetica and EOR will investigate the VCD configuration to achieve the overall performance goals on the 
project. 
 
 
Kinetica and EOR will develop a steel connection detail that can provide the required strength and stiffness 
to connect the VCDs to the structure. 
 
 
Kinetica will assist EOR in developing the structural performance requirements for the building with VCDs. 
 
 
ii) 
VCD Design and Information Transfer 
 
After approval from EOR on the design concept, Kinetica will provide the following services: 
 
 
Kinetica will produce a final VE damper for the tower optimized for cost and performance and check all 
structural limit states according to AISC-360-16 and CAN/CSA S16-19 for the dampers. 
 
 
Kinetica will produce final VE damper panel drawings for manufacturing. 
 
 
Kinetica will establish VE material properties for analytical models and assist EOR in doing their independent 
assessment of the level of added damping in the building within ETABS software. 
 
 
iii) 
VCD and Damped Building Performance Assessment 
 
After the design has been finalized, Kinetica will carry out a state-of-the-art detailed performance assessment 
of the VCD and the damped building: 
 
 
Kinetica will assess the damper performance within the overall structural model. 
 
 
If requested by design team, Kinetica will conduct time-history analyses on the building within ETABS with 
EOR using wind time-histories provided by the wind consultant and further validate the damper performance 
using Kinetica’s state-of-the-art models and extensive test database. 
 
 
iv) 
Quality Control and Site Review 
 
Following the design contract, Kinetica will continue to support the successful implementation on the project. The 
following will be included in this phase: 
 
 
Kinetica will support EOR in developing the VCD Quality Control and Quality Assurance program including 
requirements for production testing and specifications. 
 
 
Kinetica will oversee the QA and QC program of the VE damper panel manufacturer. This includes visiting 
during fabrication and manufacturing of the dampers and reviewing and witnessing the full-scale testing. 
Kinetica will also review steel mill certs reports, batch viscoelastic material testing reports and full-scale 
testing during production of the VE damper panels. 
 
 
Kinetica will stamp and seal the VE damper panel drawings and design the bolted connection. Kinetica will 
also fill the B.C. P.Eng. Schedule S-B and S-C forms. 
 
Kinetica will support EOR in developing the design of the connecting steel elements, lock-up connection and 
embedded portion of the connection of the damper panels to the structure. 
 
 
Kinetica will review shop drawings of the VCDs and VE damper panels. 
 

Viscoelastic Coupling Dampers for 4430-4488 Halifax St. 
 
 01/17/2024 
