under similar circumstances, at the same time and in the same or a similar locale. 
 
Kinetica shall be entitled to rely upon product information published by manufacturers and shall not be held liable for 
relying on information or representation which it reasonably believes to be accurate. 
 
Kinetica shall not: 
i. be required to make exhaustive or continuous on-site reviews; 
ii. be responsible for acts or omissions of the contractor, subcontractors, suppliers or any other persons 
performing any of the Work, or for failure of any of them to carry out the Work in accordance with the 
contract documents; 
iii. have control, charge, or supervision, or responsibility for construction means, methods, techniques, 
sequences, or procedures, or, for safety precautions and programs required in connection with the Work. 
 
The Client acknowledges that either Kinetica or the Client may engage consultants on behalf of and for the benefit and 
convenience of the Client; and agrees that Kinetica shall not be liable to the Client, in contract or in tort, for the acts, 
omissions or errors of such consultants whether retained by Kinetica or the Client. The Client also agrees to limit the 
professional liability for services rendered by such consultants to the lesser of the amount stated in this agreement or 
the amount of the professional liability insurance carried by each consultant. 
 
The Client shall not commence any claim or proceeding in contract, tort, breach of statutory duty or otherwise against 
any current or former employee, officer or director of Kinetica arising out of acts omissions or errors of such person 
pursuant to this contract. 
 
Termination 
Unless otherwise stated in the attached Agreement, the services of Kinetica terminate after completion of the work. 
 
Mediation 
In an effort to resolve any conflicts that arise during the design or construction of the project or following the 
completion of the project, the Client and Kinetica agree to use all reasonable efforts to resolve such disputes between 
themselves. 
 
The Client and Kinetica further agree that all disputes between them arising out of or relating to this Agreement shall 
be submitted to nonbinding mediation unless the parties mutually agree otherwise. 
 
Governing Laws and Assignment 
This Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario. Neither the Client nor Kinetica shall assign 
their obligations without the consent of the other. Such consent shall not be unreasonably withheld."
