skilled at finding structural solutions for complicated building arrangements that are both simple and 
efficient. In every project he also aims to balance the original design intent of the Architect, yet always 
taking into consideration the Client’s needs and desires. 
 
After the initial stages of design are complete, Conor Murtagh will be assisted by senior partner, Jason 
Stuart, who has more than 20 years of experience in the design of four to six level low-rise wood-frame 
residential buildings. Jason actively leads the growing specialized wood-frame team at KOR where he 
shares his extensive structural design experience and thorough knowledge of various materials on 
multiple projects. Jason is a seasoned structural designer and project manager who goes above and 
beyond to support project milestones, maintain open lines of communication between all stakeholders, 
and carefully supervises all phase of his projects from preliminary design through construction and project 
completion. 
 
Conor Murtagh and Jason Stuart will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will include 
preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Both Conor and Jason will be 
