Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be Kevin Wurmlinger, P.Eng. Struct.Eng., 
CEng, MIStructE. Kevin is a professional Designated Structural Engineer (P.Eng. Struct.Eng.) licensed in 
British Columbia with more than 20 years of experience designing a wide variety of buildings and types, 
including tall towers, office buildings, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, with expertise in 
concrete, steel, and timber. Kevin is involved in all stages of his projects from conceptual design through 
construction. He has extensive experience in structural design and review, consultant team coordination, 
drawing preparation, site reviews, as well as construction administration, which has continuously led to the 
successful delivery of his projects. 
 
After the initial stages of design are complete, Kevin Wurmlinger will be assisted by senior partner, John 
Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng. Struct.Eng., PE, SE, who is a licensed Structural Engineer in British Columbia, 
Alberta, California, Washington, Arizona, and Texas, and has more than 30 years of experience designing 
a wide variety of buildings, including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light 
industrial warehouses, and institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care 
facilities, hotels, and office buildings. John Markulin is responsible for delivering innovative structural 
engineering solutions for some of the firm’s most notable projects. John is an accomplished engineer with 
significant project experience in the design of reinforced concrete, pre-cast concrete, cast-in-place 
concrete, post-tensioned concrete, tilt-up concrete, structural steel, load-bearing steel stud, wood-frame, 
and masonry, as well as floor systems, vertical load systems and seismic and lateral systems. 
 
Kevin Wurmlinger and John Markulin will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will 
include preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Both Kevin Wurmlinger 
and John Markulin will be available and remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
Additional staff dedicated to this project will include: 
 
 Omar Alcazar Pastrana, M.A.Sc., P.Eng. 
 Andréa Neuviale, M.Eng., P.Eng. 
 Ted Olfert, M.A.Sc., EIT 
 Henry Xu, M.A.Sc., EIT 
 Michael Li, Senior Structural BIM Manager 
 Simon Szarkiewicz, Senior Structural CAD Manager 
 Chris Ford, Senior Structural BIM/CAD Technologist 
 
All personnel listed have extensive experience with similar projects. We would like to note that we have 
sufficient resources (more than 40 people) to meet your requirements on schedule. 
 
For further information on key project personnel and an introduction to Kor Structural, please visit our 
website at www.korstructural.com. 
 
Kor Structural has a good working relationship with Yamamoto Architects and we have worked on 
numerous projects together over the past years. 
 
Scope of Structural Services 
 
Our scope of services includes detailed coordination with the Architect and other consultants, as well as 
developing the project in Revit/BIM LOD 300 or AutoCAD. We will assist the Architect in completing 
Schematic Design Documents along with providing local technical expertise and participate in local 
engineering/sub-consultant coordination in support of this phase of the work. Sketches of the structure will 
be provided, defining dimensions of the structure in detail, so Architect's drawings can reflect real structural 

