Our fixed fees do include for attending site meetings during construction; however, we are on site regularly 
once construction begins (reviewing rebar), so attending these meetings only when we are required is 
appreciated. 
 
Over and above the noted proposed fixed fees, we recommend a budget allowance of $1,500 for normal 
disbursements (e.g., courier costs), not including printing and plotting. 
 
Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be John Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng. Struct.Eng., 
PE, SE. John Markulin is a licensed Structural Engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, California, 
Washington, Arizona, and Texas, with more than 30 years of experience designing a wide variety of 
buildings, including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, 
and institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, and office 
buildings. John Markulin is responsible for delivering innovative structural engineering solutions for some 
of the firm’s most notable projects. John is an accomplished engineer with significant project experience in 
the design of reinforced concrete, pre-cast concrete, cast-in-place concrete, post-tensioned concrete, tilt-
up concrete, structural steel, load-bearing steel stud, wood-frame, and masonry, as well as floor systems, 
vertical load systems and seismic and lateral systems. 
 
After the initial stages of design are complete, John Markulin will be assisted by senior partner, Rory Beirne, 
M.Eng., P.Eng. Struct.Eng., MIStructE, who has more than 15 years of experience in the construction 
industry, including more than a decade of structural design experience. His background as a carpenter, in 
conjunction with his experience as a structural and geotechnical engineer, has allowed him to gain a unique 
skillset encompassing all aspects of construction from the ground up. His practical approach to design and 
construction management has resulted in innovative and efficient solutions to some of our more challenging 
structural projects. 
 
John Markulin and Rory Beirne will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will include 
preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Both John and Rory will be 
available and remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
 
 
 

