7165 Fulton Ave, BC. The project will be executed by Intracorp and our project partner Belmont Properties. Please note 
that this invitation has been extended to other consulting firms. 
The project will be a two-phase redevelopment of an existing three multifamily tenanted rental buildings. A master 
rezoning will take place for both Phase 1 and Phase 2, with commencement of Phase 2 following completion of Phase 1. 
Phase 1 is envisioned for redevelopment of 7107, and 7165 Fulton Ave. The existing buildings will be replaced with strata 
condo density as well as an affordable rental building constructed for the purposes of replacement rental as per the City 
of Burnaby’s Rental Use Zoning Policy. The form of development for strata is envisioned to be two concrete towers at 40-
storey and 30-storey form, with a 6-storey connecting podium. The form of development for rental is envisioned to be one 
6-storey woodframe building. Underground parking of 4-storeys is envisioned to be located along the entirety of Phase 
01, with the affordable rental building accessing the parking via easement. 
Phase 2 will be the redevelopment of 7110 Fulton Ave envisioned to be 6-storey woodframe market rental, on one level of 
underground parking under the Phase 2 parcel. 
For Clarity, RFP proposals should be received with separate prices for Phase 01 and Phase 02. The project will require 
rezoning of both Phase 01 + Phase 02 at the outset of the project, and the Development Permit and Construction 
Documents for Phase 02 will only commence after construction completion of Phase 01. 
