Re: Structural Consulting Services Request for Fee Proposal – Lots 12&13 (Uplands Area 6) 
Project Overview 
Beedie Living is seeking Structural Consulting Services for two (16 and 20 storey) concrete high rise residential 
towers, currently known as Lots 12 and 13, located in the District of West Vancouver (DWV). The consolidated site 
area for these lots is 92,678 square feet. These parcels are part of a recent acquisition of 4 separate Lots from British 
Pacific Properties within Area 6 of the Uplands Community. The lots have already been subdivided and rezoned, and 
will be designed and built over one or two phases as outlined in Exhibit A. The selected consultant must ensure 
alignment with the current OCP and CD-3 zoning policy. For proposed Site Statistics, please refer to the Site Details 
chart below, as well as Exhibit B. 
 
For purposes of consultant coordination, this RFP encompasses all private assets within the lots as well as 
coordination of any changes made to adjacent private or public plans because of design impacts. See Exhibits C and 
D for current area and Consolidated Servicing Plans. 
 
Through their proposal, the consultant must demonstrate experience in the planning, design, and construction 
administration of high-end residential market condo projects. The project provides an excellent opportunity to 
showcase design excellence, inclusivity, and sustainability in one of the Region’s most desirable places to live. 
 
 
 Conceptual 3D Perspective - Lots 12 and 13 Form 

Background Information 
Site History 
 
In the 1990’s, British Pacific Properties focused exclusively on planning and development of its upland properties. 
The lands earmarked for development constituted an area of approximately 1,200 acres above the Upper Levels 
Highway between Marr Creek and Horseshoe Bay below the 1,200-foot contour. In line with the thinking of the 
times, British Pacific Properties concentrated on increasingly sophisticated urban planning and design, more efficient 
construction techniques and a continued sensitivity to the natural environment. Working closely with West 
Vancouver Council and its Official Community Plan, British Pacific Properties received Council’s approval of The 
Rogers Creek Area Development Plan in September of 2008 a major new development plan for over 200 acres of the 
most desirable residential real estate in Canada. This plan included Area 6 or the Uplands community and is where 
the subject sites are located. 
