As you know, we have been asked by Magellen Development to provide the additional structural engineering services for the re-design of the Lateral Load Resisting structure to meet the requirements of BCBC 2024. As you know when we started the project we were instructed to design to the structural requirements of BCBC 2018 and we proceeded to further the design of the structure on that basis. Our structural design to date has been completed to approximately 50% CD level. The following work will need to be completed to incorporate this change:

Re-design and re-analysis of the structural shearwalls will be required. This may require increased wall thickness and increased reinforcing steel.
Further Vs30 investigation by the geotechnical consultant is recommended to mitigate the increase in seismic loads from the BCBC 2024. Structural redesign will be performed considering the results of this further testing.
Shearwall foundations will require redesign and redetailing based on the new results from the shearwalls. 
Structural requirements for the tank will be shown on the structural drawings – all civil requirements to be shown on the Civil Engineers drawing.

Our proposed fee for these additional services is $5,000.

Please return a signed copy of this proposal with your approval.

We expect to bill for these services in our next monthly billing cycles as the work is completed.

We trust the above information is satisfactory, please do not hesitate to contact us if you have any questions.

Yours truly,

