The structural requirements of BCBC 2024 results in an increase in seismic loading over the outgoing BCBC 2018 building code.
Further Vs30 investigation by the geotechnical consultant is recommended to mitigate the increase in seismic loads. Structural redesign will be performed considering the results of this further testing.
Re-design and re-analysis of the structural shearwalls will be required. This may require increased wall thickness and increased reinforcing steel to adjust to thenew BCBC requirements.
Shearwall foundations will also require redesign and redetailing based on the new results from the Vs30 investigation and updated Seismic Loading. 

