Dear Rob: 
 
 
Re: 
Fee Proposal for Structural Engineering Services 
 
611 Brunswick Street, Prince George, BC 
 
Enclosed is our fee proposal for structural engineering services for the above noted project. The project is 
shown on DHk Architects preliminary architectural drawings dated May 2024, provided to us with your 
request for proposal email received October 3, 2024 
 
Project Description 
 
Our proposed fees are based on the following assumptions: 
 
 
 A 6-storey mixed-use building with approximately 45 affordable housing suites ranging from 
studio to 3-bedroom homes, with eight on site parking stalls at grade, residential lobby and 
amenity space. 
 
 The total structural area including slab on grade parking and amenity areas is estimated to be 
55,000 sq.ft. and the estimated breakdown is as follows: 
 
o 
Structural Wood frame above Level 2: 39,000 sq.ft. 
o 
Structural Concrete Transfer slab on Level 2: 8,000 sq.ft. 
o 
Slab on Grade at Level 1: 8,000 sq.ft. 
 
 We understand the proposed timeline/milestone dates to be as follows: 
o 
DP Application: Submission: Dec 2 (5 weeks) 
o 
Building Permit Submission: Feb 15 (12 Weeks) 
o 
Construction Commencement: June 15 
o 
Occupancy/Completion: Dec 2027 (18 months) 
o 
One Year Warranty Complete: Dec 2027 
 
The below fixed fees are based on 47,000 sq.ft. of above grade structural area. If the final area is 
increased or decreased, then our fees will be adjusted proportionally. 
 
 
 
 
 

 DHk Architects – 611 Brunswick Street, Prince George, BC 
Kor Structural • Fee Proposal dated October 7, 2024 
Page 2 of 6 
 
Proposed Fees 
 
The following fees are for complete structural engineering services for the project as noted in the 
following Scope of Structural Services. The proposed fixed fees for our services are as follows:"
2b59e1dae68e-bb0300,31171-01,31171-01,Yellowridge Construction Ltd.,611 Brunswick St Prince George,KOR,proposal,,,2024-12-11,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31171-01 (611 Brunswick St Prince George)\Newforma\email\2024-10\2024-10-07-2245-10-F7QW dsingh@korst Ugk Fee Proposal for S.eml,DHk Architects 611 Brunswick St Prince George BC 2024-10-04 KOR RB JS.pdf,4,Construction Phase Services and Field Reviews,permits_approvals|field_review,1016,"4 Construction Phase Services and Field Reviews 
$ 5,000 
Including up to 10 field review visits. † 
 
Total Base Fees 
$ 33,000 
 
† Additional field reviews over the above specified limit will be billed at a rate of $500 per visit, covering 
up to 2.0 hours, at which point hourly rates will apply. 
 
Our team has extensive experience in designing both 5-storey and 6-storey wood-frame buildings, so we 
are experts in the special design issues related to these structures. The Building Code prohibits shear 
wall transfers in wood-frame buildings over 4-storeys, hence we recommend consulting with us early 
during initial schematic design, so that important shear wall elements can be integrated into the unit plans 
and overall building massing. 
 
Preliminary work and preliminary consultations with the Architect will be charged on an hourly basis in 
accordance with the included ‘Appendix A’ Schedule of Standard Hourly Billing Rates, however, please 
note that all charges for preliminary work are included in the proposed Professional Services Fees. Our 
fixed fee does include for attending site meetings; however, we are on site regularly once construction 
begins (reviewing rebar), so attending these meetings only when we are required is appreciated. 
 
Over and above the noted proposed fixed fees, we recommend a budget allowance of $1,500 for normal 
disbursements (e.g., courier costs), not including printing and plotting. 
 
Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be Rory Beirne, M.Eng., P.Eng., C.Eng. 
(UK), Struct.Eng., MIStructE. Rory Beirne is a licensed structural engineer in British Columbia with more 
than 15 years of experience in the construction industry, including more than a decade of structural 
design experience. His background as a carpenter, in conjunction with his experience as a structural and 
geotechnical engineer, has allowed him to gain a unique skillset encompassing all aspects of construction 
from the ground up. His practical approach to design and construction management has resulted in 
innovative and efficient solutions to some of our more challenging structural projects. 
 
After the initial stages of design are complete, Rory Beirne will be assisted by senior partner, Jason 
Stuart, who has more than 20 years of experience in the design of four to six level low-rise wood-frame 
residential buildings. Jason actively leads the growing specialized wood-frame team at KOR where he 
shares his extensive structural design experience and thorough knowledge of various materials on 
multiple projects. Jason is a seasoned structural designer and project manager who goes above and 
beyond to support project milestones, maintain open lines of communication between all stakeholders, 
and carefully supervises all phase of his projects from preliminary design through construction and project 
completion. 
 
Rory Beirne and Jason Stuart will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will include 
preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Both Rory Beirne and Jason 
Stuart will be available and remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
 
 

