6530 Victoria Street, Vancouver, BC 
 
This is our fee proposal for structural engineering services for the above noted project. The project is shown 
on AIRstudio’s preliminary architectural drawings dated April 30, 2024, provided to us with your request for 
proposal email received August 2, 2024. 
 
Project Description 
 
Our proposed fees are based on the following assumptions: 
 
 A 6-storey mixed-use point access (single egress stair) residential / commercial building with 18 
residential units, courtyard and roof deck amenity spaces, at grade commercial units and parking, 
all over one level of below grade storage / services areas. 
 The total gross buildable area for the above is estimated to be 23,000 sq.ft. 
 We understand the proposed timeline of submitting for Building Permit by the end of the year and 
have sufficient resources to meet your schedule. 
 
Proposed Fees 
 
The following fees are for complete structural engineering services for the project as noted in the following 
Scope of Structural Services. The proposed fixed fees for our services are as follows:"
4b651d8da1ff-09b08a,31174-01,31174-01,1450991 BC Ltd.,6530 Victoria St Vancouver,KOR,proposal,,,2025-03-19,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31174-01 (6530 Victoria St Vancouver)\Newforma\email\2025-03\2025-03-11-1729-39-VWVN iroecker@air jBI Re- Fee Proposal f.eml,(1) Corrections_Jim Architecture 6530 Victoria St Vancouver 2024-08-07 KOR KW JM.pdf,4,Construction Phase Services and Field Reviews,permits_approvals|assignment_subconsultants|field_review,1019,"4 Construction Phase Services and Field Reviews 
$ 5,000 
Including up to 20 field reviews. † 
 
Total Base Fees 
$ 38,000 
 
† Additional field reviews over the above specified limit will be billed at a rate of $350 per visit, covering up 
to 2.0 hours, at which point hourly rates will apply. 
 
If the structural system for this project is decided to be wood-frame, our team has extensive experience in 
designing both 5-storey and 6-storey wood-frame buildings, so we are experts in the special design issues 
related to these structures. The Building Code prohibits shear wall transfers in wood-frame buildings over 
4-storeys, hence we recommend consulting with us early during initial schematic design, so that important 
shear wall elements can be integrated into the unit plans and overall building massing. 
 

 JIM Architecture. – 6530 Victoria Street, Vancouver, BC 
Kor Structural • Fee Proposal dated August 7, 2024 
Page 2 of 6 
 
Preliminary work and preliminary consultations with the Architect will be charged on an hourly basis in 
accordance with the included ‘Appendix A’ Schedule of Standard Hourly Billing Rates, however, please 
note that all charges for preliminary work are included in the proposed Professional Services Fees. Our 
fixed fee does include for attending site meetings; however, we are on site regularly once construction 
begins (inspecting rebar), so attending these meetings only when we are required is appreciated. 
 
Over and above the noted proposed fixed fees, we recommend a budget allowance of $1,000 for normal 
disbursements (e.g., courier costs), not including printing and plotting. 
 
Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be Kevin Wurmlinger, P.Eng. Struct.Eng., 
CEng, MIStructE. Kevin is a specialist Structural Engineer licensed in British Columbia with more than 20 
years of experience designing a wide variety of buildings and types, including tall towers, mixed-use 
commercial and residential projects, and office buildings, with expertise in concrete, steel, and timber. Kevin 
is involved in all stages of his projects from conceptual design through construction. He has extensive 
experience in structural design solutions, consultant team coordination, drawing preparation, site reviews, 
and construction administration, which has continuously led to the successful delivery of his projects. 
 
After the initial stages of design are complete, Kevin Wurmlinger will be assisted by senior partner, John 
Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng. Struct.Eng., PE, SE, who is a licensed Structural Engineer in British Columbia, 
Alberta, California, Washington, Arizona, and Texas, and has more than 30 years of experience designing 
a wide variety of buildings, including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light 
industrial warehouses, and institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care 
facilities, hotels, and office buildings. John Markulin is responsible for delivering innovative structural 
engineering solutions for some of the firm’s most notable projects. John is an accomplished engineer with 
significant project experience in the design of reinforced concrete, pre-cast concrete, cast-in-place 
concrete, post-tensioned concrete, tilt-up concrete, structural steel, load-bearing steel stud, wood-frame, 
and masonry, as well as floor systems, vertical load systems and seismic and lateral systems. 
 
Kevin Wurmlinger and John Markulin will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will 
include preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Both Kevin and John 
will be available and remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
