20564c3498db,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,13/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O] KOR.pdf,,5.1,Price,payment,167,"5.1 Price 
 
The Owner, in consideration of the Consultant’s full, complete and faithful performance of the Work and the 
Consultant’s full, complete and faithful performance of all of its obligations under this Agreement, agrees to 
pay to the Consultant, without duplication, the following fees (hereinafter collectively referred to as the 
“Price”): 
 
(a) 
$246,500.00, plus Sales Tax thereon of $12,325.00, for a total aggregate sum of $258,825.00, 
payable in monthly installments based on the applicable portion of the Work Completed; and 
 
(b) 
fees payable at the rates set out in Schedule “B” attached hereto for any work in addition to the 
Work (the “Additional Work”), payable in monthly installments based on the applicable portion of 
the Additional Work Completed. 
 
Invoices must be provided by the Consultant monthly, and payment shall be due after 60 days of the date 
of an undisputed invoice. Any Additional Work by the Consultant must have the prior written approval in the 
form of a purchase order or change order issued by the Owner."
20564c3498db,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,13/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O] KOR.pdf,,5.2,Completing the Work,termination|payment|permits_approvals|assignment_subconsultants,334,"5.2 Completing the Work 
 
(a) 
For the purpose of this Agreement, the Work shall only be deemed to have been Completed by the 
Consultant when, in addition to any other requirements set out in this Agreement or Applicable 
Laws or Applicable Authorities, the Consultant has submitted, or caused to be submitted as so 
directed by the Owner, to Applicable Authorities any and all required applications, documentation, 
forms, reports, studies and any and all other materials or revisions to such materials that are 
required by Applicable Authorities and Applicable Laws to the extent set out in Schedule “A”, all in 
accordance with specifications that have been recommended by the Consultant and the Service 
Providers and approved by the Owner. 
 
(b) 
If the Consultant is not proceeding to diligently perform any of the Work in accordance with, and as 
required by this Agreement and such failure continues to occur following 30 days’ prior written 
notice from Owner of such failure, the Owner shall have the right to perform, or cause to be 

 
- 7 - 
 
performed any of such Work through its own forces or otherwise using its own contractors or 
subcontractors or third-party Service Providers engaged by the Consultant. In addition, if the 
Consultant is not proceeding to diligently perform its Work herein and such failure continues to 
occur following 30 days’ prior written notice from Owner of such failure, this shall constitute a breach 
of this Agreement and an Event of Default whereby the Owner may terminate this Agreement in 
accordance with Section 7.2 hereunder. 
 
(c) 
Within 30 days of the Completion Date, the Consultant shall provide to the Owner a reconciliation 
to be approved by the Owner, acting reasonably, setting out the amount paid and payable under 
this Section 5.2 in respect of the Property and to the extent that there has been an overpayment 
on account of any of the Price, the Consultant shall within ten days of receipt of the approved 
reconciliation by the Owner repay such overpayment to the Owner."
20564c3498db,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,13/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O] KOR.pdf,,5.3,Expenses of the Consultant,insurance|permits_approvals,305,"5.3 Expenses of the Consultant 
 
The Consultant will bear all costs and expenses incurred by the Consultant, any Service Providers retained 
by the Consultant or on the Consultant’s behalf, and any other Person claiming under this Agreement in 
connection with the performance of the Work and its duties under this Agreement. Without limiting the 
generality of the foregoing, the Consultant shall pay the following expenses: 
 
(a) 
overhead: rent, telephone, utilities, office furniture, equipment and machines, other office expenses 
and all applicable taxes thereon of the Consultant used or incurred in the operation of its business; 
 
(b) 
personnel: all salaries, wages, benefits, bonus, severance, statutory deductions, and other costs 
of its employees, whether for the performance of its services hereunder or otherwise, including 
payments required by Applicable Laws including, but not limited to, Canada Pension Plan, 
employment insurance, Workplace Safety and Insurance Board, and Employer Health Tax 
contributions; 
 
(c) 
third party costs: fees and expenses payable to independent advisors and consultants employed 
or retained by the Consultant and including the legal, accounting, engineering, consultant and 
advisor fees in respect of and for the Consultant; 
 
(d) 
administrative costs: all administrative expenses of the Consultant necessary for the performance 
of its duties hereunder, including without limitation, Consultant’s insurance, licensing fees, 
subscription fees, and user fees related to its use of software and technology; 
 
(e) 
travel: all travel, lodging, and meals costs of the Consultant within the Greater Vancouver Area; 
and 
 
(f) 
other: other expenses that are customarily considered to be overhead expenses and including, for 
the avoidance of doubt, all income and other taxes payable by the Consultant for its own account 
and all Sales Tax payable on all foregoing amounts described above. 
 
The Consultant shall not incur any expenses whatsoever on behalf of the Owner without written 
authorization from the Owner’s designated representative. 
 
