20564c3498db,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,13/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O] KOR.pdf,,7.2,Termination of this Agreement,termination|dispute,267,"7.2 Termination of this Agreement 
 
(a) 
Notwithstanding anything herein to the contrary, the Owner may terminate this Agreement at no 
cost to the Owner by providing at least 30 days’ prior written notice to the Consultant and following 
such termination, the Owner shall have no liability to the Consultant except as set out in Section 
7.4 hereof. Any such termination shall not give rise to any Claim except as set out in this Section. 
 
(b) 
Upon an Event of Default of the Consultant pursuant to this Agreement that, if capable of being 
cured, is not cured within 15 days following written notice to the Consultant from the Owner 
specifying in reasonable detail the nature of the Event of Default, the Owner may terminate this 
Agreement without prejudice to its rights to pursue all legal and equitable remedies. 
 
(c) 
In the event that the Owner sells the Property, the Owner may terminate this Agreement by 
providing written notice to the Consultant of such termination which notice shall state the effective 
date of such termination, which effective date may be immediately upon delivery of the notice or 
thereafter. 
 
(d) 
Upon material default by the Owner pursuant to this Agreement that, if capable of being cured, is 
not cured within 15 days following written notice to the Owner from the Consultant specifying in 
reasonable detail the nature of the default, the Consultant may terminate this Agreement without 
prejudice to its rights to pursue all legal and equitable remedies, provided that such termination 
shall not prejudice or terminate the license granted to the Owner pursuant to Section 9.3 of this 
Agreement."
20564c3498db,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,13/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O] KOR.pdf,,7.3,Suspension of Work,termination|suspension|dispute,192,"7.3 Suspension of Work 
 
The Owner may direct the Consultant to stop all or any portion of the Work by giving the Consultant written 
notice, which shall specify the estimated period during which the Work is to be stopped. The Consultant 
shall resume Work upon the date specified in such notice, or upon such other date as the Owner may 
thereafter specify. Suspension or stoppage of Work under this Section shall not give rise to any Claim 
against the Owner or any other fees being due and payable by the Owner to the Consultant, except that 
the Owner shall be liable to the Consultant for: (a) Work Completed prior to the date of such stoppage; and 
(b) reasonable out-of-pocket costs incurred by the Consultant to recommence the Work. The Consultant 
shall not be entitled to any portion of the Price or any other fees in respect of Work performed during the 

 
- 9 - 
 
period during which the Consultant’s Work is suspended. If the Work is suspended for a period of more 
than 60 days, then the Consultant shall have the right to terminate this Agreement immediately upon written 
notice to Owner."
