THIS SERVICES AGREEMENT (the “Agreement”) is made as of January 19, 2026, and effective as of November 26, 2025.

B E T W E E N:
IMH 7360-7376 HALIFAX APARTMENTS LTD. 

(hereinafter called the “Owner”)

- and -

KOR STRUCTURAL

(hereinafter called the “Consultant”)
WHEREAS:

The Owner is the registered owner of the property municipally known as 7360 Halifax Street, Burnaby, British Columbia V5A 1M4 and 7376 Halifax Street, Burnaby, British Columbia V5A 1M5, (the “Property”); and

The Consultant is desirous of performing certain structural engineering services in connection with the Property in accordance with certain requirements and specifications including those described in Schedule “A” attached hereto, and the Owner is desirous of retaining the Consultant, as an independent contractor, to perform such work, all in accordance with the terms and conditions set out in this Agreement.

NOW THEREFORE, in consideration for the respective covenants and agreements of the parties contained herein and other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which is hereby acknowledged by the parties, the parties agree as follows:

DEFINITIONS

Definitions

The terms defined in this Section 1.1 whenever used in this Agreement shall, unless the context otherwise requires, have the respective meanings as hereinafter provided:

“Additional Work” has the meaning set out in Section 5.1;

“Affiliate” of “Affiliates” means, with respect to any Person, any Person or group of Persons directly or indirectly Controlling, Controlled by or under common Control with, such Person;

“Agreement” means this Agreement and includes the following schedules:
Schedule “A” – The Work
Schedule “B” – Additional Work Fees;

“Applicable Authorities” means any and all applicable federal, provincial, municipal, regional or local body, agency, entity, authority or otherwise, whether public, governmental, quasi-governmental, regulatory or otherwise, having jurisdiction, as the case may be in accordance with Applicable Laws;"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p4,"if the Consultant is a corporation, it is not duly organized, validly existing and in good standing under the laws of the jurisdiction of its formation;",dispute|schedule_delay,346,"if the Consultant is a corporation, it is not duly organized, validly existing and in good standing under the laws of the jurisdiction of its formation;
the dissolution, liquidation, bankruptcy, insolvency or winding-up of the Consultant; or
if the Consultant or any Person acting on its behalf are required to be licensed or certified to provide any of the Work herein, the required license or certification is not in good standing.
“Force Majeure” shall mean any event or cause (other than financial inability of the party to whom such event occurs) which is beyond the control of a party and which prevents or delays the performance by such party of any obligation hereunder other than the payment of money or funding of costs, including labor strikes, acts of God, governmental restrictions, health emergencies including a pandemic or epidemic, enemy action, civil commotion, fire, unavoidable casualty, unusual delays in transportation, adverse weather conditions not reasonably capable of being anticipated, power outages, acts of terrorism, or other similar causes;

“Notice” has the meaning set out in Section 10.3;

“Person” or “Persons” includes any individual, firm, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability partnership, joint venture, fund, limited liability company, unlimited liability company, association, trust, trustee, executor, administrator, legal personal representative, estate, group, body corporate, trust, unincorporated association or organization, governmental authority, syndicate or other entity, whether or not having legal status, however designated or constituted;

“Price” shall mean the fees payable by the Owner to the Consultant pursuant to Section 5.1 of this Agreement;

“Records” has the meaning set out in Section 3.3;

“Sales Tax” has the meaning set out in Section 6.1(a);

“Schedule” has the meaning set out in Section 3.4;

“Service Providers” shall mean the following Persons as may be selected and engaged by the Consultant, at the Consultant’s sole cost and expense, from time to time: (i) licensed professionals, qualified to practice in British Columbia; and (ii) such other consultants, contractors, employees and/or others that may be selected and engaged by the Consultant from time to time, and “Service Provider” shall mean any of the Service Providers;"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p5,“Standard of Care” has the meaning set out in Section 2.2;,standard_of_care,231,"“Standard of Care” has the meaning set out in Section 2.2;

“Term” has the meaning set out in Section 7.1; and

“Work” has the meaning set out in Section 2.1(a).

CONSULTANT FUNCTIONS
Functions

The Owner hereby engages the Consultant, and the Consultant hereby agrees to act, as an independent contractor of the Owner to Complete the work described in this Agreement for the Property (hereinafter collectively referred to as the “Work”) during the Term, subject to the terms, conditions and limitations set out in this Agreement. The Consultant is, and shall be, acting as an independent contractor and not as an employee, agent, partner, joint venturer, or dependent contractor of the Owner.

The Consultant agrees to perform during the Term, directly or indirectly, the Completion of all Work in accordance with this Agreement, and all matters in relation thereto, including but not limited to the following functions:

coordinate, supervise, and manage the planning for the Work;

arrange for, and supervise each Service Provider’s performance of any function relating to the Work;

review all material prepared and submitted by Service Providers;

prepare or cause to be prepared applications or submissions to the Applicable Authorities (with the cooperation of the Owner), as set out in Schedule “A”; and

keep the Owner appraised of all important communications with any Applicable Authorities in the course of the Work.

In providing its services, the Consultant shall:"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p6,"supply all labour, material, equipment and tools necessary to Complete all of the Work;",standard_of_care|schedule_delay,300,"supply all labour, material, equipment and tools necessary to Complete all of the Work;
exercise its own judgement and control in the performance of the Work;
devote sufficient time to Complete all of the Work in accordance with the Approved Schedule (subject to delays due to Force Majeure); 
control its work hours and place in performing the Work;
use its commercially reasonable best efforts to expedite the Completion of all of the Work, and to protect the Owner against unnecessary extra costs and expenses. 
The Owner reserves the right to assess the Work and achievement of the results resulting therefrom. Without derogating from the Owner’s rights under Section 7.2(b) herein, the Owner may, at any time during the course of the Work and acting reasonably, request the replacement of any Persons that are performing the Work in a manner inconsistent with the terms and conditions of this Agreement, including the Standard of Care, and promptly upon receipt of such request, the Consultant shall make arrangements to select and appoint a replacement acceptable to the Owner, acting reasonably. 
Consultant Conduct and Standard of Care

The Consultant covenants that it will exercise its powers and discharge its duties under this Agreement competently, honestly, expeditiously, diligently, with due care, in good faith, and that it will exercise the care and skill that a Person duly qualified to perform the Work would exercise under similar conditions in accordance with accepted industry best practices given the project complexity and the nature and character of the Property (the “Standard of Care”). 

IMPLEMENTATION
Cooperation of the Owner 

Upon request by the Consultant, the Owner shall furnish the Consultant with information and documents reasonably available to the Owner and required by the Consultant to fulfill its obligations in connection with this Agreement. 

Consultant No Power to Bind Owner"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p7,"Notwithstanding Section 2.1(c)(ii), nothing in this Agreement shall be construed so as to authorize the Consultant to make any decision or take any action which",termination|warranty_reperform,243,"Notwithstanding Section 2.1(c)(ii), nothing in this Agreement shall be construed so as to authorize the Consultant to make any decision or take any action which contravenes or is inconsistent with the Owner’s approved instructions, or which requires, and has not been given, authorization, and unless the contrary is expressly provided, no such decision or action shall be taken or made with respect thereof until such authorization in accordance with this Agreement has been obtained. The Consultant shall not bind the Owner or any of its Affiliates or partners to any contract, obligation, agreement, or make warranties or representations on behalf of the Owner, of any kind whatsoever, unless it is approved in advance in writing by the Owner or is otherwise provided for herein. 

Consultant Information, Advice and Reporting

During the Term, the Consultant will provide the Owner with all such information and advice as the Owner reasonably require from time to time for the purpose of assessing the progress or status of the various components of the Work. 

Promptly following completion of the Work or the earlier expiration or termination of this Agreement, the Consultant shall provide to the Owner record drawings, CAD files, PDFs, and editable BIM models showing the Work (collectively, the “Records”). The Consultant shall not be required to provide original copies of the Records. 

Upon the Owner’s request from time to time, the Consultant shall provide copies of any correspondence pertaining to the Work or this Agreement.

 Schedules"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p9,The Consultant will act in accordance the Standard of Care in seeking that all aspects of the work will comply with all Applicable Laws and that the Consultant ,indemnity|payment|standard_of_care|permits_approvals|lien,302,"The Consultant will act in accordance the Standard of Care in seeking that all aspects of the work will comply with all Applicable Laws and that the Consultant shall also comply with all Applicable Laws affecting the Property.

No Liens
Provided the Owner pays all amounts to the Consultant as required under this Agreement as and when due, the Consultant shall ensure that neither it nor any Service Provider retained by or on behalf of the Consultant register a lien (or give a written notice of lien), encumbrance, charge or caveat (collectively, a “Lien”) for work, labour, services or materials against the Property. The Consultant shall defend, release, indemnify, save and hold harmless the Owner in any and all actions or legal proceedings commenced against the Owner in relation to such a Lien.

Consultant COMPENSATION

Price

The Owner, in consideration of the Consultant’s full, complete and faithful performance of the Work and the Consultant’s full, complete and faithful performance of all of its obligations under this Agreement, agrees to pay to the Consultant, without duplication, the following fees (hereinafter collectively referred to as the “Price”):

$246,500.00, plus Sales Tax thereon of $12,325.00, for a total aggregate sum of $258,825.00, payable in monthly installments based on the applicable portion of the Work Completed; and

fees payable at the rates set out in Schedule “B” attached hereto for any work in addition to the Work (the “Additional Work”), payable in monthly installments based on the applicable portion of the Additional Work Completed.

Invoices must be provided by the Consultant monthly, and payment shall be due after 60 days of the date of an undisputed invoice. Any Additional Work by the Consultant must have the prior written approval in the form of a purchase order or change order issued by the Owner. 

Completing the Work"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p10,"For the purpose of this Agreement, the Work shall only be deemed to have been Completed by the Consultant when, in addition to any other requirements set out in",termination|payment|permits_approvals|assignment_subconsultants,328,"For the purpose of this Agreement, the Work shall only be deemed to have been Completed by the Consultant when, in addition to any other requirements set out in this Agreement or Applicable Laws or Applicable Authorities, the Consultant has submitted, or caused to be submitted as so directed by the Owner, to Applicable Authorities any and all required applications, documentation, forms, reports, studies and any and all other materials or revisions to such materials that are required by Applicable Authorities and Applicable Laws to the extent set out in Schedule “A”, all in accordance with specifications that have been recommended by the Consultant and the Service Providers and approved by the Owner.

If the Consultant is not proceeding to diligently perform any of the Work in accordance with, and as required by this Agreement and such failure continues to occur following 30 days’ prior written notice from Owner of such failure, the Owner shall have the right to perform, or cause to be performed any of such Work through its own forces or otherwise using its own contractors or subcontractors or third-party Service Providers engaged by the Consultant. In addition, if the Consultant is not proceeding to diligently perform its Work herein and such failure continues to occur following 30 days’ prior written notice from Owner of such failure, this shall constitute a breach of this Agreement and an Event of Default whereby the Owner may terminate this Agreement in accordance with Section 7.2 hereunder. 

Within 30 days of the Completion Date, the Consultant shall provide to the Owner a reconciliation to be approved by the Owner, acting reasonably, setting out the amount paid and payable under this Section 5.2 in respect of the Property and to the extent that there has been an overpayment on account of any of the Price, the Consultant shall within ten days of receipt of the approved reconciliation by the Owner repay such overpayment to the Owner. 

Expenses of the Consultant"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p11,"The Consultant will bear all costs and expenses incurred by the Consultant, any Service Providers retained by the Consultant or on the Consultant’s behalf, and ",insurance|permits_approvals,294,"The Consultant will bear all costs and expenses incurred by the Consultant, any Service Providers retained by the Consultant or on the Consultant’s behalf, and any other Person claiming under this Agreement in connection with the performance of the Work and its duties under this Agreement. Without limiting the generality of the foregoing, the Consultant shall pay the following expenses: 

overhead: rent, telephone, utilities, office furniture, equipment and machines, other office expenses and all applicable taxes thereon of the Consultant used or incurred in the operation of its business;

personnel: all salaries, wages, benefits, bonus, severance, statutory deductions, and other costs of its employees, whether for the performance of its services hereunder or otherwise, including payments required by Applicable Laws including, but not limited to, Canada Pension Plan, employment insurance, Workplace Safety and Insurance Board, and Employer Health Tax contributions;

third party costs: fees and expenses payable to independent advisors and consultants employed or retained by the Consultant and including the legal, accounting, engineering, consultant and advisor fees in respect of and for the Consultant;

administrative costs: all administrative expenses of the Consultant necessary for the performance of its duties hereunder, including without limitation, Consultant’s insurance, licensing fees, subscription fees, and user fees related to its use of software and technology;

travel: all travel, lodging, and meals costs of the Consultant within the Greater Vancouver Area; and 

other: other expenses that are customarily considered to be overhead expenses and including, for the avoidance of doubt, all income and other taxes payable by the Consultant for its own account and all Sales Tax payable on all foregoing amounts described above.

The Consultant shall not incur any expenses whatsoever on behalf of the Owner without written authorization from the Owner’s designated representative.

SALES TAXES

Sales Tax"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p12,"The Consultant represents, warrants and agrees that it is registered under Part IX of the Excise Tax Act (Canada) for the collection and remittance of Canada’s ",indemnity|termination|payment|warranty_reperform,326,"The Consultant represents, warrants and agrees that it is registered under Part IX of the Excise Tax Act (Canada) for the collection and remittance of Canada’s Goods and Services Tax (“GST”) and any Harmonized Sales Tax (“HST”) or any other provincial sales taxes applicable to any services performed by the Consultant hereunder (collectively, “Sales Tax”), and that it will remain registered for Sales Tax during the Term of this Agreement or shall otherwise notify the Owner should its status change.

Unless stated otherwise, the amounts payable by the Owner to the Consultant pursuant to this Agreement do not include any Sales Tax. The Consultant is responsible to determine whether it has the obligation to be registered and if tax is applicable under this Agreement. To the extent Sales Tax is payable by the Owner, the Consultant shall collect the relevant taxes from the Owner at the time the Consultant issues its invoice for the consideration payable and shall separately disclose the amount of Sales Tax that is being collected on the invoice. The Consultant shall remit any Sales Tax that it has collected from the Owner to the relevant tax authorities and shall defend, indemnify and save harmless the Owner in respect of any amounts, demands or Claim owing or which may become owing in respect of any such taxes. 

TERM; TERMINATION
Term

Subject to the following provisions of this Article 7, this Agreement shall continue in full force and effect from the date hereof until the Completion Date for the Work (the “Term”). 

Termination of this Agreement

Notwithstanding anything herein to the contrary, the Owner may terminate this Agreement at no cost to the Owner by providing at least 30 days’ prior written notice to the Consultant and following such termination, the Owner shall have no liability to the Consultant except as set out in Section 7.4 hereof. Any such termination shall not give rise to any Claim except as set out in this Section."
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p13,"Upon an Event of Default of the Consultant pursuant to this Agreement that, if capable of being cured, is not cured within 15 days following written notice to t",termination|suspension|dispute,193,"Upon an Event of Default of the Consultant pursuant to this Agreement that, if capable of being cured, is not cured within 15 days following written notice to the Consultant from the Owner specifying in reasonable detail the nature of the Event of Default, the Owner may terminate this Agreement without prejudice to its rights to pursue all legal and equitable remedies.

In the event that the Owner sells the Property, the Owner may terminate this Agreement by providing written notice to the Consultant of such termination which notice shall state the effective date of such termination, which effective date may be immediately upon delivery of the notice or thereafter. 

Upon material default by the Owner pursuant to this Agreement that, if capable of being cured, is not cured within 15 days following written notice to the Owner from the Consultant specifying in reasonable detail the nature of the default, the Consultant may terminate this Agreement without prejudice to its rights to pursue all legal and equitable remedies, provided that such termination shall not prejudice or terminate the license granted to the Owner pursuant to Section 9.3 of this Agreement.

Suspension of Work"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p14,"The Owner may direct the Consultant to stop all or any portion of the Work by giving the Consultant written notice, which shall specify the estimated period dur",termination|suspension|payment|dispute,310,"The Owner may direct the Consultant to stop all or any portion of the Work by giving the Consultant written notice, which shall specify the estimated period during which the Work is to be stopped. The Consultant shall resume Work upon the date specified in such notice, or upon such other date as the Owner may thereafter specify. Suspension or stoppage of Work under this Section shall not give rise to any Claim against the Owner or any other fees being due and payable by the Owner to the Consultant, except that the Owner shall be liable to the Consultant for: (a) Work Completed prior to the date of such stoppage; and (b) reasonable out-of-pocket costs incurred by the Consultant to recommence the Work. The Consultant shall not be entitled to any portion of the Price or any other fees in respect of Work performed during the period during which the Consultant’s Work is suspended. If the Work is suspended for a period of more than 60 days, then the Consultant shall have the right to terminate this Agreement immediately upon written notice to Owner. 

Remedies of the Owner

If this Agreement shall terminate, the Consultant shall not have any right to payment of the Price or any other fees other than as set out below; provided, however, that the Consultant is in compliance with Section 7.5 hereof: 

if applicable Work is Completed as of the date of termination and not yet paid by the Owner, the Consultant shall have the right to payment for a portion of the Price equivalent to the reasonable value of the Work Completed prior to the date of termination, provided that an invoice shall be delivered to the Owner within 30 days of the date of termination and such payment shall be due after 60 days of the date of an undisputed invoice; and"
7ef012a89375,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,14/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,,0p15,"if applicable Work is not Completed as of the date of termination, the Consultant is entitled to receive compensation in connection with its work-in-progress ac",insurance|termination|payment|confidentiality,346,"if applicable Work is not Completed as of the date of termination, the Consultant is entitled to receive compensation in connection with its work-in-progress accrued prior to the date of termination for its reasonable time for such incomplete Work in accordance with the rates set out in Schedule “B” attached hereto, such compensation being subject to the written approval of the Owner, acting reasonably, provided that an invoice shall be delivered to the Owner within 30 days of the date of termination and such payment shall be due after 60 days of the date of an undisputed invoice.

Actions Upon Termination and Expiration

Within 30 calendar days after expiration or earlier termination of this Agreement, the Consultant shall promptly deliver to the Owner or to such other Person as the Owner shall designate in writing, the Records, and any property belonging to the Owner, whether in possession of the Consultant or a Person engaged or employed by the Consultant. The Consultant shall cooperate with the Owner as the Owner shall reasonably require in order to effectuate an orderly and systematic termination of the Consultant’s duties and activities, as applicable, including without limitation at the Owner’s request, destroying or causing to destroy all Confidential Information in the possession or control of the Consultant or its Service Providers. The Consultant shall not be required to provide original copies of the Records.

Rights on Termination

Any termination of this Agreement shall terminate all of the rights and obligations of the parties under this Agreement, except as otherwise provided herein or as stated to survive the termination of this Agreement, and further except for all rights and obligations with respect to fees and other amounts owing up until termination or with respect to remedies, as applicable. 

INSURANCE AND INDEMNITY

Insurance Coverage

The Consultant and each of the Service Providers shall, at its own expense obtain, maintain and keep in force during the Term, insurance policies with insurers acceptable to the Owner, as specified below, each having limits, unless otherwise agreed to or set out below, of not less than $5,000,000.00:"
