Amount of Damages
To the maximum extent permitted under applicable law, the cumulative liability of either party arising out of or in any way connected to this Agreement shall be limited as follows:

with respect to Claims for which insurance is to be provided, the insurance limits required pursuant to Section 8.1 hereof; and

with respect to Claims for which insurance is not required and/or does not apply pursuant to Section 8.1 hereof, the lesser of two times the Price and $500,000.00.

The existence of one or more claims under this Agreement will not increase a party’s liability in excess of the foregoing.

LAWS

Governing Law

This Agreement shall be construed and the legal relationship between the parties shall be governed by the laws of the Province of British Columbia and the federal laws of Canada applicable therein. 

Health & Safety Conditions

The Consultant acknowledges having read the measures and procedures relating to occupational and workplace health and safety as prescribed by Applicable Laws. The Consultant acknowledges and understands its duties as set out therein and hereby expressly agrees to comply with all such requirements and standards in their entirety and at its sole expense unless stated otherwise herein or otherwise agreed by the parties hereto in advance in writing. In addition, the Consultant agrees to fully co-operate with all health and safety programs, rules, regulations, standards and criteria set or instituted by the Owner as set out in the Starlight Vendor Policy or referenced herein, which agreement may be in furtherance of those under Applicable Laws."
