0fd227b54a3c,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,15/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].pdf,,2.1,Functions,standard_of_care|schedule_delay,394,"2.1 Functions 
 
(a) 
The Owner hereby engages the Consultant, and the Consultant hereby agrees to act, as an 
independent contractor of the Owner to Complete the work described in this Agreement for the 
Property (hereinafter collectively referred to as the “Work”) during the Term, subject to the terms, 
conditions and limitations set out in this Agreement. The Consultant is, and shall be, acting as an 

 
- 4 - 
 
independent contractor and not as an employee, agent, partner, joint venturer, or dependent 
contractor of the Owner. 
 
(b) 
The Consultant agrees to perform during the Term, directly or indirectly, the Completion of all Work 
in accordance with this Agreement, and all matters in relation thereto, including but not limited to 
the following functions: 
 
(i) 
coordinate, supervise, and manage the planning for the Work; 
 
(ii) 
arrange for, and supervise each Service Provider’s performance of any function relating to 
the Work; 
 
(iii) 
review all material prepared and submitted by Service Providers; 
 
(iv) 
prepare or cause to be prepared applications or submissions to the Applicable Authorities 
(with the cooperation of the Owner), as set out in Schedule “A”; and 
 
(v) 
keep the Owner appraised of all important communications with any Applicable Authorities 
in the course of the Work. 
 
(c) 
In providing its services, the Consultant shall: 
 
(i) 
supply all labour, material, equipment and tools necessary to Complete all of the Work; 
(ii) 
exercise its own judgement and control in the performance of the Work; 
(iii) 
devote sufficient time to Complete all of the Work in accordance with the Approved 
Schedule (subject to delays due to Force Majeure); 
(iv) 
control its work hours and place in performing the Work; 
(v) 
use its commercially reasonable best efforts to expedite the Completion of all of the Work, 
and to protect the Owner against unnecessary extra costs and expenses. 
(d) 
The Owner reserves the right to assess the Work and achievement of the results resulting 
therefrom. Without derogating from the Owner’s rights under Section 7.2(b) herein, the Owner may, 
at any time during the course of the Work and acting reasonably, request the replacement of any 
Persons that are performing the Work in a manner inconsistent with the terms and conditions of 
this Agreement, including the Standard of Care, and promptly upon receipt of such request, the 
Consultant shall make arrangements to select and appoint a replacement acceptable to the Owner, 
acting reasonably."
