The Consultant acknowledges, confirms and agrees that the Owner reserves all right, title, and interests in 
and to all rights, including, without limitation, copyrights, patents, trade secret rights, and other intellectual 
property rights associated with any designs, drawings, specifications, documents, reports, ideas, concepts, 
techniques, inventions, processes, works of authorship, Confidential Information, or trade secrets 
developed or created by the Consultant, solely or jointly with others, during the course of performing Work 
or directly and indirectly in relation to this Agreement. 
 
Notwithstanding the foregoing paragraph, the Consultant shall retain copyright in representations, in any 
medium of expression, of the tangible and intangible creative work that forms part of the Work (the 
“Instrument”); however, the Owner shall have a complete and unconditional license to use the Instrument 
in perpetuity in the Owner’s sole discretion, including making copies of and amending same, without 
compensation to the Consultant beyond that expressly provided for in this Agreement for the Work as it 
pertains to this Instrument. The Consultant shall ensure that its agreements with its consultants and other 
third parties contain a similar provision in order to ensure that the Owner has a license in respect of the 
Instrument as described herein. For greater certainty, the license shall continue in the event that this 
Agreement is terminated for any reason. The Consultant grants to the Owner a non-exclusive, transferable, 
irrevocable, royalty-free, perpetual license to use the Instrument. The Consultant represents, warrants and 
covenants that this license does not infringe on the rights of any third party. The Consultant may rescind 
the license only if the Owner has failed to make payment for the Work relating to this Instrument when due. 
If the Consultant elects to rescind the license it must first provide written notice to the Owner. 
Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in this paragraph, if: 
 
(i) there is an unsettled dispute regarding the Owner’s unpaid invoice for the Work as it relates to this 
Instrument; or 
 
(ii) the Owner responds to the Consultant’s notice to rescind the license within 30 business days with 
a notification of dispute, 
 
then the Consultant’s right to revoke the Owner’s license will be delayed until the dispute is settled. 
 
