(a) 
The Consultant represents, warrants and agrees that it is registered under Part IX of the Excise 
Tax Act (Canada) for the collection and remittance of Canada’s Goods and Services Tax (“GST”) 
and any Harmonized Sales Tax (“HST”) or any other provincial sales taxes applicable to any 
services performed by the Consultant hereunder (collectively, “Sales Tax”), and that it will remain 
registered for Sales Tax during the Term of this Agreement or shall otherwise notify the Owner 
should its status change. 
 
(b) 
Unless stated otherwise, the amounts payable by the Owner to the Consultant pursuant to this 
Agreement do not include any Sales Tax. The Consultant is responsible to determine whether it 
has the obligation to be registered and if tax is applicable under this Agreement. To the extent 
Sales Tax is payable by the Owner, the Consultant shall collect the relevant taxes from the Owner 
at the time the Consultant issues its invoice for the consideration payable and shall separately 
disclose the amount of Sales Tax that is being collected on the invoice. The Consultant shall remit 
any Sales Tax that it has collected from the Owner to the relevant tax authorities and shall defend, 
indemnify and save harmless the Owner in respect of any amounts, demands or Claim owing or 
which may become owing in respect of any such taxes. 
 
