bc5594c95512,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,2/21,,2025-05-27,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\7360-7376 Halifax Street (Burnaby, BC) - Kor Structural - Service Agreement v2 KOR.pdf",,8.1,Insurance Coverage,insurance|termination|confidentiality,603,"8.1 Insurance Coverage 
 

 
- 10 - 
 
The Consultant and each of the Service Providers shall, at its own expense obtain, maintain and keep in 
force during the Term, insurance policies with insurers acceptable to the Owner, as specified below, each 
having limits, unless otherwise agreed to or set out below, of not less than $5,000,000.00: 
 
(a) 
comprehensive general liability insurance against claims for personal injury, death or property 
damage arising out the business carried on by the Consultant (or Service Providers) and the Work; 
 
(b) 
network security/privacy liability/cyber liability insurance in an amount not less than $2,000,000.00 
per claim, including but not limited to: protection of confidential information; network security and 
privacy liability; protection against liability for systems attacks, denial or loss of service, introduction, 
implantation or spread of malicious code; and protection against liability for security breach, 
unauthorized access and use of data, which coverage shall be in place for the Term as well as for 
an additional two (2) year time period following the expiration or the Term or earlier termination of 
this Agreement by way of annual policy renewal, or purchase of extended reporting period 
coverage; 
 
(c) 
automobile liability insurance from the date of the commencement of the Work until a period of not 
less than one (1) year thereafter; and 
 
(d) 
should the Work involve professional design, professional liability insurance in an amount not less 
than $2,000,000 per claim, covering errors, omissions, or negligent acts in the performance of the 
professional services, from the commencement of the Work until a period of not less than two (2) 
years thereafter. 
 
Such policies of insurance shall: 
 
(e) 
name the Owner, the then property manager of the Property, Starlight Investments CDN AM Group 
LP, Starlight Investments CDN AM Group Inc., Starlight Group Property Holdings Inc. and the 
beneficial owner of the Property and, if requested, all Affiliates and their directors, trustees, officers, 
employees, agents, and mortgagees as additional insureds, with respect to the Consultant’s 
fulfillment of its duties and obligations hereunder (except for professional liability insurance or 
automobile liability insurance);; 
 
(f) 
contain a severability of interest, cross liability, and blanket contractual liability clause; 
 
(g) 
be non-contributing with, and shall apply only as primary and not excess to any other insurance 
available to the additional insureds; 
 
(h) 
provide that it shall not be cancelled, or its coverage reduced, except upon 30 days prior notice (by 
registered mail) to the Owner; and 
 
(i) 
include a waiver of subrogation rights which the insurer might otherwise have against the Owner, 
the then property manager of the Property, Starlight Investments CDN AM Group LP, Starlight 
Investments CDN AM Group Inc., Starlight Group Property Holdings Inc. and the beneficial owner 
of the Property and any Affiliate, or its directors, trustees, officers, employees, agents, mortgages, 
or other Persons for whom at law it may be responsible. 
 
The Consultant shall furnish suitable evidence that such insurance has been obtained and is good standing 
prior to the commencement and for the duration of the Term and thereafter as required. 
 
If the Consultant fails to place or maintain all or any of the insurance coverage referred in this Section 8.1, 
the Owner on its behalf may, but shall not be obligated to, in addition to any remedies that may be available 
to it, place all or part of such insurance in the name of or on behalf of the Consultant and the Consultant 
shall pay, forthwith on demand, all costs and expenses incurred in so doing, including without limitation the 
premium(s) for such insurance together with an administrative fee equal to twenty percent (20%) of such 
costs and expenses. 

 
