The terms defined in this Section 1.1 whenever used in this Agreement shall, unless the context otherwise 
requires, have the respective meanings as hereinafter provided: 
 
(a) 
“Additional Work” has the meaning set out in Section 5.1; 
 
(b) 
“Affiliate” of “Affiliates” means, with respect to any Person, any Person or group of Persons 
directly or indirectly Controlling, Controlled by or under common Control with, such Person; 
 
(c) 
“Agreement” means this Agreement and includes the following schedules: 
Schedule “A” – The Work and Price 
Schedule “B” – Additional Work Fees; 
 
(d) 
“Applicable Authorities” means any and all applicable federal, provincial, municipal, regional or 
local body, agency, entity, authority or otherwise, whether public, governmental, quasi-
governmental, regulatory or otherwise, having jurisdiction, as the case may be in accordance with 
Applicable Laws; 
 
(e) 
“Applicable Laws” means, in respect of any Person, all laws, statutes, regulations, statutory rules, 
principles of common law or equity, orders and terms and conditions of any grant of approval, 
permission, authority or license of any Applicable Authorities applicable to such Person or its 

 
- 2 - 
 
business, undertaking and property having jurisdiction over the Person or its business, undertaking 
or property, in each case as amended from time to time; 
 
(f) 
“Approved Schedule” has the meaning set out in Section 3.4; 
 
(g) 
“Business Day” means any day other than a Saturday, Sunday or statutory holiday in the Province 
of British Columbia and the Province of Ontario. 
 
(h) 
 “Claim” means all past, present and future claims, actions, causes of action, suits, proceedings, 
liabilities, debts, obligations, losses, damages, penalties, judgments, costs, expenses, fines, 
disbursements, interest, payments, legal, consulting and other professional fees and 
disbursements fees on a substantial indemnity basis, and any other professional fees and 
disbursements, interest, demands and actions of any nature or kind whatsoever and howsoever 
arising, contingent or otherwise, whether liquidated or unliquidated, matured or unmatured, 
disputed or undisputed, contractual, legal or equitable, including without limitation, all costs incurred 
in investigating or pursuing any of the foregoing or any proceeding relating to any of the foregoing 
or any settlement of any of the foregoing, and all amounts paid to settle any of the foregoing or to 
satisfy a judgment; 
 
(i) 
“Complete” or “Completed” or “Completion” or “Completing” means, with respect to the Work 
and in addition to any other requirements set out in this Agreement including as set out in Section 
5.2(a) hereof, the completion of the applicable portion of the work, services, or otherwise required 
under Schedule “A” attached hereto for the Property, such Work having been fully performed in 
accordance with all Applicable Laws, and the requirements of all Applicable Authorities and this 
Agreement, and any and all deficiencies relating thereto have been rectified, all to the Owner’s 
satisfaction, acting reasonably; 
 
(j) 
“Completion Date” shall mean the date upon which all Work required under this Agreement for the 
Property has been Completed; 
 
(k) 
“Confidential Information” means: (i) information relating to the Owner or the Work that is not 
generally known to the public (including but not limited to information relating to products or 
services, pricing structures, accounting and business methods, methods and processes, customers 
and clients and customer or client lists, copyrightable works and all technology, trade secrets and 
other proprietary information); (ii) information the disclosure of which the Owner in good faith 
believes is not in the best interests of the Owner or the Work; and (iii) any other information which 
the Owner or the Consultant is required by Applicable Laws or agreement to keep confidential; 
 
(l) 
“Control,” “Controlled,” or “Controlling” means: 
 
(i) 
in relation to a Person that is a corporation, the ownership, directly or indirectly, of voting 
securities of the Person carrying more than fifty percent (50%) of the voting rights attaching 
to all voting shares of the Person and which are sufficient, if exercised, to elect a majority 
of its board of directors; 
 
(ii) 
in relation to a Person that is a limited partnership or trust, respectively, the general partner 
or trustee(s) or Person entitled to elect the trustee or more than fifty percent (50%) of the 
trustees, if applicable, of such Person, if any, or the ownership, directly or indirectly, of 
voting securities or rights of such Person carrying more than fifty percent (50%) of the 
voting rights attaching to all voting securities of the Person; and 
 
(iii) 
in relation to any Person, the ownership, directly or indirectly, of securities or other interests 
or rights entitling the holder(s) thereof to exercise direction over the activities of the Person; 
 
(m) 
“Event of Default” means any one or more of the following: 
 

 
- 3 - 
 
(i) 
the Consultant’s wilful misconduct, bad faith, gross negligence, breach of Applicable Laws, 
breach of the Standard of Care, or breach of this Agreement; 
 
(ii) 
if the Consultant is a corporation, it is not duly organized, validly existing and in good 
standing under the laws of the jurisdiction of its formation; 
(iii) 
the dissolution, liquidation, bankruptcy, insolvency or winding-up of the Consultant; or 
(iv) 
if the Consultant or any Person acting on its behalf are required to be licensed or certified 
to provide any of the Work herein, the required license or certification is not in good 
standing. 
(n) 
“Force Majeure” shall mean any event or cause (other than financial inability of the party to whom 
