not cured within 15 days following written notice to the Owner from the Consultant specifying in
reasonable detail the nature of the default, the Consultant may terminate this Agreement without
prejudice to its rights to pursue all legal and equitable remedies, provided that such termination
shall not prejudice or terminate the license granted to the Owner pursuant to Section 9.3 of this
Agreement."
1a525f7a0486,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,markup,16/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\CMP - 2026.01.05 - Service Agreement [C] and 2026.01.19 - Service Agreement.pdf,,7.3,Suspension of Work,termination|suspension|dispute,225,"7.3 Suspension of Work
The Owner may direct the Consultant to stop all or any portion of the Work by giving the Consultant
written notice, which shall specify the estimated period during which the Work is to be stopped. The
Consultant shall resume Work upon the date specified in such notice, or upon such other date as the
Owner may thereafter specify. Suspension or stoppage of Work under this Section shall not give rise to
any Claim against the Owner or any other fees being due and payable by the Owner to the Consultant,
except that the Owner shall be liable to the Consultant for: (a) Work Completed prior to the date of such
stoppage; and (b) reasonable out-of-pocket costs incurred by the Consultant to recommence the Work.
The Consultant shall not be entitled to any portion of the Price or any other fees incurred duringthein
respect of Work performed during the period during which the Consultant’s Work is suspended. If the
suspension is longer than 30 days, the consultant is entitled to submit a revised fee proposal to the owner
