The Consultant shall keep and cause to keep confidential and not disclose any Confidential Information regarding the Owner, the Property or the Work in its possession or control except to the extent: (i) disclosure of such Confidential Information is required by Applicable Laws; (ii) the Confidential Information was previously known to the Consultant; (iii) the Confidential Information is or was publicly known except through the actions or inactions of the Consultant; (iv) the Confidential Information is received by the Consultant from a third party without a breach of its obligations of confidentiality; or (v) the Confidential Information is independently developed by the Consultant without use of or reference to the Confidential Information, as shown by documents and other competent evidence in its possession. The Consultant shall only disclose Confidential Information to its employees and other Service Providers on a need-to-know basis and further undertakes to inform them of the confidential nature of the Confidential Information. 

The Consultant shall not make or permit the making of any public announcement regarding the Work, this Agreement, or its connection with the Owner without the Owner’s prior express consent. 
Assignment

This Agreement may not be assigned by the Consultant without the prior written consent of the Owner, which consent may be withheld by the Owner. This Agreement may be assigned or transferred by the Owner, in whole or in part, without the Consultant’s consent.

Successors and Assigns

This Agreement shall be binding upon and shall enure to the benefit of the parties hereto and their respective successors and permitted assigns. Whenever the terms “Owner” and “Consultant” are used herein, they shall be deemed to mean and include the Owner and the Consultant and their respective successors and permitted assigns in the same manner and to the same extent as if specified each time said terms appear herein.

Survival

The obligations of the Consultant, including those set out in Sections 4.1, 4.4, 5.2(c), 7.4, 7.5, 7.6, 8.1, 8.2, 8.3, 9.3, and Article 10, hereof, shall not merge upon but shall survive the expiration or sooner termination of this Agreement.

Captions and Interpretation

The Article and Section captions set forth herein have been included solely for the convenience of the parties and shall not be used or referred to in the interpretation or construction of this Agreement or any provision hereof. Time shall be of the essence for this Agreement. Whenever a word importing the singular or plural is used in this Agreement, such word shall include the plural and singular respectively.


Waivers

Failure by either party to complain of any action, non-action or default of the other party hereunder shall not constitute a waiver of the aggrieved party’s rights hereunder unless expressed in a writing executed by such aggrieved party. Waiver by either party of any right for any default of the other party, including a waiver deemed to occur as the result of an action or inaction, shall not constitute a waiver of any right for either a subsequent default for the same obligation or for any other default, past, present or future.

Partial Invalidity

If any term, covenant or condition of this Agreement, shall ever be held to be invalid or unenforceable, then in each event the remainder of this Agreement or the application of such term, covenant or condition to any other Person or any other circumstance (other than those as to which it shall be invalid or unenforceable) shall not be thereby affected and each term, covenant, condition and provision hereof shall remain valid and enforceable to the fullest extent permitted by Applicable Laws.

Schedules and Exhibits

Any schedules, attachments and exhibits referenced in and attached to this Agreement shall be deemed an integral part hereof to the same extent as if written in whole herein. In the event that any inconsistency or conflict exists between the provisions of this Agreement and any schedules, attachments or exhibits attached hereto, the provisions of this Agreement shall supersede the provisions of any such schedules, attachments or exhibits.

Counterparts

This Agreement may be executed in any number of counterparts and may be delivered by electronic facsimile transmission or other means of electronic communication capable of producing a printed copy, with the same effect as if all parties hereto had signed the same document. All counterparts and adopting instruments shall be construed together and shall constitute one and the same agreement.

