control its work hours and place in performing the Work;
use its commercially reasonable best efforts to expedite the Completion of all of the Work, and to protect the Owner against unnecessary extra costs and expenses. 
The Owner reserves the right to assess the Work and achievement of the results resulting therefrom. Without derogating from the Owner’s rights under Section 7.2(b) herein, the Owner may, at any time during the course of the Work and acting reasonably, request the replacement of any Persons that are performing the Work in a manner inconsistent with the terms and conditions of this Agreement, including the Standard of Care, and promptly upon receipt of such request, the Consultant shall make arrangements to select and appoint a replacement acceptable to the Owner, acting reasonably. 
Consultant Conduct and Standard of Care

The Consultant covenants that it will exercise its powers and discharge its duties under this Agreement competently, honestly, expeditiously, diligently, with due care, in good faith, , and that it will exercise the care and skill that a Person duly qualified to perform the Work would exercise under similar conditions in accordance with accepted industry best practices given the project complexity and the nature and character of the Property (the “Standard of Care”). 

