In the event that the Owner sells the Property, the Owner may terminate this Agreement by providing written notice to the Consultant of such termination which notice shall state the effective date of such termination, which effective date may be immediately upon delivery of the notice or thereafter. 

Upon material default by the Owner pursuant to this Agreement that, if capable of being cured, is not cured within 15 days following written notice to the Owner from the Consultant specifying in reasonable detail the nature of the default, the Consultant may terminate this Agreement without prejudice to its rights to pursue all legal and equitable remedies, provided that such termination shall not prejudice or terminate the license granted to the Owner pursuant to Section 9.3 of this Agreement.

Suspension of Work"
8869e9bbc7b5-67ff50,31180-01,31180-01,Starlight Developments,7376 Halifax St Burnaby,client,draft,17/21,,2026-02-20,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31180-01 (7376 Halifax St Burnaby)\Newforma\email\2026-02\2026-01-19 1443 - 7360 Halifax Street - Service Agreements.msg,2026.01.19 - Service Agreement [DV.O].docx,0p14,"The Owner may direct the Consultant to stop all or any portion of the Work by giving the Consultant written notice, which shall specify the estimated period dur",termination|suspension|payment|dispute,310,"The Owner may direct the Consultant to stop all or any portion of the Work by giving the Consultant written notice, which shall specify the estimated period during which the Work is to be stopped. The Consultant shall resume Work upon the date specified in such notice, or upon such other date as the Owner may thereafter specify. Suspension or stoppage of Work under this Section shall not give rise to any Claim against the Owner or any other fees being due and payable by the Owner to the Consultant, except that the Owner shall be liable to the Consultant for: (a) Work Completed prior to the date of such stoppage; and (b) reasonable out-of-pocket costs incurred by the Consultant to recommence the Work. The Consultant shall not be entitled to any portion of the Price or any other fees in respect of Work performed during the period during which the Consultant’s Work is suspended. If the Work is suspended for a period of more than 60 days, then the Consultant shall have the right to terminate this Agreement immediately upon written notice to Owner. 

Remedies of the Owner

If this Agreement shall terminate, the Consultant shall not have any right to payment of the Price or any other fees other than as set out below; provided, however, that the Consultant is in compliance with Section 7.5 hereof: 

if applicable Work is Completed as of the date of termination and not yet paid by the Owner, the Consultant shall have the right to payment for a portion of the Price equivalent to the reasonable value of the Work Completed prior to the date of termination, provided that an invoice shall be delivered to the Owner within 30 days of the date of termination and such payment shall be due after 60 days of the date of an undisputed invoice; and"
