Actions Upon Termination and Expiration

Within 30 calendar days after expiration or earlier termination of this Agreement, the Consultant shall promptly deliver to the Owner or to such other Person as the Owner shall designate in writing, the Records, and any property belonging to the Owner, whether in possession of the Consultant or a Person engaged or employed by the Consultant. The Consultant shall cooperate with the Owner as the Owner shall reasonably require in order to effectuate an orderly and systematic termination of the Consultant’s duties and activities, as applicable, including without limitation at the Owner’s request, destroying or causing to destroy all Confidential Information in the possession or control of the Consultant or its Service Providers. The Consultant shall not be required to provide original copies of the Records.

Rights on Termination

Any termination of this Agreement shall terminate all of the rights and obligations of the parties under this Agreement, except as otherwise provided herein or as stated to survive the termination of this Agreement, and further except for all rights and obligations with respect to fees and other amounts owing up until termination or with respect to remedies, as applicable. 

