bd11cff35dba,31194-01,31194-01,Omicron Development Inc.,Whistler Sport Legacies,KOR,proposal,,,2025-05-08,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31194-01 (Whistler Sport Legacies)\01 General\Proposals & Contracts\Structural RFP.pdf,,3,Scope of Work,suspension|permits_approvals|field_review,417,"3 Scope of Work 
 
Structural Analysis and Design: 
• 
Review geotechnical report and incorporate foundation recommendations. 
• 
Coordinate with architect and consultants to establish structural design criteria. 
• 
Design of the following structural elements: 

 
 
Page 2 of 4 
o 
Foundations (spread footings, strip footings, piles, if required). 
o 
Slabs (on-grade or suspended). 
o 
Superstructure (wood-frame, concrete, as applicable). 
o 
Lateral force-resisting systems (shear walls, braced frames, moment frames). 
o 
Roof framing system, including snow load considerations specific to the AHJ. 
• 
Compliance with BC Building Code, RMOW snow and seismic loads, and CSA standards. 
• 
Preparation of structural drawings, details, and specifications. 
• 
Provide support for Development and Building Permit applications. Respond to municipal comments. Revise 
drawings/calculations as required for permit approval. 
• 
Structural calculations for permit submission. 
• 
Letters of Assurance, as required by the AHJ. 
• 
Ongoing value engineering or alternate material review. 
• 
Attendance at consultant team meetings during the design period. 
• 
Coordination of structural construction documents with architectural, electrical, landscape, civil, mechanical, 
energy modelling, and envelope design. 
• 
Final drawings for tender and construction. Address structural questions from proponents bidding on the 
project. 
 
Construction Phase: 
 
Site visits/ Meetings 
• 
Site visits at periodic intervals to ensure conformity with the design drawings and permit certification as 
required. Anticipated number of site visits during the construction phase is 24 – the actual number may vary; if 
more/less are anticipated given the scope of work outlined, please identify in your proposal. 
• 
Provision of written reports for each field review outlining consultant’s observations and recommendations 
concerning the work in progress. 
• 
Attendance at occasional meetings on site or elsewhere to discuss construction progress. 
Construction Administration 
• 
Respond to Requests for Information (RFIs) and contractor queries. 
• 
Review of applicable shop drawings/submittals to ascertain general conformance with the drawings. 
• 
Consultation as required with the contractor or architect regarding the design intent of the drawings. 
• 
Modifications to the drawings in written or sketch format as the Consultant deems necessary to provide 
clarification or illustration of revisions. 
• 
Review of materials testing reports for compliance from the materials consultant/testing agency. 
• 
Provision of final Letter of Assurance (Schedule C-B). 
 
Additional items: 
 
• 
Professional qualifications and licensed to practice in the Province of British Columbia. 

 
 
Page 3 of 4 
• 
Provide electronic drawing files for use by the design and construction teams during the project. 
• 
Outline any additional scope required in accordance with the Engineers and Geoscientists BC guidelines for 
structural engineering services for building projects."
