95bf4b68a8c4-62e26d,31207-01,31207-01,Cressey Development Group,Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam,KOR,proposal,,,2025-11-06,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31207-01 (Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam)\Newforma\email\2025-11\2025-11-04-2231-22-TTHU dsingh@korst OGT Fee Proposal for S.eml,Cressey 727 North Road Coquitlam BC 2025-10-31 KOR KW JM.pdf,3,The Firm,field_review,344,"3 The Firm 
Kor Structural (""KOR"") is a Vancouver based Structural Engineering firm with satellite offices in Kelowna and 
Nanaimo. For over 25 years, we’ve provided expert consultation, design, and field review services throughout 
British Columbia and across North America. 
With a portfolio of over 2,000 projects across Canada and the United States, we specialize in delivering efficient, 
creative, and buildable Structural solutions. Our expertise covers all building types from tall towers (up to 65 storeys), 
mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, institutional/public facilities, sports 
facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, office buildings, and more. 
Our team of Professional Engineers are licensed in provinces across Canada and in multiple U.S. States, including 
Washington, California, Arizona, and Texas. 
Founded by three seasoned Professional Engineers, Kor has grown to a team of 40+ professionals driven by a 
commitment to superior client service, innovative design, and quality execution. We collaborate closely with your 
design team to ensure every project starts with a strong foundation, both structurally and collaboratively, built on 
technical excellence, innovative tools, and a steadfast commitment to supporting you and your team at every stage 
of development, design, and construction. 
Our Services 
At Kor, Structural Engineering is a seamless blend of creative design and practical solutions where we bring 
innovative structures to life through collaboration and precision. Our expertise includes: 
Residential / Commercial 
• 
High-rise reinforced concrete structures 
• 
Mid-rise multifamily buildings (wood and concrete) 
• 
Structural steel buildings 
• 
Commercial developments and mixed-use projects 
• 
Office buildings and hotels 
 
Community, Cultural, and Industrial 
• 
Community and cultural buildings 
• 
Healthcare facilities and social housing 
• 
Sport facilities and arenas 
• 
Warehouses and light industrial facilities 
 
Renovations & Retrofits 
• 
Renovations, retrofits, and structural upgrades 
• 
Analysis and design of unique or complex structural systems 
 
Performance-Based Design 
• 
Seismic performance-based analysis and design 
Our integrated Engineering, Drafting, and Construction teams work to deliver innovative designs that reduce 
turnaround times and optimize costs. Our goal is to make your vision structurally possible while being a reliable, 
responsive partner every step of the way. 
 

OUR COMPANY"
95bf4b68a8c4-62e26d,31207-01,31207-01,Cressey Development Group,Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam,KOR,proposal,,,2025-11-06,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31207-01 (Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam)\Newforma\email\2025-11\2025-11-04-2231-22-TTHU dsingh@korst OGT Fee Proposal for S.eml,Cressey 727 North Road Coquitlam BC 2025-10-31 KOR KW JM.pdf,4,Project Personnel and Experience,field_review,417,"4 Project Personnel and Experience 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be Kevin Wurmlinger, P.Eng. Struct.Eng., CEng, 
MIStructE. Kevin is a specialist Designated Structural Engineer licensed in British Columbia, Manitoba, and the UK 
with more than 20 years of experience designing a wide variety of buildings and types, including tall towers, mixed-
use commercial and residential projects, and office buildings, with expertise in concrete, steel, and timber. Kevin is 
involved in all stages of his projects from conceptual design through construction. He has extensive experience in 
structural design solutions, consultant team coordination, drawing preparation, site reviews, and construction 
administration, which has continuously led to the successful delivery of his projects. 
After the initial stages of design are complete, Kevin Wurmlinger will be assisted by Senior Partner, John Markulin, 
M.Eng., P.Eng. Struct.Eng., PE, SE, who is a licensed Structural Engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, California, 
Washington, Arizona, and Texas, and has more than 30 years of experience designing a wide variety of buildings, 
including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial warehouses, and 
institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, hotels, and office buildings. 
John Markulin is responsible for delivering innovative structural engineering solutions for some of the firm’s most 
notable projects. John is an accomplished engineer with significant project experience in the design of reinforced 
concrete, pre-cast concrete, cast-in-place concrete, post-tensioned concrete, tilt-up concrete, structural steel, load-
bearing steel stud, wood-frame, and masonry, as well as floor systems, vertical load systems and seismic and lateral 
systems. 
Kevin Wurmlinger and John Markulin will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will include 
preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Both Kevin and John will be available 
and remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
Additional staff dedicated to this project will include: 
• 
Omar Alcazar Pastrana, M.A.Sc., P.Eng. Senior Structural Engineer, Associate Principal 
• 
Andréa Neuviale, M.Eng., P.Eng., Structural Engineer 
• 
Henry Xu, M.A.Sc., P.Eng., Structural Engineer 
• 
Simon Szarkiewicz, Senior Structural BIM / CAD Manager 
• 
Michael Mousa, Senior Structural BIM / CAD Technologist 
• 
Lindsay Finnigan, Senior Structural BIM / CAD Technologist 
• 
Chris Ford, Structural BIM / CAD Technologist 
All personnel listed have extensive experience with similar projects. We would like to note that we have sufficient 
resources (more than 40 people) to meet your requirements on schedule. 
For further information on key project personnel and an introduction to Kor Structural, please visit our website at 
www.korstructural.com. 
 

OUR COMPANY"
95bf4b68a8c4-62e26d,31207-01,31207-01,Cressey Development Group,Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam,KOR,proposal,,,2025-11-06,projects,Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31207-01 (Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam)\Newforma\email\2025-11\2025-11-04-2231-22-TTHU dsingh@korst OGT Fee Proposal for S.eml,Cressey 727 North Road Coquitlam BC 2025-10-31 KOR KW JM.pdf,6,Project Description,permits_approvals|field_review,297,"6 Project Description 
Our proposed fees are based on the following assumptions: 
• 
6-storey residential wood frame building with approximately 95 rental units (proposed FAR 3.15), over 2.5 
levels of below grade parking. 
• 
The total structural area, including slab on grade, is estimated to be approximately 140,000 sq.ft. 
• 
The following fee is based on a structural design area of approximately 120,000 sq.ft. 
Proposed Fees 
The following fees are for complete Structural Engineering services for the project as noted in the following Scope 
of Structural Services. The proposed fixed fees for our services are as follows: 
Phase 
Fee 
Schematic Design to DP Application 
$ 
10,000 
Design Development to BP Application 
$ 
50,000 
Working Drawings to Issued for Construction 
$ 
4,000 
Construction Administration & Field Reviews 
$ 
16,000 
 Including up to 45 field review visits † 
 
Total Base Fees: 
$ 
80,000 
† Additional field reviews over the above specified limit will be billed at a rate of $350 per visit, covering up to 2.0 
hours, at which point hourly rates will apply. 
Over and above the noted proposed fixed fees, we recommend a budget allowance of $1,000 for normal 
disbursements (e.g., courier costs and printing drawing sets, if required). 
Our team has extensive experience in designing both 5-storey and 6-storey wood-frame buildings, so we are experts 
in special design issues related to these structures. The Building Code prohibits shear wall transfers in wood-frame 
buildings over 4-storeys, hence we recommend consulting with us early during initial schematic design, so that 
important shear wall elements can be integrated into the unit plans and overall building massing. 
Our fixed fee does include for attending site meetings; however, we are on site regularly once construction begins 
(reviewing rebar), so attending these meetings only when we are required is appreciated. 
 

