c9b7cb893758-62e26d,31207-01,31207-01,Cressey Development Group,Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam,KOR,proposal,,,2026-04-20,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31207-01 (Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam)\Newforma\email\2026-04\4501-01-01 0000 - FW_ Fee Proposal for Structural Engineering Services for Sherwood – Residential Development, Coqui.msg",Cressey 727 North Road Coquitlam BC 2025-10-31 KOR KW JM.pdf,6,Project Description,permits_approvals|field_review,297,"6 Project Description 
Our proposed fees are based on the following assumptions: 
• 
6-storey residential wood frame building with approximately 95 rental units (proposed FAR 3.15), over 2.5 
levels of below grade parking. 
• 
The total structural area, including slab on grade, is estimated to be approximately 140,000 sq.ft. 
• 
The following fee is based on a structural design area of approximately 120,000 sq.ft. 
Proposed Fees 
The following fees are for complete Structural Engineering services for the project as noted in the following Scope 
of Structural Services. The proposed fixed fees for our services are as follows: 
Phase 
Fee 
Schematic Design to DP Application 
$ 
10,000 
Design Development to BP Application 
$ 
50,000 
Working Drawings to Issued for Construction 
$ 
4,000 
Construction Administration & Field Reviews 
$ 
16,000 
 Including up to 45 field review visits † 
 
Total Base Fees: 
$ 
80,000 
† Additional field reviews over the above specified limit will be billed at a rate of $350 per visit, covering up to 2.0 
hours, at which point hourly rates will apply. 
Over and above the noted proposed fixed fees, we recommend a budget allowance of $1,000 for normal 
disbursements (e.g., courier costs and printing drawing sets, if required). 
Our team has extensive experience in designing both 5-storey and 6-storey wood-frame buildings, so we are experts 
in special design issues related to these structures. The Building Code prohibits shear wall transfers in wood-frame 
buildings over 4-storeys, hence we recommend consulting with us early during initial schematic design, so that 
important shear wall elements can be integrated into the unit plans and overall building massing. 
Our fixed fee does include for attending site meetings; however, we are on site regularly once construction begins 
(reviewing rebar), so attending these meetings only when we are required is appreciated. 
 

OUR PROPOSAL"
c9b7cb893758-62e26d,31207-01,31207-01,Cressey Development Group,Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam,KOR,proposal,,,2026-04-20,projects,"Projects\Projects\03 Residential\31207-01 (Sherwood North Rd Coquitlam)\Newforma\email\2026-04\4501-01-01 0000 - FW_ Fee Proposal for Structural Engineering Services for Sherwood – Residential Development, Coqui.msg",Cressey 727 North Road Coquitlam BC 2025-10-31 KOR KW JM.pdf,7,Scope of Structural Services,permits_approvals|assignment_subconsultants,210,"7 Scope of Structural Services 
Our scope of services includes detailed coordination with the Architect and other consultants, as well as developing 
the project in Revit/BIM LOD 300 or AutoCAD. We will assist the Architect in completing Schematic Design 
Documents along with providing local technical expertise and participate in local engineering/sub-consultant 
coordination in support of this phase of the work. Sketches of the structure will be provided, defining dimensions of 
the structure in detail, so Architect's drawings can reflect real structural member sizes. Preliminary drawings of the 
structure will be provided in sufficient detail for preliminary pricing of the structure. The preliminary structure will 
be coordinated with the needs of the Architect and other consultants (mechanical and electrical). Based on the DP 
submission, we will create, and coordinate construction documentation (drawings and specifications) as required to 
issue for Tender, Building Permit, and Construction. We will coordinate with the Architect and other consultants in 
the development of the construction documentation. We are able to change structure as needed to meet the final 
needs of the Architect and other consultants and keep the structure on budget, as well as to incorporate the 
recommendations of any specialist consultants if required. 
The foregoing proposed fees are for normal basic structural engineering services as follows:"
