SCHEDULE A – GENERAL TERMS AND CONDITIONS 
 
The Services to be provided by the Consultant are governed by the Terms and Conditions outlined in the 
Consulting Services Agreement, in addition to the provisions outlined below. 
A.1 
The Consultant must allocate budgets based on the completion of individual deliverables. Change 
Order requests resulting from an unexpected increase in hours, labor cost, or material cost escalation 
will not be accepted throughout the project duration. 
A.2 
The Consultant must define and adhere to milestones such as 50%, 90%, and 100% drawing 
completion. The Consultant may only bill upon reaching these milestones. With reference to Schedule 
B, the Consultant may not progress from one phase of services (ie. moving from Schematic to 
Detailed Design) to the next without the written approval of the client. 
A.2.1 Drawings must be formally submitted to facilitate payment. I.e. The Consultant must 
provide 50% complete drawings as opposed to stating that 50% of the work is complete. 
 
A.3 
The Consultant shall not start work on additional services they consider are outside of the scope of 
the Consulting Services Agreement until they have provided the Client with a quote for the additional 
services and have received an executed Change Order. 
A.3.1 Any work that is done in advance, or omission of the above, is at the Consultant’s own 
risk and the Client will not be responsible for payment. Payment will only be made at the 
Client’s discretion if the circumstances are justified. 
 
A.4 
In the event of a fee dispute regarding out-of-scope work, the Consultant shall continue to perform all 
in-scope work without interruption to prevent any delays to the Project Schedule. 
A.5 
All work must comply with applicable codes and regulations, and it is the Consultant’s sole 
responsibility to be aware of said code and regulations, including without limitation building codes, 
zoning regulations, and bylaws. 
A.6 
The Consultant shall perform their services in accordance with the Client’s specification and 
procedure documents, including but not limited to the Wood Frame Rental Specification Document 
and Issued for Tender (IFT) Checklist, which will be provided by the Client at a later date. The 
Consultant agrees to review and incorporate all requirements and standards outlined in these 
documents into their Services. Any deviations from these documents must be approved in writing by 
the Client prior to implementation. 
A.7 
The Client shall have the right to challenge designs or engineering through a peer review at their own 
expense. Should the client request modifications to the consultant’s work following such peer review, 
the consultant agrees to undertake these revisions at no additional cost to the client. 
A.8 
Any Change Orders involving third-party services shall be subject to a maximum markup of 10%. 
Invoices from third-party service providers must be submitted to substantiate the costs incurred. 
A.9 
All specified prices for all items of work under this Consulting Services Agreement and any approved 
Change Orders are considered to be a Fixed Maximum Upset Fee. Actual billings against these items 
are not to exceed the Fixed Maximum Upset Fee without a Change Order. Change Orders will be 
considered by the Client and approved if justified in the sole opinion of the Client. Change Orders 
must be proactive; the Client will not be responsible to pay for any costs due to the Consultant 
retroactively claiming for additional fees under the Fixed Maximum Upset Fee. 
 

 
 
Consulting Services Agreement"
