SCHEDULE C – COMPENSATION 
 
 
C.1 
The Client will compensate the Consultant for the Services as per the fixed maximum upset fee summary 
shown on the spreadsheet attached to this Schedule C, in accordance with terms outlined in the 
Consulting Services Agreement and Schedule A. 
 
C.2 
The Consultant acknowledges the fixed maximum upset fee shown on the spreadsheet attached to this 
Schedule C shall be fully inclusive of all Services described herein of Schedule B. 
 
C.3 
The Consultant acknowledges the fixed maximum upset fee shown on the spreadsheet attached to this 
Schedule C shall be based on the completion of individual deliverables, and that any Change Order 
requests resulting from an unexpected increase in hours, labor costs, or material costs will not be 
accepted. 
 
C.4 
All disbursements for coordination, delivery and production with other consultants as well as travel, 
mileage charges and car allowances within Vancouver and The Lower Mainland are to be included in 
the fixed maximum upset fee. The Client will reimburse the Consultant for other disbursements (at 
cost), but only if such disbursements are specifically requested and agreed upon in writing prior to 
being incurred, and appropriate backup is provided. 
 
C.5 
The Client will compensate the Consultant for Additional Services in the same manner as the 
Services identified in C.1 above except with the additional requirement of a duly executed Change 
Order. 
 
C.6 
Invoices for services rendered are to be submitted in the form shown on the attached spreadsheet to 
this Schedule C to Accounts Payable via email or mail by the 25th day of each month in order to be 
paid by the end of the following month. Only one invoice submitted monthly via either method is 
necessary. For invoices related to the development of “The Project”, please make them out to the 
following: 
 
 
 
