The Senior Structural Engineer and principal contact for this project will be Conor Murtagh, B.A.Sc., P.Eng., who has 
more than 20 years of experience of working for firms in Ireland, Australia, and Canada and extensive knowledge of 
wood design systems and provides effective and innovative solutions, he is particularly skilled at finding structural 
solutions for complicated building arrangements that are both simple and efficient. In every project he also aims to 
balance the original design intent of the Architect yet always taking into consideration the Client’s needs and desires. 
Conor will participate heavily in the preliminary stages of the work, which will include preliminary design concepts 
and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. 
After the initial stages of design are complete, Conor Murtagh will be assisted by Project Manager Andréa Neuviale, 
M.Eng., P.Eng., who has more than 10 years of experience in the design of mid-rise, high-rise and light industrial 
buildings. Andrea is involved in all stages of her projects from conceptual design through construction. She has 
extensive experience in all aspects of structural analysis, design and review, consultant team coordination, drawing 
preparation, site reviews, as well as construction administration, which has continuously led to the successful 
delivery of her projects. 
Conor Murtagh and Andréa Neuviale will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will include 
preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Both Conor and Andréa will be available 
and remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
Additional staff dedicated to this project will include: 
• 
Kate Reid, B.A.Sc., EIT, Structural Engineer 
• 
Lindsay Finnigan, Senior Structural BIM / CAD Technologist 
• 
Simon Szarkiewicz, Senior Structural BIM / CAD Manager 
• 
Michael Mousa, Senior Structural BIM / CAD Technologist 
• 
Chris Ford, Structural BIM / CAD Technologist 
All personnel listed have extensive experience with similar projects. We would like to note that we have sufficient 
resources (more than 40 people) to meet your requirements on schedule. 
For further information on key project personnel and an introduction to Kor Structural, please visit our website at 
www.korstructural.com.

