Our team has extensive experience in designing both 5-storey and 6-storey wood-frame buildings, therefore we are 
experts in special design issues related to these structures. The Building Code prohibits shear wall transfers in wood-
frame buildings over 4-storeys, hence we recommend consulting with us early during initial schematic design, so 
that important shear wall elements can be integrated into the unit plans and overall building massing. 
Our fixed fee does include attending site meetings; however, we are on site regularly once construction begins 
(reviewing rebar), so attending these meetings only when we are required is appreciated. 
Scope of Structural Services 
Our scope of services includes detailed coordination with the Architect and other consultants, as well as developing 
the project in Revit/BIM LOD 300 or AutoCAD. We will assist the Architect in completing Schematic Design 
Documents along with providing local technical expertise and participating in local engineering/sub-consultant 
coordination in support of this phase of the work. Sketches of the structure will be provided, defining dimensions of 
the structure in detail, so Architect's drawings can reflect real structural member sizes. Preliminary drawings of the 
structure will be provided in sufficient detail for preliminary pricing of the structure. The preliminary structure will 
be coordinated with the needs of the Architect and other consultants (mechanical and electrical). Based on the DP 
submission, we will create, and coordinate construction documentation (drawings and specifications) as required to 
issue for Tender, Building Permit, and Construction. We will coordinate with the Architect and other consultants in 
the development of the construction documentation. We are able to change structure as needed to meet the final 
needs of the Architect and other consultants and keep the structure on budget, as well as to incorporate the 
recommendations of any specialist consultants if required. 
The foregoing proposed fees are for normal basic structural engineering services as follows:"
