‘Jubilee’ 
20556 119 Avenue, Maple Ridge, BC 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
July 16, 2026 

Request for Proposals: 20556 119 Avenue, Maple Ridge, BC 
 
 
Page 2 of 6 
Introduction 
Established in 2016, Whitetail Homes is a leading developer of condominium, rental apartment and retail 
buildings in the Fraser Valley. Building on a foundation of concrete formwork and framing contracting at 
Cornerstone Works Ltd., Whitetail has completed thousands of apartment units in the Lower Mainland, 
with a commitment to quality, attainable projects and community betterment. 
Whitetail invites your firm (the ‘Consultant’) to provide a proposal for consulting services at our project, 
as detailed in this request for proposals (RFP) document. 
Project Description 
The project is comprised of four six-storey wood framed buildings over a shared, two-level parkade. The 
project contains approximately 300 residential units: 147 rentals in Buildings A&D and 139 
condominiums in Buildings B&C. The ground floor of each building is made up of daycare and retail uses, 
a total area of 20,942 square feet. Total above grade buildable area is approximately 267,000 square 
feet. 
 
Project Phasing 
The project will be divided into two parcels. The western parcel will be made up of the two 
condominium buildings, and the eastern parcel will be made up two rental buildings. The entire project 
will be built in on phase, with the parkade being constructed before each of the four buildings. 

Request for Proposals: 20556 119 Avenue, Maple Ridge, BC 
 
 
Page 3 of 6 
Project Schedule 
The anticipated project completion timeline is laid out as follows: 
Design Development Kick-Off 
September 2026 
Submission of Building Permit Application – Full Project 
January 2027 
Issued for Tender Drawing Complete 
June 2027 
Issued for Construction Drawings Complete/Construction Start/Full Building 
Permit Receipt 
September 2027 
Construction Completion 
March 2030 
Project Scope 
Whitetail requests that all proposals outline a complete scope of services provided for the projects under 
the following scope stages, and that they include a list of all services intended to be provided and not 
intended to be provided by the Consultant:"
