Over and above the noted proposed fixed fees, we recommend a budget allowance of $1,500 for normal 
disbursements (e.g., courier costs), not including printing and plotting. 
 
Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be Rory Beirne, M.Eng., P.Eng., C.Eng. (UK), 
Struct.Eng., MIStructE. Rory Beirne is a licensed structural engineer in British Columbia with more than 15 
years of experience in the construction industry, including more than a decade of structural design 
experience. His background as a carpenter, in conjunction with his experience as a structural and 
geotechnical engineer, has allowed him to gain a unique skillset encompassing all aspects of construction 
from the ground up. His practical approach to design and construction management have resulting in 
innovative and efficient solutions to some of our more challenging structural projects. 
 
After the initial stages of design are complete, Rory Beirne will be assisted by senior partner, John Markulin, 
M.Eng., P.Eng. Struct.Eng., PE, SE, who is a licensed Structural Engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, 
California, Washington, Arizona, and Texas, and has more than 30 years of experience designing a wide 
variety of buildings, including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial 
warehouses, and institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, 
hotels, and office buildings. John Markulin is responsible for delivering innovated structural engineering 
solutions for some of the firm’s most notable projects. John is an accomplished engineer with significant 
project experience in the design of reinforced concrete, pre-cast concrete, cast-in-place concrete, post-
tensioned concrete, tilt-up concrete, structural steel, load-bearing steel stud, wood-frame, and masonry, as 
well as floor systems, vertical load systems and seismic and lateral systems. 
 
Rory Beirne and John Markulin will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will include 
preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. Both Rory and John will be 
available and remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
Additional staff dedicated to this project will include: 
 
 Abhinav Arora, M.Eng., EIT 
 Sahil Goyal, M.Eng., EIT 
 Kyle Frank, Senior Structural Drafting Manager 
 Michael Li, Senior Structural BIM Manager 
 Chris Ford, Senior Structural BIM/CAD Technologist 
 
All personnel listed have extensive experience with similar projects. 
 
