Fees 
Please submit a fixed fee submission for the following categories: 
A. Design Development Services (Development Permit Assistance) 
B. Construction Documents Phase (Prelim Pricing, Building Permit, IFT and IFC sets) 
C. Contract Administration 
 
*Please provide a fee schedule with hourly rates. All additional work is to be pre-approved by Beedie 
 
 

 
Scope of Services 
A. Design Development Phase Services 
• 
Provide preliminary structural input to facilitate a development permit application. 
• 
Attend meetings with Beedie, and consultant team as required to develop Design Development Documents 
and Specifications. 
• 
Provide input and prepare preliminary structural analysis and design calculations for typical Primary 
Structural Elements; parkade, foundation, slabs, transfer slabs, elevator core sizing, column spacing/sizing. 
• 
Provide assistance with reviewing value engineering/design issues. 
• 
Review and obtain Beedie approval before proceeding to the next phase. 
 
B. Construction Documents Phase Services 
• 
Attend meetings with Beedie, and consultant team as required to develop Construction Documents. 
• 
Prepare complete drawing package for Building Permit Submission including plans, sections, details, and 
project data as per city submission requirements. 
• 
Provide written responses to Beedie Development Manager to address City comments on drawings if/when 
required. 
• 
Check completed documents for coordination, compliance with outline specification, accuracy, and cross-
coordination with other consultants’ work. Revise own documents as required. 
• 
Construction Documentation Deliverables: Issued for Preliminary Pricing, Building Permit Documents, 
Issued for Tender Documents, and Issued for Construction Documents & Specifications. 
C. Contract Administration Phase Services 
• 
Attend, in person or by-phone, pre-construction meeting(s) and monthly construction progress meetings as 
required to meet the project schedule. Review and comment on meeting minutes prepared by the Beedie 
Project Manager. 
• 
Respond to Requests for Information coordinated by the Prime Consultant on the interpretation of the 
structural drawings and specifications. 
• 
As necessary and always in coordination with the Prime Consultant, issue Supplementary Instructions 
during the construction period to reflect changes in the scope of work. 
• 
Advise Beedie Project Manager where changes affect previous approvals from authorities having 
jurisdiction. 
• 
If requested, advise the Project Manager on the validity of charges for additions to or deletions from the 
scopes of work and on the issue of change orders from its subcontractors. 
• 
Review all Shop Drawings, Samples and Other Submittals for conformance with the Contract Documents 
and in accordance with the requirements of the BC Building Code. 
• 
Review reports from the testing and inspection agencies to determine if the agency has verified compliance 
of the reported item of work with Structural Contract Documents. 
• 
At intervals appropriate to the stage of construction, conduct field reviews of the structural components of 
the project noting deficiencies observed and inspect completed corrections. 
• 
Record observations and provide written report to Beedie Construction Manager within 1 week of visit. 
• 
Conduct Pre-Occupancy Inspection, coordinate with Project Manager to create a deficiency list, and 
substantiate completion of its items. 
• 
Sign and seal applicable letters of assurance, as appropriate, for general compliance of construction with 
building permit documents. 
 
Additional Services 
It is understood that the fee(s) provided shall be all-encompassing for the purpose of preparing the necessary 
design and obtaining approvals to proceed and conclude the construction of this project. All requests for extras 
must be approved in writing by Beedie prior to commencement of work. 
 
 

 
