DEFINITIONS

 Beedie Living – 950 Raymur Avenue, Vancouver, B.C. 
Kor Structural • Fee Proposal dated January 18, 2023 
Page 2 of 5 
 
 
† Additional field reviews will be billed at a rate of $350 per visit, covering up to 2.0 hours, at which point 
hourly rates will apply. 
 
All preliminary work and preliminary consultations with the Architect will be charged on an hourly basis in 
accordance with the included ‘Appendix A’ Schedule of Standard Hourly Billing Rates, however, please 
note that all charges for preliminary work are included in the proposed Professional Services Fees. Our 
fixed fee does include for attending site meetings; however, we are on site regularly once construction 
begins (inspecting rebar), so attending these meetings only when we are required is appreciated. 
 
Over and above the noted proposed fixed fees, we recommend a budget allowance of $1,500 for normal 
disbursements (e.g., courier costs), not including printing and plotting. 
 
Project Personnel & Experience 
 
The project engineer and principal contact for this project will be John Markulin, M.Eng., P.Eng., 
Struct.Eng., PE, SE. John Markulin is a licensed Structural Engineer in British Columbia, Alberta, 
California, Washington, Arizona, and Texas, with more than 30 years of experience designing a wide 
variety of buildings, including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, light industrial 
warehouses, and institutional/public facilities such as ice rinks, sports facilities, extended care facilities, 
hotels, and office buildings. John Markulin is responsible for delivering innovated structural engineering 
solutions for some of the firm’s most notable projects. John is an accomplished engineer with significant 
project experience in the design of reinforced concrete, pre-cast concrete, cast-in-place concrete, post-
tensioned concrete, tilt-up concrete, structural steel, load-bearing steel stud, wood-frame, and masonry, 
as well as floor systems, vertical load systems and seismic and lateral systems. 
 
After the initial stages of design are complete, John Markulin will be assisted by senior partner, Kevin 
Wurmlinger, P.Eng. Struct.Eng., CEng, MIStructE, who has more than 20 years of experience designing a 
wide variety of buildings and types, including tall towers, mixed-use commercial and residential projects, 
and office buildings, with expertise in concrete, steel, and timber. Kevin is involved in all stages of his 
projects from conceptual design through construction. He has extensive experience in structural design 
and review, consultant team coordination, drawing preparation, site reviews, as well as construction 
administration, which has continuously led to the successful delivery of his projects. 
 
John Markulin and Kevin Wurmlinger will collaborate during preliminary stages of the work, which will 
include preliminary design concepts and preliminary design drawings for budgeting. John and Kevin will 
be available and remain fully involved in the project until construction is complete. 
 
Additional staff dedicated to this project will include: 
 
 Omar Alcazar Pastrana, M.A.Sc., P.Eng. 
 Abhinav Arora, M.Eng., EIT 
 Michael Li, Senior Structural BIM Manager 
 Simon Szarkiewicz, Senior Structural CAD Manager 
 Chris Ford, Senior Structural BIM/CAD Technologist 
 
All personnel listed have extensive experience with similar projects. 
 
For further information on key project personnel and an introduction to Kor Structural, please visit our 
website at www.korstructural.com. 
 
Scope of Structural Services 
 
Our scope of services includes detailed coordination with the Architect and other consultants, as well as 
developing the project in Revit/BIM LOD 300 or AutoCAD. We will assist the Architect in completing 
Schematic Design Documents along with providing local technical expertise and participate in local 

 Beedie Living – 950 Raymur Avenue, Vancouver, B.C. 
Kor Structural • Fee Proposal dated January 18, 2023 
Page 3 of 5 
 
 
engineering/sub-consultant coordination in support of this phase of the work. Sketches of the structure 
will be provided, defining dimensions of the structure in detail, so Architect's drawings can reflect real 
structural member sizes. Preliminary drawings of the structure will be provided in sufficient detail for 
preliminary pricing of the structure. The preliminary structure will be coordinated with the needs of the 
Architect and other consultants (mechanical and electrical). Based on the DP submission, we will create, 
and coordinate construction documentation (drawings and specifications) as required to issue for tender, 
building permit and construction. We will coordinate with the Architect and other consultants in the 
development of the construction documentation. We can change structure as needed to meet final needs 
of Architect and other consultants and keep the structure on budget, as well as to incorporate the 
