a. General Warranties - the Vendor warrants that each item of the Goods delivered is: (i) 
free of all liens, charges, encumbrances, and adverse claims of any kind whatsoever and 
that, subject to payment in accordance with the terms of this Purchase Order, the 
Purchaser shall have good and marketable title to the Scope of supply; (ii) new, of 
merchantable quality and fit for its intended purpose and (iii) complies with all 
requirements of this Purchase Order and with all laws, regulations, and technical codes 
specified or referenced in this Purchase Order. 
b. Warranty Against Defects and Deficiencies -the Vendor warrants that the Scope of 
Supply complies and will perform in accordance with the quality and performance 
specifications set out in this Purchase Order. The Vendor warrants that the Scope of 
Supply will be free from defects and deficiencies in design, workmanship, or materials 
appearing within the period expiring 12 months after the date of Acceptance of the 
particular Goods or Services forming the Scope of Supply, as the case may be. 
c. General Services Warranty - the Vendor warrants that the Services will be performed 
in a good and workmanlike manner and in compliance with all requirements of this 
Purchase Order and with all laws, regulations, and technical codes specified or 
referenced in this Purchase Order. 
d. Certification for use in Jurisdiction- The Vendor hereby certifies that all Goods, 
delivered under this Purchase Order are properly certified by a Nationally Recognized 
Testing Laboratory to be used and installed by the Purchaser on the site in the 
Jurisdiction of use, and that the Goods confrom to, and sitisfy, all applicable Building 
Codes and regulations in the Jurisdiction. 
The Vendor shall provide, for all Goods, the Manufacturers certification, and other 
documentation, required to satisfy all applicable authories in the Jurisdiction that the 
Goods are certified for the intended use in that Jurisdiction, prior to shipping the Goods. 
The Goods must bear a registered mark and/or stamp to show that the Goods have 
been independently tested and certified for use in the Jurisdiciton. 
e. Remedies - the Vendor shall repair, replace, or re-perform, at its own expense and 
under the same delivery limits set out in this Purchase Order, any portion of the Scope 
of Supply failing to meet the warranty in: 9a(ii), 9a(iii), 9b, or 9c. Repair, replacement, or 
repeat performance must be carried out promptly after notice from the Purchaser and 
at a time and in a manner specified by the Purchaser, acting reasonably. Any portion of 
the Scope of Supply repaired, replaced or re-performed under this warranty is further 
warranted by the Vendor against defects or deficiencies in design, workmanship, or 
materials appearing within a period expiring 12 months after the date of completion of 
repair, replacement, or completion of the re-performance. The foregoing warranties are 
in addition to, and not in substitution for, any guarantee or warranty set forth 
elsewhere in the Purchase Order or implied by law. 
f. Subcontractor Warranties - the Vendor, at the Purchaser's request, shall assign to the 
Purchaser, as the Purchaser directs, the benefit of all warranties, performance 
guarantees and similar obligations given to the Vendor by any subcontractor. 
Warranties, performance guarantees, and similar obligations given by any subcontractor 
and any assignment thereof do not relieve the Vendor of its obligations under this 
Purchase Order."
